o as our home. It is currently a rental. The city has the official living space as not including the back part of the house, which is an attached garage, bathroom and laundry room. The bathroom is original to the house, as is obvious from the tiling and fixtures. It remains a functional bathroom. The attached garage can still function as a garage, but was long ago physically converted (from before our purchase) to additional living area. We used it as an art studio and our tenants use it as a music and exercise studio.\n\nWe want to hire an architect to create the necessary drawings, including whatever physical work may be needed, to submit to the city to get a permit to do whatever additional work is needed. Our goal is to do the minimum necessary for the city to approve conversion of the garage square footage into part of the house\'s official living space. We believe the garage will need new windows, will require replacing the garage door with a wall and probably firring out and insulating the exterior walls, which are cinderblock. The space\'s ceiling is already insulated (though without drywall) and it has a mini-split air conditioner. The city has already confirmed that there is no parking issue for this particular property to eliminate the garage as parking space. We also believe the requirement of floor height as compared to the crest of the adjacent street will be met without raising the garage floor.\n\nWould this be a project you would be interested in? If so, how much would you charge to inspect and create permit drawings?',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-05-14 19:52:45','2023-05-14 19:52:45'),(560,609,609,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17173539202',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Need construction of walls to separate 6 rooms/classrooms.  The bathroom, stairs, and side windows are already in the space: we would only need the construction of the walls and the doors for each room.  Because we will be operating a piano teaching/practicing studio the walls will need to be constructed to be mostly soundproof (depending on the price).  The height of the walls would need to be 10 feet tall.  Looking to open at the latest by early/mid-August 2023.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-05-15 15:39:44','2023-05-15 15:39:44'),(561,610,610,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17173539202',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Need construction of walls to separate 6 rooms/classrooms.  The bathroom, stairs, and side windows are already in the space: we would only need the construction of the walls and the doors for each room.  Because we will be operating a piano teaching/practicing studio the walls will need to be constructed to be mostly soundproof (depending on the price).  The height of the walls would need to be 10 feet tall.  Looking to open at the latest by early/mid-August 2023.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-05-15 15:39:46','2023-05-15 15:39:46'),(562,611,611,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17173539202',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Need construction of walls to separate 6 rooms/classrooms.  The bathroom, stairs, and side windows are already in the space: we would only need the construction of the walls and the doors for each room.  Because we will be operating a piano teaching/practicing studio the walls will need to be constructed to be mostly soundproof (depending on the price).  The height of the walls would need to be 10 feet tall.  Looking to open at the latest by early/mid-August 2023.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-05-15 15:39:47','2023-05-15 15:39:47'),(563,612,612,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14752238686',NULL,NULL,NULL,'we are a company that works in the New York area doing new jobs Innovation everything that has to do with the construction area',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-05-16 13:26:27','2023-05-16 13:26:27'),(564,613,613,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14752238686',NULL,NULL,NULL,'we are a construction company we make New Houses we make foundations we make slogans we make Rut we are a company trained in all areas of construction with all licenses and insurance',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-05-16 13:48:07','2023-05-16 13:48:07'),(565,614,6