),(679,728,728,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1788772523',NULL,NULL,NULL,'This is a standard size bathroom, and a co-op apartment that would need to be completely gutted and remodeled. I would like a toilet without a tank, self flushing, and comfort height. Possibly some open storage above the toilet. The sink would be replaced with a cabinet underneath for storage. This is an in wall medicine cabinet, which I no longer want, it will be replaced by a LED lighted mirror hung vertically. I will still need lighting above this mirror. The bathtub would be replaced with a jetted air tub. I would need a niche for storing items in the shower, grab bars, and possibly a folding shower seat. The showerhead would be mounted on the wall as well as handheld. I want to remove this closet hamper combination and instead of filling in the wall I would replace it with a full length cabinet.  I would need some kind of exhaust fan and possibly heat. And possibly some kind of lighting in the shower alcove. I would like subway tiles on the wall and penny tiles for the floor.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-06 13:25:34','2023-07-06 13:25:34'),(680,729,729,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18036789123',NULL,NULL,NULL,'3289 Poplar Lane',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-06 15:45:27','2023-07-06 15:45:27'),(681,730,730,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16465049224',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Attached rowhome in Jersey City located at 257 Randolph Ave.  in need of bright, modern, and thoughtful updates that maximize usage of limited space.  The home is a narrow, prewar wood frame home with a brick foundation.  \n\n1. The first floor is an open layout with living room and dining room with kitchen in back leading to a small backyard.\n\n- This space will need lighting and a new floor. The floor is currently carpet covering the original heart pine floor/subfloor. I like the idea of using this floor as the actual floor, but I’m not sure if it’s possible or energy efficient. The floor is attached directly to the joists\n- I would also like to change the dining area into an eat-in kitchen, moving it from the dark back area into the front room. I love to cook so a larger space to do so would be appreciated. Space in need of new window.\n-A coat closet separates the living room space from the dining room space. I would like to have this become a powder room for guests.\n-The back room, currently the kitchen, has no natural light and feels closed in. I would like to brighten this space by replacing the back door which leads to the back yard with something that will brighten the space. The floor has a slope to one corner due to settlement.\n\n2. The second floor has 3 bedrooms and 1 bathroom\n-New flooring. The stairs leading up and the floor throughout was covered with carpet of the original heart pine floor/subfloor.\n-Main bathroom. The main bathroom is small (30-35sq ft) and cramped with no ventilation and in need of thoughtful updates. I would like a pocket door as the current door when opened takes up nearly half the space. Maybe borrowing space from the adjacent closet of the middle bedroom. The bathroom has a skylight in good condition covered by a drop ceiling. The drop ceiling will need to be removed and the drywall repaired.\n-Middle bedroom. In need of flooring refresh and new window. May need drywall refresh as walls and ceiling show signs of previous repair. The space has a recessed closet behind the door whose space could be used to add sq footage to the bathroom.\n-Back bedroom. Situated above the current kitchen. Floor has a slope due to settlement. Will need floor, new window, and drywall refresh.\n-Master bedroom. Currently the  room in the best condition. May need a paint refresh.\n\n3. The Backyard is small, but I love gardening and would like a space for entertaining and relaxing.\n -The backyard has an old deck that is falling apart and will need to be replaced. The yard itself is covered in mulch.\n\n4. The basement is unfinished with a concrete floor\n -The basement has the second bathroom and laundry.\n -In the future, I would like to turn this into living space. It will require digging out as the ceiling is roughly 6’4” high.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-06 17:02:31','2023-07-06 17:02:31'),(682,731,731,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15094204844',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-07 08:07:04','2023-07-07 08:07:04'),(683,732,732,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18434727272',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-07 09:50:05','2023-07-07 09:50:05'),(684,733,733,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12527147739',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Thanks',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-07 11:07:24','2023-07-07 11:07:24'),(685,734,734,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17024018232',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-07 11:21:28','2023-07-07 11:21:28'),(686,735,735,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17347551164',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-07 17:51:17','2023-07-07 17:51:17'),(687,736,736,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15042281719',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-07 17:54:47','2023-07-07 17:54:47'),(688,737,737,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1473687681',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-08 07:29:43','2023-07-08 07:29:43'),(689,738,738,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17742255942',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-08 11:08:24','2023-07-08 11:08:24'),(690,739,739,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15737952929',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remodelling',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-08 11:12:29','2023-07-08 11:12:29'),(691,740,740,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17862872227',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Need work through out the house , need to change some door frames , paint , bathroom etc',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-08 20:34:02','2023-07-08 20:34:02'),(692,741,741,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1379109067',NULL,NULL,NULL,'bathroom remodeling',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-10 11:13:13','2023-07-10 11:13:13'),(693,742,742,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19372150674',NULL,NULL,NULL,'None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-10 12:09:21','2023-07-10 12:09:21'),(694,743,743,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12283276530',NULL,NULL,NULL,'repair',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'20