nstalled. \n\n bathroom 3: adding half glass enclosure to existing tub. Single vainty, toilet, mirrors, lights, floors, and tile installed.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-21 14:07:29','2023-07-21 14:07:29'),(732,781,781,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17177486611',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Pintar',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-22 09:00:57','2023-07-22 09:00:57'),(733,782,782,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12067475618',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I\'m looking remodel a bathroom and re-do the sublooring',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-22 19:16:42','2023-07-22 19:16:42'),(734,783,783,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13479556282',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-23 11:04:58','2023-07-23 11:04:58'),(735,784,784,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16189775973',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Living/Dining Area\n- Convert entry closets to be floor to ceiling closets with new doors (remove upper door)\n- Add minibar counter where small closet is, next to double door closet\n- Put in new engineered wood flooring (entire apartment minus bathroom)\n- Determine if wall is possible between bedroom and living room (worried about air flow)\n- Remove wall mirrors and book shelves, paint ceiling and walls in entire apartment (minus bathroom)\n- Replace baseboards\nKitchen \n- Determine if current cabinets can be lifted with toe box to be taller or get new cabinets\n- Replace counter top\n- Replace stove and fridge (determine if water line can be ran to current fridge location)\n- New backsplash\n\nI like white, simple, clean lines, with pops of color.  Like I want a navy wall in my bedroom and on the minibar wall',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-23 23:51:35','2023-07-23 23:51:35'),(736,785,785,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16465659452',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-25 15:51:01','2023-07-25 15:51:01'),(737,786,786,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11777885555',NULL,NULL,NULL,'adasdasd',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-25 19:14:45','2023-07-25 19:14:45'),(738,787,787,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15612333122',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am reaching out in hopes to get some information about possibly working to redo our marketing/storage room. We are a sports based organization and have some ideas in terms of what we would like to incorporate but are hoping to seek a more professional opinion on moving forward for redecorating our space. We hope to incorporate some storage in the back to hold marketing items such as merchandise. But in the front, we hope to have an area where people are able to hang out or have lunch in. We at the moment have stuff in the area, but ideally will be moving alot of it to the back or out of the room.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-26 17:42:12','2023-07-26 17:42:12'),(739,788,788,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11646272965',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello,\nWe would like get a quote for a one bedroom apartment renovation. The project involves the transformation of a the apartment, where we plan to relocate the kitchen to a different area within the unit. The current kitchen space will be converted into a bedroom. We would require new plans submitted for approval and new plumbing for the kitchen. Thank you for your time.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-27 02:12:59','2023-07-27 02:12:59'),(740,789,789,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13059720455',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Garage/Studio renovation',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-27 19:42:51','2023-07-27 19:42:51'),(741,790,790,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13059720455',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Gabi is testing and setting up scenario in Make for Mailchimp',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-27 19:56:26','2023-07-27 19:56:26'),(742,791,791,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14802274649',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We have an accepted offer for 15 Broad Street, Apt 2100.  We wanted to get a few things done and build a third bedroom.  The attached files have details of what we absolutely want to do, and what we would like to get done budget permitting.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-07-29 02:36:05','2023-07-29 02:36:05'),(743,792,792,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19177967330',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Good morning!\nWe live in a townhouse on the Upper East Side and are looking to replace our old cabinets as well as install more lights around our den. Many of the cabinets have fallen off the hinges or are detached from the  main unit.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-01 14:53:39','2023-08-01 14:53:39'),(744,793,793,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19175740596',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remove existing floor and install new floor including kitchen flooring, Demo closet and walls at bathroom entrance, Frame new closet layout with access to bathroom, Install new bathroom door at existing frame, Frame wall to create a bedroom and install new door, Remove and dispose of builtin next to the window.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-01 19:04:07','2023-08-01 19:04:07'),(745,794,794,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13128486236',NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://streeteasy.com/property/1375296-175-west-73-street-9e\n\nFull bathroom remodel \nconvert tub to a shower \nbuild out the bathroom to make it square \n\nFull kitchen remodel \n\nReplace the floors in the entire unit \n\ninstall closet doors (combined closet now)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-01 22:21:11','2023-08-01 22:21:11'),(746,795,795,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13128486236',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-01 22:40:47','2023-08-01 22:40:47'),(747,796,796,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16466454261',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I’m looking to replace the bedroom and bathroom doors. I’d also like to have the door frames sanded down and repainted to make them look nicer.\n\nI also want to install a soaking tub. The current bath tub is too shallow to take baths in. Instead of the shower curtain we’re currently using I’d like to install a partial glass partition. (Maybe something that slides 1/3-2/3, I don’t want a full partition.) I would also like to retile the bathroom floor.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-02 14:21:01','2023-08-02 14:21:01'),(748,797,797,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16077610106',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remove the signs on the plaster wall and refinish the wall to install the new sign.\nThe wall size is W 1203.5\" x H 100\".',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-02 18:22:40','2023-08-02 18:22:40'),(749,798,798,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16179478137',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A mover did significant damage to our apartment and we are looking to get the following scope  repaired;\n\nRepaint damaged Entry Door and Frame scraped \nRepair Brazilian Hardwood Kitchen Door that was scraped\nRepaint Kitchen door frame scraped \nRepair Kitchen Door molding damaged\nRepaint Entry / Living room Floor \nRepair Brazilian Hardwood Cabinet scraped and gouged',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-03 13:14:14','2023-08-03 13:14:14'),(750,799,799,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17184507908',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I\'m looking for a quote for my bathroom remodeling project (about 30 ft2) in Jackson Heights. I\'m planning to change the tile, bath tub, toilet and potentially the sink. Can you send me a quote for this?',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-03 23:42:28','2023-08-03 23:42:28'),(751,800,800,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13477247196',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Full bathroom remodeling, 36 sqr ft',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-04 15:58:49','2023-08-04 15:58:49'),(752,801,801,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12123196919',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Had a major leak in the unit from building pipes bursting\n\n2600 sq ft \n\nreplace all hardwood floors throughout the unit \nreplace all baseboards throughout the unit\n\nReplace millwork cabinetry in the home office \n\nRefinish wall and ceiling paint throughout the unit \n\nkitchen \nreplace all base cabinets that are affected by the water damage \n\nMold remediation company coming next week. Insurance will cover that immediately, all MCG work will be submitted to the insurance company and scheduled for next June, 2024',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-04 18:29:23','2023-08-04 18:29:23'),(753,802,802,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19176124102',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Electric, Plaster repair, Bathroom, Closets, Kitchen, strip paint from window moldings, radiators and possibly doors, floor refinish...  During closing, the plaster became damaged by steam from a radiator valve leak and needs more attention than we\'d hoped. Interested in trying to keep the early 1940\'s original character and feel. Modernize a little, but not too modern in style. We like the original hamper and drying rack in the bathroom (which cannot be seen in the video we are attaching).',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-06 14:43:17','2023-08-06 14:43:17'),(754,803,803,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17863897792',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Master bathroom full renovation \n\n5x11 (Length: 66 inches wall to wall in the tub area,  5 ft wall to wall in the toilet area, and 5 inch wall) \n\nmold in the wall - need to open and fix, this bathroom is adjacent to other other bath. May need to remodel the second bath as well depending on the findings)\n\ninstall double vanity \nReplace the  tub \nfix the mold \ntoilet keep, reuse\nWall tile wet area only \nreplace floor tile \npartition wall btw the toilet - remove the wall possibly \ninstall vent with the light \ncurtain rod \nreplace the mirrors \nceiling fixture replace, wall fixture replace \nreplace the tile around the window \nreplace the door',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-07 14:32:50','2023-08-07 14:32:50'),(755,804,804,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13477010439',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Entire apartment (timeline 2-4 weeks - target to move in by end of August, can do part of the work before we move in the other after we move in)\n- Prep the apartment for the demo work. Remove existing crown\nmoldings in the living, dining rooms, entry hallway and the hallway near the\nbedrooms. Install new crown moldings in these areas. All base/floor moldings\nstay as is.\n- Optional: Provide skim coating in the living/dining and both hallways areas’ walls\nonly (no skim coating on the ceilings), prep the skim coated for the “picture\nframe” moldings installation. Size, design, and calculation of the frames will\nbe discussed with the client.\n- Doors. Replace 6 (six) room doors in the apartment, install new pre-\nfinished doors. All the door jambs will remain as is, replace the door \nlocks/handles and the hinges if needed. Replace tall closet double doors in the\nliving room, if necessary, replace the frame/jamb unit for it, as well.\n- Paint entire apartment walls, ceilings, trim works, and existing doors\n(not pre-finished), new picture frames and crown moldings. No painting in the\nbedrooms, bathrooms, closets is proposed per client’s request. Patch/fix and\npaint the entire apartment walls, ceilings, trims, etc with the low VOC primer\nand paints; patch all the holes and cracks where needed.\nAll the existing hardwood floor planks and the base moldings will remain\nas is, cover/protect them during the work.\n\n\nKitchen and pantry (next few months due to lead time)\n- Full demo in the kitchen and the pantry rooms. Remove existing kitchen\ncabinets, countertops, appliances and sink, flooring in kitchen and the pantry\nareas; inspect the subfloor, repair as needed, and provided waterproofing\nmembrane (or other) before floor installation (All the buildings and Board\nrequirements). Remove the partition wall top near the doorway to the kitchen,\nopen it up to the ceiling.\n\n2.- Design the kitchen cabinetry with the same layout/locations of the\nappliances, fixtures and cabinets. Optional: see the possibility to relocate and\ncombine washer and dryer units next to the kitchen sink and make them\nstackable if possible. Or move the refrigerator to the middle of the pantry area\n- Electrical work. Bring all the electrical connection to the code. Provide\nelectrical work in the kitchen, update all the outlets and switches, and provide\nthe power lines for the under-cabinet lights if needed.\n- Prep the area for the rough plumbing, replace and update the\nsink/dishwasher water valves and drain pipes. Patch and paint all walls and\nceilings in new kitchen;\n- Install new tile or hardwood flooring, new kitchen cabinets, light\nfixtures, dishwasher, stove, fridge, hood, double oven/microwave units,\nwasher/dryer, etc;\n- Install new kitchen sink and the faucet, and finish kitchen plumbing\nafter installing stone countertop and the backsplash.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-07 20:04:37','2023-08-07 20:04:37'),(756,805,805,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13127254036',NULL,NULL,NULL,'1bd renovation at East River Coop 455 FDR Dr B1904\nRemove wall between living space and kitchen (requires architect). Renovate kitchen  new cabinets/countertop/peninsula. \nMake flooring consistent across living space, bedroom, kitchen, and closets. \nBathroom renovation. Replace alcove tub, flooring, walls, toilet, vanity, recessed mirror. Install washlet. \nBring electrical up to code.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-08 18:06:28','2023-08-08 18:06:28'),(757,806,806,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15033193361',NULL,NULL,NULL,'i need you to fully furnished my house',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-09 04:59:20','2023-08-09 04:59:20'),(758,807,807,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19173799926',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello! I own a store in Brooklyn.\nThe store is need of repairs.\nCeiling needs fixing or replacing, 800ish of flooring needs installing.\nfront of store needs repairs. Basement stairs and entire ceiling need fixing or replacing.\nA wall needs to be removed and replace with new wall.\n\nI am not opposed to design service as well. Thanks!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-09 15:50:45','2023-08-09 15:50:45'),(759,808,808,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16087062064',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Actually I just reviewed your business, and I thought that professional and eye catching logo would be the great additon for your business? We will design 3 eye catching logo concepts for you and will show you the logos within couple of hours today and if you like it then you may pay us only $50 if not that\'s fine.And it means that you have not to pay until you like the three samples of logo designs.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-09 18:42:45','2023-08-09 18:42:45'),(760,809,809,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19176603721',NULL,NULL,NULL,'113 Liberty View Dr, 1G, Jersey City, NJ07302\n\nI am opening a childcare center at the above address. I need a Cert of Occupancy. The last tenant was also a childcare center. They moved out, I moved in. No renovation. Building Dept asked me for a blueprint/drawing of the space.\n\nPlease let me know your pricing, or if you need more info, email nhat.ntu@gmail.com or call 9176603721',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-09 22:57:54','2023-08-09 22:57:54'),(761,810,810,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17046043523',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Full kitchen renovation \nreplace cabinets, appliances, floors \nmove the stove 6 inches off the wall to have access \n\nbathroom full renovation \ntub reglaze \nAdd glass partition half wall \nTile full wet area and half wall at the end of the tub and sink, rest painted  \n\ninstall washer/dryer in the hallway closet \n\nreplace the floors partially in the hallway (prior water damage)\n\npaint walls and ceilings, doors and trims, inside the closets\n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/property/1257991-425-east-63-street-e1e',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-10 16:53:58','2023-08-10 16:53:58'),(762,811,811,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15126578451',NULL,NULL,NULL,'kitchen\nu shaped \nreplace appliances and cabinets \ntile floor replace with vinyl floor (no work on our end)\ngas stove \nno work on the light \nno under cabinet light  \nreplace countertop and backsplash, tile backsplash \nno window \nisland no work \nno doors \nno paint work \n\n\nmaster bath \nfull gut\njacuzzi and standing shower \nreplace the tub with another jacuzzi\ndouble, replace with the standing vanity \nreplace toilet with standing (provide options for floating) \nmirrors now, replace with mirrors\nreplace ceiling fixture with recessed light \nreplace the wall light \nwindow no work \nno painting in the bath \nno work on the doors \nwet areas \n\nmodern design for both, will send inspiration \nWill send photos of the space, does not have a floor plan\nplanning stage, will be his first estimate',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-10 18:47:09','2023-08-10 18:47:09'),(763,812,812,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16467171167',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Redo bathroom entirely:\n- New bathtub/shower combo\n- New sink\n- New toilet\n- New flooring\n\nNote: inspiration photo is just for the vibe. We are not looking for something exactly like that. We would like there to be a lot of built in storage including storage behind the mirror. Open to your input and creativity.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-11 17:32:49','2023-08-11 17:32:49'),(764,813,813,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12126514388',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi, im a real estate agent and my clients are looking at a property at 430 East 87th. Theyd like to open up the living room wall into the primary to creat a large lving space nd add a door into the studio apartment next door making the studio a primary. They would also like to delete the current kitchen in the studio and renovate the studio bathroom and kitchen. \n\nplease see the included listing below',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-12 20:05:31','2023-08-12 20:05:31'),(765,814,814,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12246377839',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I want to redo the flooring of this apartment and switch out the cabinets to something very nice and modern while still being budget friendly.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-15 03:57:23','2023-08-15 03:57:23'),(766,815,815,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19543191545',NULL,NULL,NULL,'enclose existing 180 sq ft carport and relocate kitchen.\n1 new bathroom.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-15 18:39:59','2023-08-15 18:39:59'),(767,816,816,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14257368978',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remove carpet, repair and refinish hardwood. Strip and re-paint walls, repair walls as needed. GFCI outlets installed throughout. Demo sealed dumbwaiter shaft and install washer/dryer. Explore demo of wall between kitchen and living room.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-16 14:11:29','2023-08-16 14:11:29'),(768,817,817,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18622161358',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are looking to get our floors redone (believe it needs a sand/buff and refinish) as well as repaint our entire unit. We are in a one bedroom apartment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-17 14:42:21','2023-08-17 14:42:21'),(769,818,818,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17863761848',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are looking to maximize the living space by opening the kitchen/living room areas, add master bedroom.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-17 20:14:50','2023-08-17 20:14:50'),(770,819,819,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16318969194',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bathroom Remodel 1:\nRe tile floor and walls to ceiling\nRemove bath tub /Shower installation \nRemove toilet/ New toilet installation\nMillwork for 2 cabinets and heater cover\nRefinish current vanity and keep current marble countertop\nChange out fixtures and lighting\n\nBathroom Remodel 2:\nRe tile floor and walls to ceiling\nRemove pedestal sink/ New pedestal sink installation\nRemove toilet/ New toilet installation\nMillwork for 1 cabinet and heater cover\nChange out fixtures and lighting\nFix window\n\nPrimary Bedroom:\nElectrical to add second sconce and outlets for each side of bed\nMillwork for wall built in unitMillwork for heat and AC cover\nMillwork for closet doorShelving for small walk in closet\nRepainting\n\nHome Office:\nMillwork for heat and AC cover\nShelving for closet\n\nLiving Room:\nElectrical to install second sconce on other side of couch\nMillwork for heat and AC cover\n\nKitchen:\nRemodel cabinets\nNew countertop, backsplash, sink, fixtures\nNew appliances',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-17 22:27:02','2023-08-17 22:27:02'),(771,820,820,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12016559437',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi - I am closing on a condo at The Windsor (107-24 71st Rd, Queens, NY 11375) apartment #10B. I am looking to renovate the kitchen, paint the walls, change the doors and handles, update shades, update light fixtures, replace floors, and renovate the primary bathroom. The apartment is 1,300 square feet - a 2 bedroom and 2 bathroom space. You can find pictures of its current condition here: https://photos.google.com/share/AF1QipNhEoV12uVl10c3zfA9U1Q5i9MpKz3qCcmWnir0Ftzy1gh7ZECl3DJx1GeCD-27Fg?key=aU50aGYyT21sSldkNmVrdnJMYzhjSl9MN2ZHV3pB\n\nI look forward to hearing from you. Thank you!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-18 02:22:30','2023-08-18 02:22:30'),(772,821,821,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14154252049',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello, I was wondering if you could help me the last week of August with four small jobs, about one day\'s work (but requiring two visits).  I\'ve attached pictures.\n\n    The insulation around my metal door frame is crumbling into dust.  I would like it removed, but it is screwed in, so the holes have to be filled in and painted over.  I have the paint color for the door frame (it will also need a metal primer).\n\n    The metal door has a scratch.  Can you touch it up without repainting the whole door?  It was last painted in 2016.  I have the paint color for the door (it will also need a metal primer).  This is low priority.\n\n    My newly refinished tub was caulked with GE Advanced Silicone 2 (white).  But after a couple of weeks, I gently wiped it, and the caulk just peeled up like paper.  Apparently it wasn\'t really sealed, and as soon as you touched it, the unsealing spread.  To avoid damaging the new paint, the caulk was removed with a plastic razor, we let it dry for 24 hours, wiped lightly with alcohol and let dry another 30 minutes, then recaulked, and I didn\'t use it for 36 hours.  But the same problem happened again.  I need recaulking, but am showering with the failed seal for now and just wiping it dry with a paper towel afterwards.  I prefer to remove the caulk, wait a couple of days to make sure it is dry, then recaulk.  This is a priority.\n\n    The granite kitchen counter needs to be caulked.  The brown grout along the backsplash washed out (reno was 15 years ago but in good condition), and a painter painted over the caulk along the side, which gets a little wet from the sink.  The paint along the edge needs to be scraped and touched up, and the area recaulked--do you recommend clear silicone, or brown or gray caulk? I have the wall paint for this.\n\nI am going on vacation Aug. 20-27, and hope to have this done Aug. 30-Sept. 1.  This is because my office is allowing remote work that week, so it\'s convenient, and also since I am showering with failed caulk, I want to fix that as soon as possible.  I know these are small jobs, but if you can help, please let me know an estimate breakdown and if you prefer I provide supplies.\n\nThanks so much,\nAnnie\n415-425-2049',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-18 15:36:47','2023-08-18 15:36:47'),(773,822,822,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19494390496',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi! Here are my renovations in list of priority. I spoke to Daniel on the phone a little bit about them. It is a new building currently finishing up and I want to switch up the finishes and potentially add some space. \n\n1. ADD CLOSET\n- in the space between the bathroom and the W/D, create a skinny, deep linen closet \n- Add shelving \n\n2. BATHROOM \n- Demo whole bathroom interior \n- paint, new vanity, new toilet, new tiles, new everything \n- make space smaller (shave off room for linen closet) \n\n3. BEHIND THE FRONT DOOR \n- add sliding door or some door to create a closet in that tiny sliver. \n- add shelving possibly\n\n4. BEDROOM\n- Tear out current closet + make wall flat \n- on one of the longer walls create a floor to ceiling wardrobe wall \n- to shave off costs, use IKEA PAX carcass as base\n- paint and simple crown molding in whole bedroom \n\n5. KITCHEN \n- Paint cabinets beige and add paneling to cabinets like inspo',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-19 17:25:50','2023-08-19 17:25:50'),(774,823,823,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15717079789',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The support posts are leaning in the crawlspace and the main beam towards the front is starting to dip and twist. \n\nThe deck has some rusted teko straps Item 1(Picture) and and area shored up unprofessionally Item 2(Picture). There is also a large hole in the rear where a possible staircase might go Item 4(Picture). There is also a footing that is cracked. Item 5(Picture). Some of the decking is loose and needs to be screwed down Item 3(Picture). Recommend having all repaired by a licensed contractor.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-19 20:29:34','2023-08-19 20:29:34'),(775,824,824,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18173072602',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We recently purchased a 2 bedroom coop in the uws.  Looking to have it renovated. Please call to discuss details. Thank you',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-20 16:18:41','2023-08-20 16:18:41'),(776,825,825,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11908591257',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello, I would like to schedule a consultation to renovate my bathroom and kitchen.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-22 18:39:37','2023-08-22 18:39:37'),(777,826,826,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13056066003',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-23 18:15:37','2023-08-23 18:15:37'),(778,827,827,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19175336745',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello, my name is Paul and Id like to have my guest bathroom remodeled.  I want a minimal modern look.  Id like white subway tile with black grout and black hex tile on the floor.  Tub will be replaced with walk in shower even floor with full room.  \n\nAll other fixtures including toilet and showerhead and sink vanity will be replaced.  I will supply the replacements to be installed.  \n\nI can tell you morw details during a walk through.  I would like to have you come out to site on friday or monday.  Preferrably friday if possible.  My number is 917-533-6745.  \n\nI can provide pictures via text from that number as the upload feature here does not seem to be working.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-24 04:50:44','2023-08-24 04:50:44'),(779,828,828,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14012012012',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hey\nI would like to offer some suggestions for your site. No commitment for future work, fine print, or hidden anything - just an opportunity for you to see how we can improve your site and leads.\n\nWould it be ok to send you the suggestions I have in mind?\n\nPlease let me know.\nRegards,\nSteve Johnson',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-24 04:52:43','2023-08-24 04:52:43'),(780,829,829,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1352813978',NULL,NULL,NULL,'no',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-25 01:51:29','2023-08-25 01:51:29'),(781,830,830,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19517648549',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello,\n\nWe live in the west village, and we have a couple items in our two bathrooms that we\'d like fixed/renovated: \n\n1. Our glass shower door recently fell off - we\'d like to completely replace this with a sliding glass door. It\'s a floor to ceiling shower(no bathtub), and the aesthetic of the house is quite bare and modern. The drainage system is also quite finicky and gets dirty/clogged very easily, so we\'d love to replace that with something more practical as well.\n\n2. Our downstairs bathroom shower/bath plumbing has always been a little strange. The temperature knob doesn\'t work and it\'s not possible to switch between the bath faucet and the showerhead. We\'d like to re-do the system so that it works, and perhaps install a door or splash guard as well. (There\'s a curtain on there right now)\n\n3. We need a closet door fixed/replaced\n\nPlease let us know if you can give us a quote, or if you need more information/pictures. Thanks so much for your time. \n\nBest,\nJae',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-28 22:13:24','2023-08-28 22:13:24'),(782,831,831,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19173457410',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Basement full assessment: - Frame and close off the washer dryer and hvac with walls and separate doors – Install recessed lights throughout the space and new electrical outlets and light switches – Close the ceiling with sheetrock Install new vinyl floors throughout - Install heating, baseboard radiators - Paint everything 1 st Floor: - Paint everything - Cover the popcorn ceilings by laminating with sheetrock over all areas where there are pop-corn ceilings - Install Recessed lights everywhere (entry, hallway, living / dining room). (The kitchen already has lights.) – Remove all interior doors and install new, and new door handles – Remove existing and install all new closet doors - Install new backyard door – Remove the current baseboards - Install all new vinyl flooring above the existing (the current floors are straight and sturdy, no squeaks or gaps, great to serve as base.) - Install new baseboards Replace floor in the bathroom Replace radiator - Kitchen: Existing kitchen cabinets will be removed, sand and paint Install new sink and new countertops - Install new Backsplash Create some type of venting system to outside from the kitchen Run electrical line and install outlet on the island 2 nd Floor: - Cap the stairs or stain them to have the same or similar floor finish look as the new flooring from downstairs (or upstairs. Client will decide on the final floor finish). – Gut renovates the bathrooms Install a few hallway lights (recessed or regular ceiling lights) – Close off one room from the rest (with sheetrock, or shelf, TBD) Replace radiator Soundproof room and bathroom Within the room install small kitchenette instead of the closet (bathroom is at the back, to take water from and run pluming lines) – Laminate the ceilings where there is pop-corn with sheetrock, so it’s new and straight - Convert the primary bathroom from tub to standing shower - Paint everything (hallway, room, hallway between room and bathroom and bathroom) Fix and repair all closets on the second (all new closet doors) Tenant entry Replace the two doors Remove carpet and install vinyl wood on the stairs Paint the hallway Replace radiator Change lights in the hallway Other exterior repair Ground floor: replace black door Fix siding change rotten wood Sand and prime, fill and fix and paint – Fix the exterior 3 steps that are cracking- epoxy stairs crack - Power-wash the stairs - And then paint stairs with exterior hard paint backyard Install small awning above the backyard door so the rain doesn’t come in',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-29 17:37:53','2023-08-29 17:37:53'),(783,832,832,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13474396441',NULL,NULL,NULL,'After fire incident, restoration work is underway. Almost completed. Need to start work for new kitchen, floor, paint.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-30 18:03:18','2023-08-30 18:03:18'),(784,833,833,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12679948316',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remove the closet, which was built on top of the floor and has electricity box in it, add two real walls to make it a real bedroom (right hand side of the living room from floor plan, Electrical box shall be embedded in the wall), however the floor is now fully covered by wooden floor.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-08-31 17:38:16','2023-08-31 17:38:16'),(785,834,834,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16178667234',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello,\n\nmy name is Tim Ioannidis and I\'m the owner of a small studio apartment at 240E 46th St in Manhattan (post-war, well-maintained building). \n\nI found your contact information online since I would like to plan a renovation project to replace the kitchen and bathroom (and potentially some closet space as well), ideally sometime this fall. It will require bringing down a wall to open up the kitchen area.\n\nIs that something you can potentially help me with? What\'s the usual process?\n\nThanks,\nTim Ioannidis',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-01 16:55:07','2023-09-01 16:55:07'),(786,835,835,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13334445555',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I\'m looking to get a ball park range quote for build out of bar in LIC/Astoria area ~2500 square feet.\n\nhi it will be approx 10 room karaoke bar with an open bar area up front',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-02 13:37:45','2023-09-02 13:37:45'),(787,836,836,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16464041351',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello,\n\nLooking to fully renovate our kitchen. All cabinets, countertops, backsplashes & floor.\n\nAprox. 10 ft long x 8 ft wide\n\nPlease do let us know what other information is necessary to provide with a rough estimation.\n\nThanks,',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-03 00:46:06','2023-09-03 00:46:06'),(788,837,837,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12038955172',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am interested in creating a media unit with a built in electric fire place and bookcases built in a coop in Queens.\n\nThe space is 8 feet 8 inches wide, 1 foot deep.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-05 01:54:05','2023-09-05 01:54:05'),(789,838,838,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16174652921',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Design, choose furniture and suppliers, purchase and install.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-06 12:11:39','2023-09-06 12:11:39'),(790,839,839,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13479089348',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We need help we the city riquirements as follow Structural\n\n1. CLARIFY SCOPE OF WORK. CLEARLY IDENTIFY ALL NEW WORK TO BE PERFORMED AND ALL EXISTING CONSTRUCTION AND OTHER PLAN ELEMENTS. PROVIDE ALL NECESSARY DRAWINGS AND OTHER INFORMATION. DRAWINGS MUST BE OF SUFFICIENT CLARITY AND QUALITY TO EFFECTIVELY CONVEY THE NATURE AND SCOPE OF THE PROPOSED WORK. \n\n2. PROVIDE DIGITALLY SIGNED/SEALED PLANS AND DOCUMENTATION OR SUBMIT MANUALLY SIGNED/SEALED/DATED (IN ORIGINAL) PLANS AND DOCUMENTATION AT THE BLDG. DEPT., FOR PROCESSING/SCANNING INTO OUR SYSTEM.\n\nElectrical\n\n1.PROVIDE LIGHT POLE MANUFACTURE SPECIFICATIONS (CUT SHEETS). FBC 107. 2.PROVIDE LIGHT POLE BRANCH CIRCUIT INFORMATION, SUCH AS CONDUIT, CONDUCTORS   AND OCPD SIZE. 3.PROVIDE GFCI RECEPTACLE @BATHROOM 3\' FROM SINK. NEC 210.52(D). 4.TAMPER RESISTAN RECEPTACLE REQUIRED. NEC 406.12. ADD NOTE ON PLAN. 5.PROVIDE/DEPICT ILLUMINATION @BATHROOM (LIGHT & SWITCH). NEC 210.70. 6.SMOKE ALARM REQUIRED INSIDE AND OUTSIDE ALL SLEEPING UNITS. FBC 907. 7.DRAWINGS TO BE SIGNED BY ELECTRICAL QUALIFIER AND NOTARIZED. FS 489.505.12. REVIEWER: SANTANA CAICEDO, PHONE# 786-315-2269. EMAIL: CAICEDO@MIAMIDADE.GOV THIS PLANS ARE INCOMPLETE. RESPONSE TO ABOVE COMMENTS MAY GENERATE ADDITIONAL  COMMENTS AT NEXT REVIEW.\n\nPROVIDE MANUFACTURER SPECIFICATIONS SHEETS. FBC 107\nPROVIDE PANEL SCHEDULE - CIRCUIT/CONDUCTORRACEWAY/OCPD/VA, SIZES. NEC 220.14,   NEC 240.4\nMISSING GFCI FOR ACCESSORY BUILDINGS, BATHROOM, GARAGE, KITCHEN, OUTSIDE,       SINKS, AND WITHIN 25\' OF AC UNITS. NEC 210.8 & NEC 210.63\nPROVIDE NOTE ON PLAN FOR TAMPER RESISTANT RECEPTACLE OUTLETS REQUIRED. NEC      406.12\nSMOKE ALARMS REQUIRED INSIDE & OUTSIDE ALL SLEEPING AREAS. FBC 907\nDRAWINGS TO BE SIGNED BY ALARM OR ELECTRICAL QUALIFIER AND NOTARIZED. FS        489.505.12\nREQUIRE NEW ELECTRICAL SHEETS. FBC 10728\nPLEASE PROVIDE A RESPONSE SHEET. FBC 107\n\nPlumbing\n\nTHIS REVIEW IS FOR: BATHROOM RENOVATION, 1-PROVIDE COMPLETE PROPOSED ARCHITECTURAL FLOOR PLAN AND SITE PLAN INDICATING THE AREA OF WORK (FBC/B107.3.5). 2-PROVIDE SANITARY AND WATER PIPE LAYOUT/CONNECTION TO THE EXISTING FOR THE BATHROOM RECONFIGURATION (FBC/B107.3.5). 3-PLEASE ADD/PROVIDE PLUMBING FIXTURES CLEARANCES PER FBCR P2705.1 4- THE PLAN MUST BE SEALED, SIGNED AND DATED BY THE DESIGN PROFESSIONAL OR HAVE THE CONTRACTOR QUALIFIERS NUMBER WITH THE PRINTED NAME OF THE QUALIFIER, THEN SIGNED BY THE QUALIFIER, DATED AND NOTARIZED. IT MUST ALSO INCLUDE THE OWNERS NAME AND JOB ADDRESS ON ALL PAGES. FOR QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS REVIEW COMMENTS, YOU CAN EMAIL ME AT CLAY.DENNIS@MIAMIDADE.GOV .\n\nZoning\n\n1. PLANS ARE INCOMPLETE AND A THOROUGH REVIEW IS NOT POSSIBLE AT THIS TIME. 2.  SCOPE OF WORK IS FOR A RAMP/BATH, A DETAILED FLOOR PLAN AND SITE PLAN WILL BE REQUIRED SHOWING SCOPE OF WORK AND LOCATION. 3. OTHER COMMENTS MAY FOLLOW. 4.EMAIL JESSE.HERNANDEZ@MIAMIDADE.GOV IF YOU HAVE ANY QUESTIONS\n\nBuilding\n\n1-CONSTRUCTION DOCUMENTS SHALL BE OF SUFFICIENT CLARITY TO INDICATE THE   LOCATION, NATURE AND EXTENT OF THE WORK PROPOSED AND SHOW IN DETAIL   THAT IT WILL CONFORM TO THE PROVISIONS OF THIS CODE - FBC 107.2.1 -  A-PROVIDE STRUCTURAL AND ARCHITECTURAL PLANS FOR LANDINGS AND RAMPS SHOWING    ALL DETAILS FOR EDGE PROTECTION, HAND RAILS ETC..  B-PROVIDE ALL DETAILS OF BATHROOM CONVERSION TO INCLUDE MATERIALS, HEIGHTS    OF INSTALLATION ETC.. 2-THE CONSTRUCTION DOCUMENTS SHALL BE PREPARED BY A REGISTERED DESIGN   PROFESSIONAL  - FBC 107.1 FURTHER REVIEW PENDING RECEIPT OF REQUESTED DOCUMENTATION. IF YOU HAVE ANY QUESTIONS REGARDING THESE REVIEW COMMENTS, PLEASE CONTACT DON HATLEY BY E-MAIL AT A666@MIAMIDADE.GOV',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-06 16:42:27','2023-09-06 16:42:27'),(791,840,840,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19173557969',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi, I would like to have a basic renovation of my kitchen, and bathroom area, in a Manhattan studio apartment (floor-plan included).  \n\nKitchen:  Remove existing appliances, renovate the walls and floor.  Resurface the floor, and walls.  Install new toilet, sink and fixtures, including sink, cabinets, refrigerator and dishwasher.   Expand entrance-way to kitchen.\n\nBathroom: Remove existing fixtures, floor and wall.  Expand entrance-way areas to bathroom.  Install bamboo wall, re-tile walls.  install tankless toilet and bidget, new vanity etc',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-08 18:38:42','2023-09-08 18:38:42'),(792,841,841,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13478396715',NULL,NULL,NULL,'jewelry company, 12 people now, need to expand to 20 people capacity\n\nbreak one wall \n\nremodel the offices to fit more people \n\n hvac split between the offices \n\nmove the jewelry vaults - as per building requirements need reinforced wall\n\n\nPlease kindly see attached for :\nProposed layout and demolition plan\nProposed layout w. vaults\nOur current space marked up ourselves just for overview\nSample COI',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-08 20:49:11','2023-09-08 20:49:11'),(793,842,842,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13012549386',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Repair floor tile in corner next to tub (8\" square area), remove tile in bathroom (tub/shower area and walls), replace with standard white subway tile, replace tub/shower faucet fixtures, install shower curtain rod.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-09 15:10:27','2023-09-09 15:10:27'),(794,843,843,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1783443127',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Galley style kitchen, coop apt, Queens NY.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-09 15:39:58','2023-09-09 15:39:58'),(795,844,844,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13476687434',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kitchen, mid size NYC Queens condominium. Gut renovation and redesign possible - need assessment of structural status and potential',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-09 21:01:22','2023-09-09 21:01:22'),(796,845,845,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17249947122',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello, \n\nWe are working on medium-sized kitchen project in the UES. Currently, the kitchen is partially torn apart, but we plan on demoing what is left of the kitchen and then building a new one out. We have a millworker on board already and have the design figured out. I attached the plans for your review. We are ready to go asap so the faster',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-10 17:08:38','2023-09-10 17:08:38'),(797,846,846,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13476994999',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Renovation of 5\' x 7\' primary bathroom in co-op apartment. Replacement of all fixtures. Changes to electrical and plumbing. New tile for floors and shower.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-13 18:01:29','2023-09-13 18:01:29'),(798,847,847,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17862033672',NULL,NULL,NULL,'bathroom remodel 9x5 ft\n\nreplace the wall tile wet area + full wall on the vanity wall, the rest is painted\n\nreplace the floor tile \n\nno work on the tub, curtain rod, no work\n\nreplace the vanity \n\nremove the separate medicine cabinet and mirror \n\nInstall a new medicine cabinet above the vanity \n\nreuse the toilet \n\nno window \n\nno work on the door\n\nreplace the wall fixture \n\nreplace the outlets and the light switch (the boxes and covers)\n\nno additional shelves above the toilet \n\ntoilet and vanity base mounted \n\nreplace the fan cover \n\nmodern style, light, maybe grey color',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-14 18:52:41','2023-09-14 18:52:41'),(799,848,848,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16783334802',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The unit is a 2 bedroom, 2 bath house, lower level unit of a duplex. I would like to do a full kitchen and bathroom remodel, converting a half bath to a full bath to make it 2 full bathrooms. for the kitchen, I would like an open layout. Also, would like to do tile flooring throughout the unit and identify/create a space for washer/dryer unit.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-15 22:45:09','2023-09-15 22:45:09'),(800,849,849,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17189749958',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I need renovation done to my one-family home.  It is currently 4 bedrooms and 4 baths.  Two baths upstairs with 4 bedrooms. I bath on the first floor with a kitchen, a living room and the formal dining room used as a bedroom.  The basement has one bath and open space. We currently use the basement as a storage and laundry. \nOn the first floor, we would like a bedroom with an accessible bathroom/shower: eat-in kitchen and a half bath. \nThe four bedrooms on the second floor, we want each with a closet and two of the bedrooms with inbuilt bathrooms and a shared bathroom for two bedrooms.\nThe basement with a full bath. Laundry and one or two bedrooms. apartment.\nThank you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-16 22:45:16','2023-09-16 22:45:16'),(801,850,850,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14804679176',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Full Kitchen Renovation after water damage from unit above. Also interested in remodeling the bathroom while work is being done.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-17 14:18:21','2023-09-17 14:18:21'),(802,851,851,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19177477582',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I wish to renovate a small space in Lower East NY.\nCould you please assist with a price quote for the following:\nRemoving a \"78.7x \"123.62 plaster wall.\nRebuilding the wall (\"78.7x \"123.62): layered plaster, wood, construction, wood and plaster.\nCovering  \"287x\"123.62 brick wall with wood, construction, plaster and paint.\nPlease find attached images of the space with marks on the specified walls.\nI look forward to hearing back from you.\n \nBest regards,\nAdina',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-18 18:27:08','2023-09-18 18:27:08'),(803,852,852,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18083440038',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Renovate two bathrooms, possibly a new bathroom addition',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-19 18:38:35','2023-09-19 18:38:35'),(804,853,853,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11917576898',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Renovation of 3 family Brooklyn Brownstone. Ideally not a full gut. Would need to add split units for heating/cooling, upgrade electrical and plumbing, and conform to revised floor plan for each floor outlined by our architect/expediter (we already have one). But we\'re trying to stick to as much of original floor plan as possible. This would be for investment purposes.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-20 19:28:59','2023-09-20 19:28:59'),(805,854,854,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12039425391',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We want to remodel our in-law suite which was originally transformed from a detached one-car garage more than 10 years ago. There\'s an opportunity to make it a loft space ideal for a home office and improved guest cottage.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-23 15:39:09','2023-09-23 15:39:09'),(806,855,855,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13016467828',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello - I am interested in getting a quote for an apt renovation on the UES. The apartment is a 1 bd and 1.5 bathroom. The apt is located on 400 E 56th New York NY 10022. We are interested in renovating the kitchen, the master bathroom, converting the dining room into a second bedroom, and adding a closet to the master bedroom. \n\nAttaching original floor plan and desired floor plan with annotations on what we want to remodel.\n\nOld apartment listing that contains picture of current state: https://streeteasy.com/building/plaza-400/24o\n\nThank you,\nNicolas.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-23 22:24:16','2023-09-23 22:24:16'),(807,856,856,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19177444356',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Two one beds, need to combine the units (500 sq ft each) \n\n one unit convert into a bigger kitchen and living room the other unit will be two bedrooms\n\ntwo bathrooms, two fireplaces, one needs to be renovated \n\nfull reno on all rooms in both units \n\nneeds architectural work + renovation',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-09-25 