:10','2023-10-08 15:20:10'),(827,876,876,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12623272409',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am looking to refresh my kitchen with new cabinet doors/paint (or replacement cost depending), backsplash, floors, appliances, and countertops.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-09 17:41:48','2023-10-09 17:41:48'),(828,877,877,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13472603202',NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://streeteasy.com/building/liberty-court/8m\n\nfull bathroom remodel \nnew fixtures \nnew tub \nglass door sliding \nfloor to ceiling wall tile \nreplace floor tile \nno niche \ntoilet and vanity wall mounted \nrecessed medicine cabinet double \nwall light replace - one long fixture above the medicine cabinet \ndoor and trim - refinish - ???\nconcealed toilet tank \n\nDesign: \nlarge format style on the walls - cement like \nwood looking tile floor \nwood vanity to match the floor \nstainless steel \n\nKitchen - full remodel \nopen the kitchen - make an island \nneed demo only - and floor waterproofing \nhardwood floors \nall cabinets, appliances and countertop/backsplash by themselves \n\nwhite kitchen cabinets, white countertop and backsplash \nstainless steel fixtures \n\nDesign:\n img-0153 - a stylistic example of what we want. This is our apartment in Minsk\n- img-0174 - a stylistic reference with the wooden bathroom vanity cabinet and grey walls \n- img-0199 - the plan with measurements',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-09 22:14:31','2023-10-09 22:14:31'),(829,878,878,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13302613626',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Primary and secondary bathroom remolded',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-10 16:51:29','2023-10-10 16:51:29'),(830,879,879,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15615421647',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am Heidi from DataMax System Solutions. We are located in Boca Raton, FL 33487.\nWe are looking to redesign what we call Suite C.  It is a pretty large space with a reception area, conference room, 5 offices, 1 bathroom and an open floor with cubicles.  The view is a pretty lake. I\'ve attached some photos.  We don\'t know if we want to knock wall down or just do interior design but if someone could come out and advise us we would greatly appreciate it. Thank you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-11 18:48:14','2023-10-11 18:48:14'),(831,880,880,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18622018212',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I own a single family property in Newark Nj in a R-3 zone. I’m interested in converting to a 2 family.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-11 23:32:26','2023-10-11 23:32:26'),(832,881,881,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19544246222',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Our office is currently set up for 8 people but we would like to redesign it to accommodate at least 11. \n\nOur wish list:\n•	Open layout to maximize space\n•	Accommodate 10 desks for our staff, around 5-6’ wide, with a small drawer cabinet that can maybe go under the desk. \n•	We would like to have glass dividers to block out some of the noise as everyone takes phone calls throughout the day. I am proposing glass only to keep the space “open” but open to your suggestions.\n•	The glass office will remain for our CEO. We aren’t planning on touching this space except to maybe replace his current desk with a desk that also serves as a small conference table for meetings.\n•	Its ok to “block” windows if needed. Its no problem if a desk needs to face a window and covers it partially, for example.\n•	We need to reserve room for 3 things: a tall filing cabinet, the router box and our Xerox machine.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-13 14:33:31','2023-10-13 14:33:31'),(833,882,882,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13473248131',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Looking at renovations that could be in 2 stages or combined and done all at once depending on costs.\n\nStage 1 - Open up kitchen to the living room, ideally with walk through access. Close off dining room into multi-purpose room /or third bedroom. Re-model kitchen. Also thinking about moving cupboard on the right side of the front door to open up space and adding additional narrow storage along the walls in the gallery area.\n\nStage 2 - Rip and replace for 2.5 bathrooms. Both full bathrooms have tubs and almost exactly the same layout - we would replace one with a tub and the other with a shower.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-14 01:49:12','2023-10-14 01:49:12'),(834,883,883,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13059720455',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-16 17:45:19','2023-10-16 17:45:19'),(835,884,884,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17203558339',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-17 15:33:00','2023-10-17 15:33:00'),(836,885,885,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19176992829',NULL,NULL,NULL,'attic renovation, outside terrace addition, stucco siding',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-17 16:13:10','2023-10-17 16:13:10'),(837,886,886,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19176370506',NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://streeteasy.com/building/lincoln-terrace/2e\n\nkitchen reno \nreplace floor with the wood \nreplace all cabinets  - open shelves on the side of the fridge, the rest cabinets \nreplace appliances with the stainless steel (reuse the microwave)\nslab countertop and backsplash \nreplace ceiling fixture \nno under cabinet lights \nno door \nDesign: totally white cabinets and backsplash marble like, flat cabinets, brushed nickel/chrome to match the appliances, light wood floors: like white oak /pine - colder tones possibly \n\nbathroom reno \nreplace tub for a tub \nreplace all fixtures \nlarge white tiles, minimal grout lines \n50% tiles on the wall \ngrey textures tile on the wall, simple design \nwall mounted vanity \ntoilet is base \nmedicine cabinet - replace with a double recessed medicine cabinet \nreplace the wall light - line of light bulbs across \nno ceiling light \nReplace with curtain rod \nreplace the door with a slab door, replace trim \nrelocate the outlet in the bath possibly ? \nDesign: minimalist style with a bit of a flare. Everything white/light \n\nEntire unit: \nReplace all doors and trims:\nreplace 2 bifold doors with two sliding doors - one in the hallway, one in the bedroom. \nfoyer closet replace with pocket door \nReplace 4 doors with single slab doors - one in the living room (not shown on the floor plan), one in the bedroom, one in the bathroom, one in the WIC.\nno refinish in the closets, just the floors and doors \n\nreplace closet organization in the sliding doors closet in the bedroom \n\nreplace the floors with wood and baseboards \n\npaint everything - all rooms\n\nElectrical panel: 8 brackers on the panel, should be in a good shape \n\nHas many decor items picked out already',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-17 22:48:37','2023-10-17 22:48:37'),(838,887,887,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19549146880',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello. I described everything on attached file. Please read and send me approximate quote. Thanks',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-18 14:13:14','2023-10-18 14:13:14'),(839,888,888,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16463789884',NULL,NULL,NULL,'This is a 1957 white brick mid-rise co-op studio apartment with a galley kitchen. Dimensions: 7\' x 6\'. The original metal cabinets are in place, along with the original built-in slattery oven. The renovation I have in mind is to: \n     -Replace all the metal cabinets \n     -Install a new gas oven (the current stove is gas)\n     -Install new overhead light fixture\n     -Install ductless exhaust hood over cooktop\nIn 2016, I upgraded the sink, faucet, cooktop, and replaced the countertop with granite. In 2009, I had new wood floors put in. The plumbing was brought up to code.\n\nThis renovation is being done in advance of putting the apartment up for sale or perhaps to rent long-term.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-19 01:29:56','2023-10-19 01:29:56'),(840,889,889,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13059720455',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-20 18:52:31','2023-10-20 18:52:31'),(841,890,890,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17818505633',NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://www.redfin.com/FL/Miami/16451-SW-45th-St-33185/home/43375397\n\nmaster bathroom remodel, approx 10 by 10 ft, maybe a bit larger. \n\njacuzzi tub leaks replace the tub with regular deep soaking tub\n\nseparate shower - replace \n\ndouble vanity - replace with floor mounted \n\nReplace the toilet \n\nWall tile wet area only \n\nreplace the floor tile \n\nno work on the window \n\nno work on the door\n\nreplace the mirror with the mirror \n\nreplace the light fixtures: one wall and one ceiling fixture \n\njets on the jacuzzi are leaking, no issues with the plumbing itself \n\nDesign:  modern style, grey and white  (do not want beige), chrome /brushed nickel fixtures \n\nwill potentially do two other bathrooms as well - depending on the price.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-20 19:43:36','2023-10-20 19:43:36'),(842,891,891,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12036403885',NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://streeteasy.com/property/1144690-102-west-75-street-24\n\nBathroom:\ninstall w/d \nremove the closet, replace with shelves \nconvert tub to a shower \nall new fixtures \nbase mounted fixtures \nreplace medicine cabinet with a larger medicine cabinet \nreplace wall tile in the wet area and the rest is wallpaper\nreplace floor tile \nreplace ceiling light fixture \nno work on the window\nno work on the door or trim \n\ndesign: neutral or grey/white, eclectic, a mixture of modern fixtures and something classic, clean and sleek \n\nkitchen:\nmake the kitchen open \nremove the closet and install peninsula with two bar stools \nmove the stove over to have a narrow cabinet between the stove an wall on the left side \nreplace all the appliances, \ninstall over the stove mw\nreplace cabinets \nno icemaker, reuse the fridge \nreplace floors with wood floors \nreplace ceiling fixture - with recessed lights \nadd under cabinet lights \nno door \nInstall pendant lights over the bar \n\ndesign: veiny white quartz, open to color for the cabinets, subway tile backsplash - sheen tile \n \nadd half bath: \nright off the kitchen \n\nCentral air - install \n\ngetting a quote for all windows - will be replaced',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-20 20:43:25','2023-10-20 20:43:25'),(843,892,892,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12014106767',NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://www.redfin.com/NJ/Weehawken/218-Maple-St-07086/home/36626112\n\ngut renovation of a three family home \neverything needs to be done - floors, kitchens, bathrooms\n\npartial floor plan attached, do not have measurements of the third floor.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-20 21:09:45','2023-10-20 21:09:45'),(844,893,893,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'194906323',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-24 13:29:13','2023-10-24 13:29:13'),(845,894,894,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13059720455',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-24 16:09:52','2023-10-24 16:09:52'),(846,895,895,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19176001092',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-24 23:40:06','2023-10-24 23:40:06'),(847,896,896,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11111111111',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are currently converting our garage into a fully functional gym and have already completed the initial rendering project. Now, we are in need of an experienced contractor team to bring our vision to life. \nThe services we require for this project are to put the Flooring, Windows, and Painting Walls. Additionally, there may be other specific needs that we\'ll discuss during the project consultation. We kindly request a quote for your services and a breakdown of the costs.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-25 14:11:47','2023-10-25 14:11:47'),(848,897,897,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16173199569',NULL,NULL,NULL,'hi i need kitchen bath reno, floors sanded, stained lighter, paint all room including closets, remove some wallpaper. kitchen frameless panel fridge and dishwasher i’ll get 24”fridge 18” dishwasher 24”gas range. large kitchen tiles or wood floor whichever better easier cheaper, bathroom looking for walk in shower if coop allows me to remove tub, if i have to keep tub then reno around it? need to get new toilet and floating vanity . remove laundry shoot.\n\nhttps://share.icloud.com/photos/092V5IU5wys5YeDBj595QOWNw',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-26 15:16:51','2023-10-26 15:16:51'),(849,898,898,NUL