ns, construction service\n\nsteam water pipes now, need to replace with HVAC. Allowed by the building - manager Hoffman (Gordon from 175 W 73 street, Erin and Kelsey)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-03 20:35:10','2023-11-03 20:35:10'),(856,905,905,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19173875171',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kitchen renovation \n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/property/1482795-311-east-71-street-8a\n\nCurrently has a gas slide in range. Replace with gas cooktop and install an oven across from it on the opposite wall\nMake stacked oven and built in microwave and wine fridge \ncounter microwave now - need to built in \nreplace the cabinets and appliances - panel ready \nreplace dw at current location \nReplace the sink with smaller deeper sink \nFloor tile - replace with tile \nreplace ceiling fixture \nadd under cabinet light \n install fridge with ice maker \nstone backsplash \n\nDesign: natural wood walnut color cabinets \nmid century modern style\nstone backsplash - light color quartz, maybe white with some veins/color',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-03 21:00:54','2023-11-03 21:00:54'),(857,906,906,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19292591272',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi - we would like to:\n- redo the kitchen including cabinets, backsplash, countertops, and island\n- add some built-ins to the living and dining rooms\n- redo closet doors\n- add one custom closet\n- redo entryway cabinetry\n- add pocket or french doors in between the living room and den, so that the space flows better\n- add carpet to kids room',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-05 20:30:25','2023-11-05 20:30:25'),(859,908,908,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19293175842',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I live in Jackson Heights and would appreciate an estimate for the following job if you are able to complete it by early to mid December:\n\n- Replace an in-wall shower in our second bathroom (i.e., remove tiles, replace existing shower, retile);\n- Install new wiring for a wall light in our ensuite bathroom (i.e., remove around 6 tiles, run new wires from the switch to the light, retile);\n- Replace four radiator boxes (remove existing boxes, build and install new ones);\n- Rehang a curtain rod.\n\nAccording to our co-op, we need a COI and a licensed plumber to do the work. In a second project, we might look at replacing the cabinets in the kitchen.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-07 04:06:43','2023-11-07 04:06:43'),(860,909,909,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13157061950',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We would like to replace the floor, renovate the kitchen (replacing the countertop, maybe cabinets, and maybe appliances). Maybe also bathroom',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-07 20:21:22','2023-11-07 20:21:22'),(861,910,910,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17921269235',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-07 21:33:01','2023-11-07 21:33:01'),(862,911,911,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12016063085',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Apparently my driveway is not up to code with the city of Bayonne and we\'re unable to park any vehicles because it does not meet the depth requirements of 16.5\' from structure to property line. \n\nI have no idea what this means and how to go about it. The city zoning officer, Tracey Tuohy, advised me to reach out to an architect, as she too, does not know how to guide me to come to compliance with the city codes.\n\nI wanted to reach out to you to see if you\'re able to help with drawing up a new driveway plan to meet their requirements (working with the City of Bayonne directly) and make it a reality so I can actually park my vehicles in my driveway.\n\nI\'ve attached a photo of the driveway. According to the city of Bayonne, it does not meet the driveway code requirement of 16.5\' depth in order to park vehicles. I\'ve parked two vehicles for over a year, only to learn this past month I\'m not legally able to.\n\nTracey Tuohy, the zoning officer of Bayonne City, advised to have an architect re-design my driveway so it\'s compliant with the City\'s code; section 35-17 of the city of Bayonne Zoning Ordinance. I\'ve screenshot and attached this too. She said if the city accepts the new re-design, then I can get the project started and use my driveway for parking.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-07 23:26:45','2023-11-07 23:26:45'),(863,912,912,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13473457299',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remodel kitchen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-07 23:29:44','2023-11-07 23:29:44'),(864,913,913,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15613033143',NULL,NULL,NULL,'REFERRAL  FROM SHARI MAURER - SISTER IN LAW. VIP\n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/lincoln-towers-150-west-end-avenue-new_york/21m\n\nApartment is for sale - need cost efficient design and scope of work. \nVery simple design to appeal to the most buyers. Everything white/neutral. \n\ngalley kitchen - full renovation \ndirect replacement of cabinets and appliances\nreuse fridge \nremove the door in the kitchen leading into the dining room (open doorway)\nFloor tile now, replace with tile \nreplace the light fixture \n\nguest bathroom off the hall - full remodel \nreplace wall tile, wet area only \nreplace floors \nreplace all fixtures \nReplace tub for tub \nReplace with curtain rod \nremove hamper \nneutral colors, all standard and base, no niche \n\nmaster bath \nreplace the floor - stained around the toilet (will check during the walkthrough if can polish or somehow fix instead)\nwhite tile \n\nreplace the floor in the living, dining, hallway - vinyl/engineered wood \n\nBedrooms have carpet, no work there. The unit has been painted already',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-08 19:23:40','2023-11-08 19:23:40'),(865,914,914,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14794618269',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It’s for a one bedroom coop on the UWS. I need the kitchen to be renovated with new appliances, need the floors to be polished and stained, and need a bathroom renovation as well.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-09 14:48:15','2023-11-09 14:48:15'),(866,916,916,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18287739377',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Construct hall wall partition and upgrade air treatment for IT room. Install elongated kitchen island, expand existing pantry by