,NULL,NULL,'18455961400',NULL,NULL,NULL,'bathroom remodel \nconvert tub to a shower \nPedestal sink replace with a vanity \nnew toilet \nWall tile Wet area only \nreplace the medicine cabinet\nbase mounted fixtures \nno window \nreplace the door and trim \nwall fixture replace \nregular shower, no handheld fixture \nno preferences for design\n\nkitchen \nReplace sink \nreplace ceiling light with the recessed lights',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-29 21:07:02','2023-11-29 21:07:02'),(875,925,925,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16462260230',NULL,NULL,NULL,'master bath \nreplace tub with walk in shower \nfull remodel \nwet area only \n\nbathroom by the entrance \nget new fixtures \npreserve the tile \nthe tub preserve \nchange shower fixture \nrepaint \n\nsecond bathroom \nleave the tub \nsame work as the second bath \n\n\nkitchen \ngut reno \nnew cabinets, appliances \ntile floor \n\nreplace all floors in the unit with the engineered wood \npaint all walls and ceilings \nreplace the ptec covers - 7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-11-29 22:08:34','2023-11-29 22:08:34'),(876,926,926,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17185932292',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One family home, need to take over the project halfway through the construction. Daniil spoje and scheduled, no additional details available',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-12-04 17:52:38','2023-12-04 17:52:38'),(877,927,927,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13477854898',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bathroom remodel \n\nreplace the tub with a new one \ncurtain rod \nreplace floor tile \nwall tile wet are and wall on the vanity floor to ceiling, other two walls is 4 ft up \nreplace vanity, medicine cabinet \nreuse the toilet \nreplace the window sill \nno work on the door \nwall light replace \n\nmodern design, has inspo. Wants bigger tiles',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-12-04 18:28:36','2023-12-04 18:28:36'),(878,928,928,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12016061911',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I\'m looking for interior work to be done on a basement apartment in a 6 unit residential property.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-12-04 18:32:01','2023-12-04 18:32:01'),(879,929,929,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19177718315',NULL,NULL,NULL,'kitchen full reno \n\nnew cabinets, new appliances \ncooktop and oven \n24 size appliances, already purchased the dw\n\nneeds to enlarge the kitchen - need to review the floorplan in person and advise\n\ndisability - may need ADA features in the future',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-12-04 20:43:04','2023-12-04 20:43:04'),(880,930,930,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19177169392',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello.  I’m looking for estimates for my duplex coop for restoration work in the first floor area and master bedroom after 3 water pipe bursts. We are hoping for mold remediation on 2 walls in the living room, a closet and 1 wall in the bedroom. Our engineered floors also suffered significant water damage as well. The first floor will need to be completely redone and we need to find a floor that resembles our original floor. The master bedroom, upstairs, has continuous floor throughout.  The water damaged walls and floors are on parallel sides of the room. Luckily we have 6 boxes in storage of the flooring. Each box claims to cover 35.5 sq ft. Our first floor is approximately 254 sq ft. Bedroom is approximately 192 sq ft. We reached out to the company that had sourced the floors for us originally. Unfortunately the floors are no longer in production. We were limited to our options for flooring 10 years ago due to time constraints and height issues with our new kitchen tile and fire safe door allowances. Very frustrating. \nWe were also hoping for a separate estimate for new stair treads. The company that had resurfaced the apartments original floors also messed up the landing treads. The treads are part of the original apartment and could use a replacing after a botched repair job. There are 14 treads total. They are pine stained to match though we are willing to explore options for these.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-12-06 15:33:16','2023-12-06 15:33:16'),(881,931,931,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16262783958',NULL,NULL,NULL,'put up temporary wall for 2nd bedroom in the dining area\n\nremove the pillars in the dining area (not load bearing) - this is where the temporary wall for the 2nd bedroom will go\n\nextend and open up the kitchen - add pantry to kitchen and a breakfast bar\n\nre-sand and varnish the flooring as needed (maybe just the bedroom?)\n\nreplace the bath with a standard tub (in ensuite bathroom)\n\nreplace the vanity fittings in the ensuite bathroom\n\nremove the wallpaper in the 2nd (half bathroom) and paint it\n\nturn walk-in closet (master bedroom) into a home office with sliding door to the foyer (see mock up on ppt)\n\nfit shelving in all of the closets',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-12-07 20:04:50','2023-12-07 20:04:50'),(882,932,932,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19176024514',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am reaching out because we recently had some work done on our garage, including putting up half a wall so the two doors no longer open to allow a car in. A DOB inspector came by to say that a neighbor called about a violation. We did not allow him in the house, but he told us we have two months to have an architect file with the DOB in order to avoid the violation. I am reaching out to see if anyone in your office handles such claims and how we might proceed.\n\n31-53 30th st. We didn\'t get the violation yet, just a warning. I\'m sending the survey of the house. Let me know if you need anything else. \nmy phone # 917 602 45 14',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-12-09 21:53:50','2023-12-09 21:53:50'),(883,933,933,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12023210180',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Small kitchen at south beach condo',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-12-11 16:10:15','2023-12-11 16:10:15'),(884,934,934,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14156277638',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Need to quickly freshen up master bathroom and 2 other small bathrooms. nothing super fancy since the apartment will go for a full remodeling in 2 years',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-12-11 20:49:33','2023-12-11 20:49:33'),(885,935,935,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'