ULL,NULL,NULL,'13475261923',NULL,NULL,NULL,'3 family house, coo is for  a 2 family (3 floors and a cellar)\nproperty taxes of 3 family \n\n2 violations - had a full bath \n1st floor - not supposed to be an apartment but is an apartment \n\n\n2017/2018 Alt 1 is submitted, rejected back then, then the architect had a stroke and died, no further development. \n\nhas a survey \nAlt 1 most likely - convert to a three family ideally \nright next to him are all three family houses',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-04 20:40:11','2024-01-04 20:40:11'),(902,952,952,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11914330572',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I would like to remodel my kitchen. I think it is a typical refresh of a small galley kitchen in a coop. New cabinets, new tiling, some new appliances, new lighting, etc.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-05 15:15:21','2024-01-05 15:15:21'),(903,953,953,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17324925654',NULL,NULL,NULL,'1 bedroom UES, full renovation \nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/308-east-79-street-new_york/2f\n\nentire unit: \nnew floors - hardwood, replace with 3 inch white oak, not engineered and not finished \nRefinish the walls, heavy prep or skim coat \nremove picture railing/crown molding throughout \nrefinish the doors and trims\nReplace radiator covers \nremove cedar closet - in the hall, replace walls and ceilings with drywall \n\n\nbathroom \nreplace tub with shower \nwet area + 50% wall tile \nreplace all fixtures \nInstall heated floors, remove the radiator \nwindow, trims and sills - no work \n\nKitchen \nInstall wood floor in the kitchen \nreplace all cabinets - has the person for it, do not calculate kitchen cabinet labor or decor\nreplace appliances \nwood floor \nno heated floors \nInstall banquette - radiator cover (like Violeta)\nwill do custom inset kitchen, no work only prep work in the kitchen \n\nDesign: \ntraditional style, no grey or modern pre-war, art deco, would like to keep the style, wood and earth tones',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-05 20:06:48','2024-01-05 20:06:48'),(904,954,954,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19546559618',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Master bath 90 sq ft \nfull remodel \nhas a jacuzzi, remove and install a walk in shower \ndouble vanity now, replace \ntoilets, medicine cabinets \nWall tile shower + 50% \nno heated floors, just tile replacement \nno window \nno doors, not needed \ninstall shower niche \nrecessed lights now, plus wall lights - only replace the wall lights \n\nDesign:\nroyal blue with gold accents - more modern larger tile on the floor\n\nhttps://www.realtor.com/realestateandhomes-detail/19134-NW-81st-Pl_Hialeah_FL_33015_M57866-89464',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-05 21:00:00','2024-01-05 21:00:00'),(905,955,955,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12027050804',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We require \"as built\" architectural renderings of our home, approximately 1600 sq ft, one-level home built in 1954. I tried to upload the Lot Boundary Survey, but I\'m not sure if it worked.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-06 16:52:11','2024-01-06 16:52:11'),(906,956,956,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12013208918',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Installation of built in cabinet lowers along both sides of the fireplace. Move or insulate the small radiators in place now.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-06 23:33:28','2024-01-06 23:33:28'),(907,957,957,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1564580486',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I would like to remodel my master bath.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-08 16:48:19','2024-01-08 16:48:19'),(908,958,958,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15164580486',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I would like to renovate my 8x5 master bath and 5x7 walk in closet. I need a new toilet bowl, sink and vanity and I would like to replace the existing bath tub with a walk in shower. I would also like to incorporate a steam shower and proper ventilation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-08 19:46:01','2024-01-08 19:46:01'),(909,959,959,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13367087777',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bathroom remodel:\nreplace wall tile wet area +50% \nReplace floor tile\nReglaze the tub \nReplace vanity and medicine cabinet\nReuse the toilet \nReplace ceiling fixture \nNo work on the window, maybe replace the sill \nNo work on the door or trim \n\nStyle classic New York, subway tile, black and white design \n\nHallway:\nPantry closet by the bathroom - install w/d \n\nReplace floor tile in the hallway to hardwood floors to match the rest of the unit, and a piece of the floors by the fridge (patch wood)\n\nCombine two entryway closets into one, replace closet organization \n\nMaster bedroom:\nRemove two bedroom closets \n\n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/509-east-77-street-new_york/1b',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-09 01:43:36','2024-01-09 01:43:36'),(910,960,960,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12032526914',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remodel laundry unit to allow for more modern finishing and coverage for upper half of entry way',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-09 22:02:33','2024-01-09 22:02:33'),(911,961,961,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16464752523',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi team – I saw your contact information on Yelp (phenomenal reviews!) We are doing some work on an apartment and are getting estimates from general contractors. I tried clicking on the schedule appointment link, but it didn’t work. There may be something wrong with my browser, hence I wanted to reach out via e-mail. \n\nHere are some details: \n\n1.	Location – Carnegie Hill (Lexington Avenue and East 93rd Street, right by 4-5-6 lines and the Q line)\n2.	Unit size – 2BD/2BA, approximately 1050 square feet. \n3.	Desired start date – very soon. End of next week would be ideal if doable. \n4.	Scope of work\na.	Floors – sanding, but no staining.\nb.	Walls – remove old wallpaper, then paint walls\nc.	Guest bathroom\ni.	Re-glaze bathtubs\nii.	Replace the old vanity\niii.	Potentially replace the floor tiling as well and the wall tiling\niv.	Fix or repair a leaking shower faucet\nv.	Replace the toilet\nvi.	Remove the rusty shower curtain hanger\nd.	Master bathroom – pretty much same thing as guest bathroom\ne.	Guest bedroom – get a door\nf.	Kitchen\ni.	Repair some cabinets if possible. If not, replace the cabinets and countertops. I don’t want anything expensive/customized. For example, something like quartz (in other words, something that looks like marble but is much cheaper and much easier to maintain) would be fine. For cabinets, I’m open to suggestions. Anything clean and easy to maintain. \nii.	Install a microwave\ng.	General\ni.	Remove some old wiring, shelves, electrical sockets that have been painted over, etc. \nii.	Install some GFCI outlets\niii.	Install a reverse-osmosis water filter under the sink\n\nWe are price-sensitive. I’m not looking for a complete luxury renovation. Just something reasonably decent. \n\nWould one of your team members be able to come over here some time this week to look at the unit?',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-09 23:58:30','2024-01-09 23:58:30'),(912,962,962,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14062062255',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi,\n\nLet us be your estimation partner. We provide estimation takeoff services. Do you have any projects for which you need estimation services or any questions regarding our services? Please feel free to reach out to us.\n\nIf you would like to review our past work, simply respond with \'Sample.\'\n\nLooking forward to working with you. Thanks!\n\nBest Regards,\n\nJos Buttler\nAll Star Estimation LLC\nEstimation and Takeoff Services',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-10 12:31:29','2024-01-10 12:31:29'),(913,963,963,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1979933905',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We would like to convert a detached garage in our backyard into an ADU.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-10 19:39:45','2024-01-10 19:39:45'),(914,964,964,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13473457299',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Renovate my coop',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-10 22:33:44','2024-01-10 22:33:44'),(915,965,965,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13059674267',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Full kitchen remodel \nreplace cabinets, appliances \nremove walls to make an open concept \nFloor tile replace, unsure with what yet \nReplace ceiling fixtures - not sure with what \n\nLiving room:\nremove the wall separating the living room from the den \nreplace the floors \npaint wall and ceiling',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-12 00:15:38','2024-01-12 00:15:38'),(916,966,966,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12128790597',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Redo Kitchen.  Minor update to bathroom (light, replace Medicine cabinet, vanity and shower door) pain.  Add a pantry.  Seal a walk through door.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-12 04:33:21','2024-01-12 04:33:21'),(917,967,967,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14754559064',NULL,NULL,NULL,'1) Replace flooring to wide plank natural wood coloured flooring (likely Engineering Wood, I have a dog)\n2) Paint upper kitchen cabinet to white and change to bronze/gold handles, and paint the lower kitchen cabinets and island to possibly this colour: https://www.benjaminmoore.com/en-us/paint-colors/color/776/santa-monica-blue\n3) Paint all the walls, doors, baseboards white\n4) Knock off the sliding door cabinets and the two side shelves\n5) Revamp walk in closet\n6) Revamp laundry closet\n7) Revamp reach-in closet\n8) Replace pendant lights in kitchen\n9) Replace washroom lighting\n10) Potentially paint window frames to black',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-15 18:32:32','2024-01-15 18:32:32'),(918,968,968,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17184507908',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bathroom upgrade, including:\n- some minor upgrades on tiles (some replacements and refreshing the grouts),\n- potentially creating floating shelves,\n- replacing the toilet with a new one\n- replacing what was potentially a laundry chute (maybe can be an extra storage space in the bathroom?)\n- potentially changing the faucet and shower head\n- etc.\n\nI want to keep the color scheme to light pink, black, white and gold (I don\'t have adding more, maybe like green). The style can be either coastal, mediterranean, tropical, or modern and contemporary vibe.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-15 21:50:09','2024-01-15 21:50:09'),(919,969,969,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13477686720',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Thank you for speaking and connecting us. We would like to move forward and get a bid from you as soon as possible. In the meantime, we are requesting access to the home for 1/19 or the following week, if possible, as we are near a close date. \n\nWould it be possible to receive a bid by the end of this week based on the review of the information attached? \n\nFor reference, I\'ve attached the following:\nPreliminary schematic pending additional adjustments with our architect\nCurrent as build (existing conditions) of the property\nInspection report\nInformation on the 203K Loan as a reference\nTi confirm our general contractor with our lender- you will need to provide our lender with the following information:\nContractor Bid\nHomestyle Contractor Approval \nA fully completed and executed profile confirming a minimum of 3 years in business.\nCompleted W9\nCopy of contractor license\nCertificate of Insurance showing valid/sufficient Commercial and Workman’s Comp coverage for the project. The certificate needs the holder to be listed as Annie Mac or the borrower with the property address.\nLead Renovator Certification',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-15 22:26:59','2024-01-15 22:26:59'),(920,970,970,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12125328932',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are looking to demolish a walll and repurpose a door',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-16 20:28:17','2024-01-16 20:28:17'),(921,971,971,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12125328932',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remove a wall and place a door',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-16 20:29:38','2024-01-16 20:29:38'),(922,972,972,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19177142675',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Finish the basement \n\nwaterproofing is done\n\nneed support beams, laundry, storage, bathroom, electrician',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-17 18:28:32','2024-01-17 18:28:32'),(923,973,973,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19999999999',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Test',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-17 18:59:59','2024-01-17 18:59:59'),(924,974,974,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17203558339',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Test lead Vicki Severson',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-17 19:26:01','2024-01-17 19:26:01'),(925,975,975,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14252330867',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Please see attached',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-18 19:42:36','2024-01-18 19:42:36'),(926,976,976,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13146146461',NULL,NULL,NULL,'buying co-op at 308 W 103rd st, with a 6\'10\" x 5\'5\" old kitchen. Need new oven/stove/cooktop, sink & Dishwasher. Keeping old refrigerator for now. Budget $10,000ish.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-19 19:45:59','2024-01-19 19:45:59'),(927,977,977,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16465802993',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello - I am looking for someone to start a small kitchen reno for me in the next week.\nhere is scope of work, please provide a price.\n\n1. Disconnect appliances including washer dryer; save\n\n2. Disconnect plumbing; remove existing sink, faucet, backsplash and counter; dispose\n\n3. Remove doors and panels; sand, prime and paint beige satin; Sand, prime and paint edge of cabinet boxes and fillers beige satin\n\n4.  Modify existing sink base cabinet to accept new fireclay  27\'\' farmhouse sink\n\n5. Install new farmhouse sink (Barclay Crofton Sink from Home Depot)\n\n6. Replace existing over the door silver pulls with new over the door brass pulls\n\n7. Provide, fabricate and install new MSI Calcutta Leon Gold quartz countertop slab\n\n8.  Install new backsplash (Kingston3x8 white ceramic tile from Home Depot)\n\n9. Install new faucet (Brizo Rook Articulating Bridge Faucet)\n\n10. Re-install appliances\n\nOwner will provide - sink, faucet, backsplash tiles, cabinet door pulls unless contractor can get better price\n\nContractor will provide - MSI Calacutta Leon Gold slab',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-21 16:03:35','2024-01-21 16:03:35'),(928,978,978,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11347249073',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I’d like to deglaze the bathroom floor and wall tiles as well as the bathtub and replace the toilets, sinks, and vanities.  I’d like to replace the floors in the living and dining rooms with engineered wood and refinish the floors in the rest of the apartment that seem to be in better shape. Kitchen to add floor and wall tiles, new cabinets as well as appliances. Pantry to add new cabinets as well as to install a new stacked washer and dryer.  Through out the apartment I’d like to skim coat the walls and repaint, update the light fixtures, install curtain roses for the windows, add electrical outlets in every room (pre war building so there are very few).',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-21 17:33:03','2024-01-21 17:33:03'),(929,979,979,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19177249757',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am about to close on an apartment in the West Village next week that\'s in need of a gut reno. Attached is a very thorough outline of what I\'m looking to do. I\'m not sure whether I am going to do the bathroom just yet, so for now the scope of work with exclude that.\n\nPlease have a look through and if you could provide me with a rough estimate for labor excluding finishes (i.e. cabinets, appliances, countertops) that would be much appreciated.\n\nI do see that you had some prefabricated packages that have a short lead time. Please refer to my design references and let me know if you have a similar cabinet option. If not, I am happy to source myself.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-22 16:42:32','2024-01-22 16:42:32'),(930,980,980,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13476620835',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am seeking to obtain a certificate of occupancy for a mixed use property. The Dept of Dob have a 3 family and commercial. Currently the property is 2 family and 1 commercial. I need a Certificate of occupancy to reflect the new layout for the first floor. \nThe applicant  has the plans from the letter of no object that was denied for not having a CO. Can we use those plans ? Yes the two family is the second and third floor. The first floor was a commercial and residential. Now it\'s just a commercial.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-23 14:19:07','2024-01-23 14:19:07'),(931,981,981,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16464507443',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello-- I have a small kitchen in a one-bedroom apartment and need a new cabinets, sink, counter top and flooring. Will save the newer appliances. The unit is in the upper east side in Manhattan in a Condop. The building requires architectural design, review and approval, as well as a licensed/insured contractor.\n\nRami would like a clean simple modern design with light colors (white-gray...light)\nWould like  a \"man-made\" countertop option with modern look in addition to the backsplash and tile flooring.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-23 20:07:15','2024-01-23 20:07:15'),(932,982,982,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19178341556',NULL,NULL,NULL,'standard 3 piece bathroom in Queens, Bayside. Should be around 5 x 8 \n\nconvert the tub to a shower\nInstall glass door \nInstall niche \nreplace all fixtures, vanity and toilet \nmirror now replace with a medicine cabinet \nWet area only for the wall tile \nreplace the floor tile \nwindow, no work\nreplace the door and trim \nfloor mounted fixtures are fine \n\ndesigner suggested, no ideas for design',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-25 20:17:39','2024-01-25 20:17:39'),(933,983,983,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18458567014',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-25 20:34:27','2024-01-25 20:34:27'),(934,984,984,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16623035935',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-28 05:41:10','2024-01-28 05:41:10'),(935,985,985,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17407169748',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-28 13:51:07','2024-01-28 13:51:07'),(936,986,986,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12283659154',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-28 21:15:28','2024-01-28 21:15:28'),(937,987,987,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18566934037',NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1W_i2L1ZUKgwtq1bkl3DED-k-F8u6mP7d\n\nHere is a folder with our current floor plan, proposed new floor plan, scope of work, condo alteration agreement and photos/video of our unit. \n\nWe are working with an architect who will be assisting with the renovation process and DOB filing as well.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-29 14:07:13','2024-01-29 14:07:13'),(938,988,988,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12512200484',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Renovate studio apartment. Renovate Kitchen, bath, living area.\nRemove one small partition wall. Electrical upgrade.  May want to put laminate tile over hardwood flooring.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-29 18:27:13','2024-01-29 18:27:13'),(939,989,989,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15514868017',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We have a 2 family 6 over  6 rooms home in the jersey city heights\n\nWe plan to remodel both bathrooms (2nd and 3rd floors) as follows\n\n1. Remove both tubs\n\n2. Remove all existing wet area tile and remediate pipes and drains as needed\n\n3. Install new tile  shower pans over remediated subfloors and install full size walk in showers\n\n4. Retile wet areas and install new faucets and elder safety elements\n\n5. Install full size sliding glass doors \n\n6. Both toilets, vanities and existing flooor tile to remain in place\n\nWork should include all permits demolition and debris removal and be completed as one project beginning mid July 2024\n\nNo financing needed and no prefab kits wanted',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-31 15:39:25','2024-01-31 15:39:25'),(940,990,990,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15514868017',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-31 15:40:53','2024-01-31 15:40:53'),(941,991,991,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19088381039',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Small kitchen remodeling on a budget. Need to add a small combo washer/dryer unit near the sink. I do not mind having a smaller sink and/or gas stove. \nIdeally, would like to change all the cabinets and have marble countertops and backsplash. Thanks for your help!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-02-01 01:21:50','2024-02-01 01:21:50'),(942,992,992,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16306986360',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-02-03 04:58:58','2024-02-03 04:58:58'),(943,993,993,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19174564601',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We would like to get the entire place done. I am looking for a designer and contractor who could help optimize function/storage while creating a minimal/Japandi like space.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-02-04 02:24:00','2024-02-04 02:24:00'),(944,994,994,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16466207097',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Looking at a wall between a living room and bedroom to see if structurally it can be taken down.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-02-04 21:34:30','2024-02-04 21:34:30'),(945,995,995,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18453212864',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-02-05 06:01:01','2024-02-05 06:01:01'),(946,996,996,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12134535166',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Single family zoned, wants to add an additional floor and to convert to a 2 family home.  This property needs a complete renovation  from basement up. \n\n*There are no floor plans of this property but will send  pics and most recent appraisal to Maria',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-02-05 19:56:58','2024-02-05 19:56:58'),(947,997,997,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19178161340',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Has accepted offer, possible access to schedule with an agent\n\nkitchen renovation project \nwall needs to be removed - remove the full corner between the hallway and dining area. \nPropose a new layout for the kitchen to maximize space, build an island \nReplace all fixtures: new countertops, appliances, cabinets, wood floors \nreuse the w/d \nReplace with wood floor \nno ceiling work or light work \nNo under cabinet light or concealed appliances\n\nDesign: natural wood, white cabinets, simple but intricate tile backsplash \n\n250 w 94 street apt 13G \nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/the-stanton-250-west-94-street-new_york/13g',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-02-05 21:25:01','2024-02-05 21:25:01'),(948,998,998,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15617859978',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I’m touching base to seek for your professional service, we was working with a contractor last year and our project was schedule to be finalized by October 2024 as it’s a big project, unfortunately the contractor didn’t make it to 2024, we are s