sher and electric dryer closer to the backyard to install a vent and 220V outlet because the vent from the front of the house is too far. There may be other needs, but these are our current requests pending your feedback from the onsite consultation.  We\'ll be at the venue on 3/7 and 3/12 before 1 pm.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-06 23:20:35','2024-03-06 23:20:35'),(1004,1054,1054,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17868032429',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remodeling kitchen\nRemodeling bath 2 half / 2 full baths\nFlooring \nDoor \nClosets',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-07 17:19:57','2024-03-07 17:19:57'),(1005,1055,1055,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1732043772',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Fully remodeling a small (30 sq ft) bathroom. Changing the tiling on the floor and walls, new toilet and sink (in the same location, so pipes won\'t need to be moved), more/new cabinets on the walls',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-09 02:45:52','2024-03-09 02:45:52'),(1006,1056,1056,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19298107621',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I have a co-op apartment in Washington Heights, Manhattan that I\'m looking to construct a new bedroom out of the living room. We have architect\'s drawings already and the architect will file for NYC DOB Alt-2 permit. Please see attachment for the drawings. \n\nWe will need the contractor to be licensed with the City of New York to be able to pull that permit.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-09 19:50:38','2024-03-09 19:50:38'),(1007,1057,1057,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19199225751',NULL,NULL,NULL,'kitchen,4 bathrooms\nDesign',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-10 00:38:39','2024-03-10 00:38:39'),(1008,1058,1058,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17738790488',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-10 06:42:56','2024-03-10 06:42:56'),(1009,1059,1059,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14042970975',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-10 19:48:17','2024-03-10 19:48:17'),(1010,1060,1060,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17014215177',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-11 01:36:49','2024-03-11 01:36:49'),(1011,1061,1061,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19175022849',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Looking to remodel 3 bedroom and 1.5 bathroom co-op apartment unit. Want to redo floors, the bathrooms and trims/paint. Depending on costs, we would also like to redo the whole kitchen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-11 16:36:30','2024-03-11 16:36:30'),(1012,1062,1062,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16098029025',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bathroom remodel \n\nConvert tub to a shower. May reuse all other fixtures, needs as cheap as possible\n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/30-west-60-street-new_york/3u',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-12 15:42:49','2024-03-12 15:42:49'),(1013,1063,1063,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17182882033',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kitchen remodel \n\nkitchen 10 by 7 \nreplace the cabinets, backsplash and floor \ntile floor, replace with new tile\nreuse current appliances, has dishwasher \nquartz backsplash and countertop \nadd garbage pull out can or next to the kitchen\n\nno preference for design yet \n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/361-86-street-brooklyn/9 - maybe similar size and layout, she said L shaped kitchen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-12 18:38:59','2024-03-12 18:38:59'),(1014,1064,1064,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19048590246',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Redo the bathroom floors (1.5 bathrooms)\nRestructure Existing Walls/ Put in New Walls to Create Additional Bedroom',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-13 19:55:05','2024-03-13 19:55:05'),(1015,1065,1065,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19176864076',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Full bathroom remodel \n\nreplace all fixtures \nreuse toilet \nHas a shower with the curtain rod replace to a new tub with a curtain rod \nWall tiles all walls floor to ceiling \n\nHad a major leak, the bathroom has not been used in over three months \n\nDesign: all white tile',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-14 17:42:07','2024-03-14 17:42:07'),(1016,1066,1066,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13472626211',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi! \n\nPlease see the attached renovation list and floor plan. Would love to connect to discuss project and get an estimate. \n\nThanks,\nElizabeth',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-15 22:12:03','2024-03-15 22:12:03'),(1017,1067,1067,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11917288948',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Gut renovation on a 1-bedroom pre-war apartment (~950 SF) in downtown Manhattan. Project to include:\n1) demolition of 2 interior walls to open up the kitchen;\n2) demolition of an additional interior wall to open up the living space to the kitchen;\n3) full remodel of kitchen including addition of either an island or a peninsula to create a U-shaped open kitchen;\n4) full remodel of bathroom (remove tub and replace with walk-in shower) and combining the closet next to the bathroom to the bathroom footprint (including relocating the vanity to that area);\n5) sound-proofing the interior wall separating the bedroom and living space;\n6) remove exisiting parquet floor and replace with new flooring and 2 or 2.5\" flat baseboards;\n7) raising the ceiling from current height of 9\" to 11\";\n8) install new light points -- possibly need to update the electric panel -- as well as replacement of some of the current light fixtures;\n9) new closet doors;\n10) adding additional storage above the existing closets;\n11) cabinet covers for existing heating and incorporate solution for in-window air conditioners.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-16 22:13:14','2024-03-16 22:13:14'),(1018,1068,1068,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19174850350',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Commercial remodeling - referral from OS studios and Bobby\'s Night Out\n\ninstagrammable bar - working on the theme, need ideas for the concept  \n\nhas a location 1500 sq ft - negotiating the contract\nbrand new building, landlord may pay for some work\n\nno HVAC, no wiring or plumbing yet, everything needs to be done \nnot enough storage, need to create storage\n\nairfryer, microwave - not a full kitchen \nmostly bar and seating \n\n4 partners total, 3 are active - will need to agree on the design concept, price, etc',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-17 13:59:39','2024-03-17 13:59:39'),(1019,1069,1069,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19177535372',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Currently has a 2 bed /1 bath two story house\nflat roof, has 5.2\" crawl space. \n\nLooking to add an extra floor consisting of 2 bathrooms and 4 bedrooms.\n\nNeeds a quote for survey, architectural services, and construction afterwards',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-18 15:24:22','2024-03-18 15:24:22'),(1020,1070,1070,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19732143513',NULL,NULL,NULL,'See scope attached',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-18 18:51:29','2024-03-18 18:51:29'),(1021,1071,1071,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19178461622',NULL,NULL,NULL,'gut renovation of the unit. currently in contract \n\nhttps://www.realtor.com/realestateandhomes-detail/2335-Bell-Blvd-Apt-3F_Bayside_NY_11360_M99201-96299',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-20 16:03:45','2024-03-20 16:03:45'),(1022,1072,1072,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15078847057',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Master bathroom remodel',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-20 22:05:20','2024-03-20 22:05:20'),(1023,1073,1073,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15166752782',NULL,NULL,NULL,'full kitchen remodel \n\nCurrently U shaped, closed off\nOpen up towards the living room, install an island\nReplace all appliances \nReplace cabinets \nReplace countertop, stone backsplash \nAdd under cabinet lights \nReplace ceiling fixture \nAdd pendant lights \nReplace tile floor for tile floor \n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/the-veneto/702',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-21 13:55:58','2024-03-21 13:55:58'),(1024,1074,1074,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17322611299',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are interested in a single family home in Flatbush, 138 E 29th St. If you look up the listing, you\'ll get an idea of what we want done: mainly new hardwood floors throughout, also new stairs (both to the basement and to the second floor); potentially some work needed on the exterior as well.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-22 14:38:46','2024-03-22 14:38:46'),(1025,1075,1075,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15165260475',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I want to install new closet doors in my bedroom. I recently had new floors put in, and the contractors broke the previous doors. \n\nI also would like to move a closet in my second bedroom to a different location. For the second bedroom closet relocation, no walls will need to be moved. Please see attached diagram for additional context. \n\nThat said, if this is not within the scope of the work your firm does, I would greatly appreciate any recommendations to contractors who can work on this project. Thank you!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-22 22:46:35','2024-03-22 22:46:35'),(1026,1076,1076,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13023199439',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi ,\n\nHope you\'re doing well!\n\nAs a general contractor, ensuring your project is on time and within budget is key. That\'s where we come in. Our seasoned professionals leverage cutting-edge technology and industry-standard software to deliver precise estimates and takeoffs promptly.\n\nTo provide you with the best service, we need detailed project drawings/plans. If you already have them, fantastic! If not, we\'re happy to assist in creating tailored plans for our estimation and takeoff services.\n\nOur comprehensive approach aims to streamline estimates, cut costs, and ensure top-notch project completion.\n\nGot questions or need to discuss further? We\'re here for you.\n\nLooking forward to collaborating on your next project.\n\n\nBest regards,\nJames Cook\nMarketing Executive\nProfine Estimating',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-26 07:18:11','2024-03-26 07:18:11'),(1027,1077,1077,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12013037616',NULL,NULL,NULL,'3000 Sq feet store front ground floor (rectangle area) that has exposed pipe under the ceiling of already built commercial residential building. We are renting the space for convenient store/ grocery store front and want to hide those exposed pipes with drop ceiling. It doesn\'t have to be fancy, just basic tiles to hide pipes. Please include labor and material in estimates.\n\nWants commercial ceiling tiles with 2x4 lights. Provide a full estimate with labor and decor so he can present to the owner to cover the costs. Once the contract is signed, can do a walkthrough.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-26 15:30:39','2024-03-26 15:30:39'),(1028,1078,1078,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19172387117',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello, I am looking to completely renovate an existing single story ranch style house located at 1919 West 3rd Street in Brooklyn. I would like to extend the front portion of the existing structure and add a second floor with attic space. The zoning is r4a and will remain a single family home. I am still in the infancy stage of shopping around. I will need an architectural survey, architect, and GC for the entire project.\n\nI want to confirm the sprinkler system is not required. I want to bump the current porch so the front is squared off. I also want to square off the back of the house. \nAdd second floor to match the first level and have attic space. \n\nSurvey us completed, need an architect and GC',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-26 20:32:23','2024-03-26 20:32:23'),(1029,1079,1079,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19174559130',NULL,NULL,NULL,'house in queens 1940s built. part of the property is on city land. stayed in the family from her mother, will be building within her property lines.\nhas the survey - will email \n\ntree was removed - part of the fence came down, ground is not leveled \nInstall a cement wall instead of the fence \nInstall driveway all the way, cemented \nBuild a room 18 by 22 - for physical therapy - either an extension of the house or a separate building with three walls and one glass wall facing the the yard, separate entrance',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-29 13:23:58','2024-03-29 13:23:58'),(1030,1080,1080,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18606818666',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Basement full remodel \n\nthe floor needs to be leveled, has linoleum now in patches. Replace with the floor tile \nceiling and walls full drywall replacement, paint \n3 ceiling light fixtures replace with recessed lights \nthere is a temp wall, want to remove it\nInstall a pantry closet under the stairs (has a small closet currently, want to enlarge)\n\nbathroom \ntoilet and a shower in one room, sink outside of the bath - combine in one room\nreplace shower with tub \nreplace vanity, \nreuse toilet replace \nReplace the floor tile, \nInstall fiberglass tub (no tile on the walls)\nexhaust fan with built in fixture, replace with recessed lights \nnothing in terms of style, very basic and neutral',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-03-30 17:51:09','2024-03-30 17:51:09'),(1031,1081,1081,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13019808481',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I have water damage to the ceiling of my second bedroom',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-01 15:56:35','2024-04-01 15:56:35'),(1032,1082,1082,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13475937046',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Full gut - kitchen, bathrooms, electric, plumbing. Floor and doors might be salvaged.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-01 22:24:18','2024-04-01 22:24:18'),(1033,1083,1083,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19176967150',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Full apartment renovation \n\nplaster walls, refinish and paint \nparquet floors, refinish or replace, preferably refinish. has some gaps. most likely has asbestos - need to test \nreplace all light fixtures with recessed lights \n\nremove the living room closets to make the living space open, possibly relocate closets  \n\nfull bathroom renovation\nreplace all fixtures \n\nfull kitchen renovation\nremove part of the wall in the kitchen toward the floors \nreplace gas with induction stove \nreplace all appliances and cabinets \nwood floors (linoleum now)\n\nsecond bedroom \nneed to move the closet towards the bedroom and turn into the linen closet\n\nnot a high end, medium quality \nbasic finish GE type appliances \n\ndesign: simple, neutral, modern style, muted tones, but not too sanitary',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-04 12:43:27','2024-04-04 12:43:27'),(1034,1084,1084,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16073161585',NULL,NULL,NULL,'kitchen \nreplace the countertops with light color quartz\nadd backsplash stone \nremove wall cabinets on the island side \nreplace the rest of the cabinets \nreplace the floors with wood \nwant the regular island (straight with no breakfast bar)\n\n\nbathroom - partial \nreplace vanity, toilet \nreglaze the tub \nreplace mirror with a standard size mirror and do shelves above the toilet \n\nEntire unit: \nreplace the floors \npaint wall and ceilings \n\nmodern look, black hardware skinny long handles \n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/1760-2-avenue-new_york/15a',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-04 14:27:25','2024-04-04 14:27:25'),(1035,1085,1085,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19172261980',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Removal of kitchen cabinets and linoleum down to the subflooring. The kitchen measures 7\' x 8\' 4\". The building was built in 1958 and has the original metal cabinets and flooring in place. There are actually 2 layers of flooring which need removal.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-05 03:19:27','2024-04-05 03:19:27'),(1036,1086,1086,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16466923328',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am looking to instal a custom extension to my existing concrete bar to provide bar seating.\nI already have some drawings of the project and would like to schedule a visit with you to start a scope of work,\nPlease contact me by phone or email\n\nBest\n\nBenoit Amsler',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-08 18:27:21','2024-04-08 18:27:21'),(1037,1087,1087,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19172707733',NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://www.compass.com/listing/25-burns-street-unit-5c-forest-hills-ny-11375/1459598033771462289/\n\ncrown moldings \nnew radiator covers \nreplace outlet covers and switches \n\nbathroom\nreplace the tub for a shower \nreplace all fixtures \nreplace wall tile shower and 50% \nreplace floor tile\nrefinish window trim and sill \nrefinish door and trim\nreplace ceiling light fixtures \ndesign: modern looking, larger tiles, neutral colors, off white, maybe blue, polished \n\nkitchen \nreplace cabinetry and appliances \nreplace the floor tile for tile \nreplace the countertop and backsplash with stone \n\nhallway closet combine the closets and replace the doors',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-08 20:11:59','2024-04-08 20:11:59'),(1038,1088,1088,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19178607707',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi, I am a potential investor and would be interested to know how much it will cost to completely remodel two floors. Each floor has two bedrooms and a bathroom. The property is located in Union city NJ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-08 22:41:54','2024-04-08 22:41:54'),(1039,1089,1089,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17862418471',NULL,NULL,NULL,'see plans attached',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-09 13:08:14','2024-04-09 13:08:14'),(1040,1090,1090,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13474909587',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I need to remodel my kitchen it\'s very dated, I would like to change the layout. There is a gas stove and the sink has a garbage dispposal',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-11 15:14:41','2024-04-11 15:14:41'),(1041,1091,1091,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16465914670',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello, I\'m looking to start a 2 story addition on an existing 1 level/1 family home.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-12 20:51:29','2024-04-12 20:51:29'),(1042,1092,1092,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19173996956',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Good morning. I was referred to you by Orsid, my building\'s management company. Seeking an estimate. Job includes electrical, plumbing, and carpentry punchlist.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-15 13:39:45','2024-04-15 13:39:45'),(1043,1093,1093,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19172707293',NULL,NULL,NULL,'private house, queens. Forest hills gardens - private managed comminity \ncannot replace the vent plumbing is old \n\none bathroom - second floor \nbad ventilation, cannot put a new vent due to the building\nconvert from tub to shower \nno glass door, \nshower install grab bar \nreplace all fixtures \nmedicine cabinet replace with a flat mirror \nreplace the wall light \nInstall recessed light in the shower \ninstall a wall mounted toilet \ninstall shower niches \nreplace the window, trim and sill \nmove the shower fixtures around, all to one wall instead of different walls \n\ndesign: less grout lines, large format tiles, more classic and contemporary since the house is old. Different color combinations, mostly off white , beige, warm. This bathroom gets a lot of sun light, maybe something mother of pearl so it reflects the light \n\nsecond bathroom - third floor \nreplace tub for tub, lower profile \nshower curtain\nreplace fixtures \nwall mounted toilet \nhas a skylight window, replace \nWall tile wet zone only \nhas a lot of pipes - questions about the layout \ndesign: not sure if she wants the same or different design, large format tiles. Possible for blue colors',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-15 14:30:13','2024-04-15 14:30:13'),(1044,1094,1094,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18622522158',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Redo the basement to make it a standalone rental unit; convert the top three floors into a single family. Add a deck, and extend the kitchen out',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-16 16:07:29','2024-04-16 16:07:29'),(1045,1095,1095,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19173401605',NULL,NULL,NULL,'First time home buyer - looking to make an offer for the property\n(search criteria: 1 bed coop, UWS, UES, Midtown) \n\n1960s building, needs gut reno.  750 sq ft\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/525-east-86-street-new_york/1b\n\nEntire apartment: \nPaint all walls and ceilings, door trims, window trims and sills \nreplace the doors \nreplace closet organization \nreplace flooring with engineered wood, replace baseboards\nupgrade electrical, replace outlets where needed\n\nLiving room \ninstall recessed lights \n\nHallway\nRemove the wall between the dining room and hallway\nRearrange the closets in the hallway and bedroom, see proposed floor plan \n\n\nkitchen - full renovation \nremove the wall between the kitchen and living room, make open kitchen\ninstall the peninsula \nreplace all cabinets and appliances\nreplace floors with engineered wood \nInstall pendant lights over the island or possibly recessed lights \n\n\nbathroom - full remodel \nExpand the bathroom, see proposed floor plan \nreplace tub for a shower \nwall tile floor to ceiling \ninstall double vanity \nrelocate the toilet \nreplace all fixtures \ninstall recessed lights \nfloor mounted vanity and toilet \n\nhave a good sense for the design concept - will send references \n\n\nWalkthrough to be scheduled for May 1-3, they are on vacation prior to that',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-17 15:35:20','2024-04-17 15:35:20'),(1046,1096,1096,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17325436239',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are looking to upgrade our electrical equipment, and Con Ed said that the wall with the meters, which happens to be creating a boiler room, needs to be moved back 3 feet. Because of this, we will also need a grill installed in the foundation for ventilation.\nSo demo of the wall, a new wall, up to plumbing code as far as fireproof, etc. \n\nI also have a foundation issue in the cellar door, do you work on that?',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-17 16:01:06','2024-04-17 16:01:06'),(1047,1097,1097,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19176978676',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am looking for a contractor to perform some work at a co-op in Queens Village. It includes a wall being removed in the dining room/kitchen area- kitchen renovation as well & washer dryer install where the wall used to be. Bathroom installed into closet space on the first floor. Closet removed in a room on the second floor. Attic access being relocated from one room to the next as well as the orientation of the opening being change. Bathroom renovation. As well as a few other items. An architect has already drawn, submitted, and had these plans approved. Let me know if this is something you\'d be interested working on at your earliest convenience. EPA lead-based certification is a must from the co-op',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-17 21:34:57','2024-04-17 21:34:57'),(1048,1098,1098,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19177490631',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Two bathroom master bath and guest bath that need to be remodeled. The master bath the tub needs to be switched out for a standing shower, the tiles need to be replaced and a radiator needs to be moved as well. \n  The guest bathroom she needs tiles replaced and and sink and fixtures replaced',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-17 22:22:43','2024-04-17 22:22:43'),(1049,1099,1099,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17138182642',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We just purchased a 450 sqft condo that was partially renovated as part of the contract. The kitchen and floors are brand new and lovely. The main things that are left to renovated are: \n1. The walls - these are in poor shape and likely need to be sanded down before they can be re-painted. \n2. Removal of certain parts of walls - we have strange corners and juts that are anywhere from 3-6 inches in length and span from floor to ceiling. We would like to remove these to make the space feel bigger. This is the bulk of what we are looking to have done. \n3. Addition of walls to create a small home office - extending an existing closet by 2-3 feet will accomplish this. \n4. Addition of walls to create a bedroom - we are planning on installing an Ikea PAX closet system and want to understand how the walls need to be configured to best accommodate the length and width of the closet.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-18 15:11:03','2024-04-18 15:11:03'),(1050,1100,1100,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12819104512',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Houzz lead, Anna spoke on the phone: \n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/405-west-48-street-new_york/1fe\n\nKitchen - full remodel\nreplace the cabinets \nreplace the appliances (dw now, install a drawer style mw, replace the hood with a vent towards the window, replace with regular gas range) wolf and subzero panel ready appliances \n\nfloors are wood, continuous throughout the unit, no work\nreplace the light (it\'s above the cabinets), open to recessed lights \ninstall under cabinet lights \nreplace the backsplash with tile\nreplace countertop \ncover the window and put the cabinets \n\ndesign: more timeless and classic than modern, lighter colors, natural wood but to not look like wood, much lighter off white wood. Could be a shaker, unsure yet, panel ready appliances\n\nStart of the project after the summer \nDays off on  wednesday and thursday - contact then for a quicker response',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-19 19:40:59','2024-04-19 19:40:59'),(1051,1101,1101,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16467757368',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Anna spoke via email, awaiting a call to discuss the scope \n\nSee attached drawings',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-19 21:12:31','2024-04-19 21:12:31'),(1052,1102,1102,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13475249072',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2BD Coop apartment - Renovation thoughts/requests\nnotes here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rM3Afpn84rC-7XK-ls5qL4oCTYwtw8GIxtSFfp0Fb9w/edit?usp=sharing\n\nKitchen Needs\nTop Priority\nMore counter space! Currently I have 25-26” of work space, would like to have 40 minimum\nSpace for bulk items in glass jars\nCookbook space\nSlide out pantry\nReducing hard-to-reach dead space\nEfficient storage for pots/pans\nUtensil storage not right in front of work space\nImprove lighting\nCheck possibility of re-opening kitchen vent and how to filter/fan/kitchen exhaust\nExtend opening/window between kitchen and living room\n\nWould like to discuss, but not 100% necessary\nWould like to explore induction cooking to see if possible\nSmall built-in desk/work space?\nBetter storage for wine/sparkling water\n\nBathroom needs\nTop Priority\nReplace spa tub with regular tub/shower\nAdd electrical outlet\nTile that is easy to clean and doesn’t show brown minerals in water\nKeep linen/bath closet space - add organization?\nAdd shower surround (glass doors, but modern)\nTowel space for 4\n\nWould like but not 100% necessary\nLinen closet organization\nLevel bathroom floor - right now it is very uneven\nImprovements to ½ bath in main bedroom - current tile\nBedrooms\nTop Priority\nAdd closet to girls bedroom by taking space from larger bedroom\nAdd built-in clothing storage (hanging and shelves/drawers) to both bedrooms\nReplace lighting/fan in kids bedroom with LED energy efficient\n\nWould like but not 100% necessary\nAdd ceiling pendant to main bedroom and/or bedside lighting\n\n\nThroughout\nTop Priority\nClassic modern aesthetic - in keeping with age of building - not trendy or easily dated\nFix peeling ceilings\nRefinish floors and repair damage, if possible, rather than replacing\nBetter/energy efficient lighting (keeping integrated LED fixture above dining table)\n\nWould like, but not 100% necessary\nSkim coat and paint walls\nBetter closet organization\nMore bookshelf space in living room (built-in shelves on ½ wall facing kitchen?)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-21 16:31:23','2024-04-21 16:31:23'),(1053,1103,1103,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1456041058',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi,\n\nWe are an Architectural / Estimation company. We provide these services to different General Contractors, Sub-Contractors, Home Builders and Specialty Contractors.\n\nPlease send over the project details if you are interested and mention the exact scope of work for the quote on our services charges. You will surely find our prices and work exceptionally outstanding.\n\nYou may ask for the samples of our previous work which we did recently. Thanks.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-22 14:04:16','2024-04-22 14:04:16'),(1054,1104,1104,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14127191282',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client needs Arch that separates the living room and the kitchen demolished needs that space painted as well as the ceilings in both rooms kitchen and living room',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-22 14:10:59','2024-04-22 14:10:59'),(1055,1105,1105,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16465914670',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Looking to add add an addition to an existing 1 level family home, but also includes gutting , but also includes gutting the existing floor. Plans were submitted and approved by DOB about 9 years ago, looking to get an estimate and move forward with project',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-22 19:06:14','2024-04-22 19:06:14'),(1056,1106,1106,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13476243162',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client needs tub replaced or refinished, medicine cabinet and mirror need to be replaced, new tiles on wall the toilet does not have to be replaced as she recently got it installed the hallway needs to be repainted and the living room repainted and replastered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-23 19:42:52','2024-04-23 19:42:52'),(1057,1107,1107,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16467346452',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I have a 600 sf studio in the Parc Vendome at 56th and 9th.  Generally I am pleased with the apartment but feel it could be made more comfortable and appealing.  Ideally I would like options, eg, what I can do with a $5k budget, 10k budget, 15k budget, etc.  Would you be able to help with this.  Photos attached.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-26 14:27:50','2024-04-26 14:27:50'),(1058,1108,1108,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17182192579',NULL,NULL,NULL,'semi detached house in queens \nLooking to add an extra bedroom and bathroom. \n\nOption 1: \nmiddle bedroom 10 x 10 - convert into a bathroom (2 floor), there is another bathroom on that floor, close but not adjacent \nAdd an extension on the second floor to keep 3 bedrooms \n\nOption 2: \nAdd an extension to the back of the house on the first floor to build a bedroom and the bathroom there (no bathroom there now, just the kitchen) . Second floor will remain as is. \n\nWe are the first contractor she is speaking to, needs a quote for a survey first',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-26 20:22:57','2024-04-26 20:22:57'),(1059,1109,1109,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13478668233',NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://streeteasy.com/building/the-oxford-422-east-72-street-new_york/36a\n\nmaster bathroom 9x6 plus shower 3x3 \nreglaze the jacuzzi tub \nreplace the shower, new door \nreplace the floor tile \nreplace all fixtures \nwall tile 50% \nreplace wall light fixture \nrefinish the window sill and trim \nno work on the door or trim \n\nDesign: more contemporary and modern, more clean, but not all white, no subway tiles. beige, grey, silver, or light blue neutral tones. Maybe one accent\n\n\nguest bathroom 9x6\nreglaze the tub \nwall tile only in the wet area \nreplace all fixtures\nno work on the door or trim \nno work on the window \ncurtain rod is fine \n\nDesign: more contemporary and modern, more clean, but not all white, no subway tiles. beige, grey, silver, or light blue neutral tones. Maybe one accent. Cohesive design with the master bathroom',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-26 20:59:39','2024-04-26 20:59:39'),(1060,1110,1110,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17029070062',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am seeking a professional and reliable contractor to undertake a renovation project on a residential building focusing on the top three floors, with an optional scope for the basement. Below, I have detailed the specific work requirements for each floor to enable you to provide a comprehensive and competitive quote.\n\n*Project Scope:*\n\n- Floor 3:\n  - Move one electrical panel from wall that will be removed.\n  - No major additional electrical work .\n  - Demolition of one wall.\n  - replace skylight or fix\n  - Installation of a new bathroom in the existing kitchen space, and framing off the new bathroom\n\n- Floor 2:\n  - Conversion of the current kitchen into a master bathroom , and framing off the new bathroom.\n  - Demolition of the entryway wall.\n  - No major additional electrical work.\n\n- Floor 1:\n  - Demolition of one wall.\n  - Relocation of the current secondary door back to create a mudroom.\n  - Removal of the existing stairs to basement, cover and extend the existing kitchen.\n\n- Basement (Optional):\n  - Clean up and modify the entryway.\n  - Removal of one wall.\n  - Addition of a galley kitchen.\n  - Framing off the electrical boxes.\n  - Installation of a separate ELCB for the electrical system.\n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/283-4-street-jersey_city/3',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-26 23:29:40','2024-04-26 23:29:40'),(1061,1111,1111,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13474951312',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi, I would like to install a door and a metal staircase with a small deck going from the 1st floor of my house down into the backyard.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-29 16:40:01','2024-04-29 16:40:01'),(1062,1112,1112,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19178419025',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client would like to expand attic and make into a room, half the attic is finished the other half is not; would like to replace staircase .\nAdd a bathroom to the first floor and convert sunroom into an actual living area.\nRedo the basement and make it into a living space',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-29 17:13:50','2024-04-29 17:13:50'),(1063,1113,1113,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19179214180',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Customer needs kitchen remodel, needs new backslash and counter tops , needs the stove moved , gas line needs to be changed. Client wants to change closet into a washer dryer room, plumbing needs to be added to the closet',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-04-29 19:43:45','2024-04-29 19:43:45'),(1064,1114,1114,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12037634679',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Buildzoom lead, Anna spoke on the phone \n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/221-east-76-street-new_york/4c\n\nSCOPE OF WORK\nKITCHEN:\n1. REMOVE ALL EXISTING LOWER KITCHEN CABINETS AND INSTALL UPPER AND LOWER CABINETS.\n2. REMOVE KITCHEN SINK AND ASSOCIATED PIPING AND REPLACE WITH NEW\n3. REMOVE EXISTING DISHWASHER AND REPLACE WITH NEW.\n4. REMOVE EXISTING GAS STOVE AND REPLACE WITH NEW.\n5. ADD ELECTRICAL OUTLET FOR GAS STOVE.\n6. INSTALL NEW HOOD INCLUDING NEW WIRING.\n7. RESURFACE THE KITCHEN FLOOR\n\nBATHROOM\n1. REMOVE ALL EXISTING WALL AND FLOOR TILES AND REPLACE WITH NEW 12X24\n2. REMOVE SINK, CABINET, AND REPLACE WITH NEW.\n4. REMOVE EXISTING MEDICINE CABINET AND LIGHTING. REPLACE WITH NEW.\n5. REPLACE COLD WATER RISER ISOLATION VAVLE.\n6. NEW VANITY\n7. REFINISH THE BATHTUB WITH GLAZING',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-02 12:33:46','2024-05-02 12:33:46'),(1065,1115,1115,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14805288208',NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://streeteasy.com/building/40w55-condominium/4d\n\nI\'m working on a project in midtown - 1000sqft 1 bed to 2 bed conversion. I was wondering if you would like to bid out on the construction part of the project. Few notes below:\n\nScope for construction:\n\n-Demo (based on plan)\n-Kitchen: (millwork, appliances install/integration(priced and purchased separately), moving plumbing ,electrical panel millwork built out\n-Washer/Dryer millwork (washer dryer water supply/dry hookup)\n-electrical panel upgrade\n-Fireplace wall buildout \n-Raising fireplace opening\n-Second bedroom addition + soundproofing for walls\n-office murphy bed millwork\n-office shelving\n-Guest bathroom reno based on design (to remember: toilet/storage buildout change to wall mounted toilet with tank, moving tub plumbing)\n-master bedroom closet millwork \n-master bedroom headboard wall brick install\n-master bathroom reno based on design ( to remember: moving entry door, moving shower over a dry area - currently a closet - moving shower controls to opposite wall as per design, adding additional sink for a double vanity)\n-dropped ceiling throughout to add recessed lights and coves + potentially a pendant above dining table \n-existing floor to be refinished (only if required, preferred to stay as is)and fixed OR number for new flooring throughout \n-all construction materials to be included \nmaterials/fixtures that will be calculated once samples are approved: \n-kitchen counter, bathroom tiles, fireplace wall plaster, master bedroom brick \n\nPlease find the attached design, plans and millwork drawings for your use.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-02 12:43:38','2024-05-02 12:43:38'),(1066,1116,1116,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16466781641',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remove and replace wall tiles and (possibly) large wall mirror  in  guest bathroom to update \n\nGet rid of closet doors and update',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-03 17:00:58','2024-05-03 17:00:58'),(1067,1117,1117,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15164451214',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Install recessed lights - Referral by Freya Motafram. Daniil approved the smaller scope of work',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-03 17:57:35','2024-05-03 17:57:35'),(1068,1118,1118,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18124578886',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remodeling of Kitchen, Flooring, painting, bathrooms. \n\nKitchen:\nWe have the appliances in the kitchen and they have to be moved and the cabinets need to be painted different color.  Moving the location of the appliances and stove and need to move the gas and other things similar to that.\n\nThe laundry room needs to be moved from ground floor to the upstairs area.\n\nFlooring:\nThe wood floor needs to be stripped stained with a different wood color vs changing the floor to different tiles.\n\nBathroom:\nThe powder room needs to be redone.\n\nMain bedroom bathroom needs to be redone.\n\nBedroom:\nMaking door between two bedroom to connect them together.\n\nPainting:\nWhole house needs repainting.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-06 17:32:19','2024-05-06 17:32:19'),(1069,1119,1119,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14153108630',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Co-op two small bathroom, bigger bathroom\nGuest bathroom needs to be replaced\nThe toilet for tank toilet, move slightly replace the tub with a smaller one, replace all fixtures.\nWet area only needs electrical line possibly as per other contractor\n\nMaster bathroom replace shower for a new shower ,replace the shower head and lower.\nReplace the toilet with a tank toilet. Wet area get tiles with bright colors\n\nWants a very modern design',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-07 14:18:26','2024-05-07 14:18:26'),(1070,1120,1120,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16469631295',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Community center in the Bronx , that needs to be up and running by July 1st , the state will funding the project.\nThere is a weight room that the floors need to be replaced with the padded gym floors . Remove current AC wall unit and add a split AC unit. Radiator needs to be repainted,\nWe need to add recessed lightning , need to replace and add new outlets \n\nBasketball court repainted add new hardwood flooring, needs to be repainted and new recessed lightning added outlets and replace old outlets',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-07 15:07:23','2024-05-07 15:07:23'),(1071,1121,1121,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14153108630',NULL,NULL,NULL,'co-op. two small bathrooms\nhttps://www.zillow.com/homedetails/63-61-99th-St-E7-Rego-Park-NY-11374/2068578307_zpid/?\n\nbigger bathroom - guest bathroom\nreplace the toilet for a tank toilet, move slightly \nreplace the tub with the smaller one\nreplace all fixtures \nWall tile wet area only \nneed electrical line possibly? - as per the other contract \n\nmaster bathroom \nreplace the shower for a new shower \nmove the shower head to lower \nreplace the toilet with a tank \nWall tile wet area only \n\nbright colors, modern design \n\nspoke to two other contractors',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-07 15:28:39','2024-05-07 15:28:39'),(1072,1122,1122,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17999999999',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Test',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-07 21:54:38','2024-05-07 21:54:38'),(1073,1123,1123,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15512857002',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Complete bathroom remodeling. Small bathroom with toilet, shower, and sink in a condominium. Would like to replace the sink’s plumbing as well.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-08 21:42:57','2024-05-08 21:42:57'),(1074,1124,1124,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13473490961',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I have a dining room and I need a wall built to separate the dining room preferably with sheet rock material my dining room is about 13 feet across in about 10 to 11 feet tall if possible, you can give me a call. I’m available anytime my number is 347-349-0961.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-11 00:28:07','2024-05-11 00:28:07'),(1075,1125,1125,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19175726194',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Combine 2 side-by-side manhattan condos. See as-built',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-11 15:31:00','2024-05-11 15:31:00'),(1076,1126,1126,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19173011095',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client is