ion, by the book, with appropriate permits.  I have contacted the DOB to help me navigate thru this process, and an advocate pointed me to a website that provided licensed general contractors to pick from.  I would appreciate an estimate.  \n\nMy number is 917-696-2121',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-30 14:15:11','2024-05-30 14:15:11'),(1082,1132,1132,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19178054051',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I\'m looking for to do a standup shower I removed and demo the bathroom now I need to do membrane sealant do a new shower\n\nPlus exterior work on the stairs',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-31 13:25:23','2024-05-31 13:25:23'),(1083,1133,1133,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16467712470',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi my name is Richard Velez i\'m writing to inquire if you can help with an amendment to a classification of a church/ place of worship. around the 1930s the first floor was a laundromat and the 2nd and 3rd floor were apartments. The church purchased the building and turned it all into a place of worship. Fast forward to today the church no longer holds services there only meetings on the 3rd floor occasionally. the 1st floor was rented out to a deli where a notice to change classification was given to us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-05-31 14:01:04','2024-05-31 14:01:04'),(1084,1134,1134,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13474008739',NULL,NULL,NULL,'New kitchen. Remove kitchen entrance way walls and a small wall that divides the appliance and opposite cabinet run with the eat-in area. \nRefinish all wood floors throughout the apartment and new floor moldings.  \nAdditional electric sockets in all rooms, add additional breaker to the panel.\nPainting of all rooms.\nRemove all molding around the door (and possibly windows)\nAll new windows.\nConvert tub to shower, tile and install new toilet (washlet) and sink (no vanity) either wall mounted or pedestal.\nRemover foyer closet double doors to make walk-in closet (no door replacement, will have curtain).\nBedroom and hallway linen closet that connects to make a walk-in closet from the hallway, close off door in the bedroom. \nWishlist:\nSoundproof bedroom ceiling? (A girl can dream can’t she lol).',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-02 18:21:15','2024-06-02 18:21:15'),(1085,1135,1135,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13473275748',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client wants  to change floor plan in basement by adding   a bathroom with walk in shower , add toilet, sink. Vanity and mirror , tiles 100% wet area and 50% through out new floor tiles electrical work and plumbing. \n\nClient is not sure if he wants to add kitchen to basement, with a microwave hood\n\nWe need all new walls flooring ceiling lights and electrical outlets  and walls , client would like engineered wood floor through out apt\n\nIn the upstairs kitchen client would like to switch out floors , install new fridge and gas stove and added dishwasher\nRefinish cabinets ; under lighting added. Add new sink and backsplash and change counter tops to be the same queartz',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-03 14:45:02','2024-06-03 14:45:02'),(1086,1136,1136,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16466915500',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kitchen remodel \n\nreuse appliances\nreplace everything else \n\ndesign: looking for a more modern feel',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-03 23:22:57','2024-06-03 23:22:57'),(1087,1137,1137,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12122542315',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kitchen remodel 6x8 \n\nReplace the cabinets\nReplace quartz countertops (selected cambria  hayden/mountag)\nReplace appliances (subzero, wolf), cooktop and oven \nReplace floors with porcelain tiles (possibly replace with parquet)\nRepaint the walls \nreplace doors \nGas now, may keep gas or switch to electric, need to see the panel\n\n\n52 year old kitchen - most likely all internal plumbing replacement too \nlooking to do the project in 1.5 years (fall 2025)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-04 15:43:37','2024-06-04 15:43:37'),(1088,1138,1138,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15102067815',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Entire house remodel: \n\npainting, new floors, repair the windows, replace the doors, remove wallpaper \n\nremodel the kitchen - replace cabinets, replace appliances, no work on the floors\nnew door in the bathroom\n\nplaster walls \nadd a new wall to add an additional room \n\nWill send a floor plan shortly',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-04 16:34:55','2024-06-04 16:34:55'),(1089,1139,1139,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12128660532',NULL,NULL,NULL,'full bathroom remodel \n\nreplace the tub \nshower curtain \nWall tile wet area +50%\nreplace floor tile\nreplace all fixtures \nbase mounted fixtures \nceiling and wall light fixtures, replace \nsmall window, no work for now, possibly replace the sill \nrefinish door and trim \n\nDesign preferences: none for now\n\nhttps://www.zillow.com/homedetails/30-33-32nd-St-2E-Astoria-NY-11102/2077566601_zpid/?mmlb=g,6',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-04 19:35:16','2024-06-04 19:35:16'),(1090,1140,1140,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16097325012',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2 BATHROOMS RENOVATED GUTTED \nNew shower hardware \nNew tiles slabs 100% \nKeep toilet \nFlooring porcelain large format \nVanity single new\nVessel type of sink \nNo heated flooring \nUnderlightining cabinet \nAdd recessed lightining , currently have light fixture \nNo lightining fixture above medicine cabinet\n\nSecond MASTER BATHROOM\nreplacing stone with porcelains tile large format\nRedo ceiling coated and repainted; add recessed lighting \nAdd make up mirror with led lightining \nWindow above the tub 1/2 inch slab around the tub,\nKeep current vanity\nChange sink \nPlumbing new fixture no hand held fixtures\nReglaze tub\nFlooring add new tiles\n\nPivot door between bedroom and bathroom door needs to be replaced/ or try to fix the pin above the door  \nLiving room radiator cover needs to be replaced /refinish just the top',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-05 17:41:19','2024-06-05 17:41:19'),(1091,1141,1141,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13476080523',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wants to add a kitchen to where there used to be a kitchen ;install new appliances ;microwave hood ; gas stove new cabinets keep existing flooring no dishwasher',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-05 19:30:48','2024-06-05 19:30:48'),(1092,1142,1142,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12122542315',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client wants to redo entire kitchen, wants to replace stove with wolf stove; remove dishwasher does not want new dishwasher , new sink added new tiles . Does not want to add a hood but wants a built in microwave above the stove . Wants to add a arch way on the entrance to the dinning room entrance\nKeep current light fixture\nAdd quarts counter top; keep current cabinets however would like the doors replaced and the rest of the cabinet refinshed',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-07 22:36:28','2024-06-07 22:36:28'),(1093,1143,1143,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13475540580',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi,?I need to remodeling my my bathroom completely, wall need to be down I have mildew in the bathroom, I would like to have a walking shower , it is a small bathroom. I will send you a pictures.\n\nI would like to have a consultation',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-09 20:35:07','2024-06-09 20:35:07'),(1094,1144,1144,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13477892616',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Maintenance and restoration for 3b3 1/2b duplex Apt. in downtown Manhattan. Major works are: 1. Remove rolling shades and drapery channels in 3 bedrooms only. 2. Patch & paint for the entire unit 3 bedrooms 3 1/2 Bathrooms with Staircase 3. Wood floor refinish for the entire unit (entire unit size - total 2,265 ft^2; Wood floor area - round up to 1,800 ft^2) 4. Stone refinish in kitchen, 3 1/2bathrooms and pantry.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-10 12:21:10','2024-06-10 12:21:10'),(1095,1145,1145,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15164566355',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Thanks for your email and telephone message. \nSee photos attached: my Jackson Heights galley kitchen with eating area, about 110 square feet total.\n\nUPGRADES:\n-- FLOORS: Remove vinyl tile. Replace with square 8\" ceramic tile.\n-- CABINETS: Keep current cabinets, replace fronts with wooden Shaker-style doors.\n-- NEW CABINET: Add one lower cabinet for recycling.\n-- NEW STORAGE: \n         1) Add upper shelf unit for new fridge (which is taller than current fridge, so removing upper cabinet)\n         2) Add upper shelf unit above new recycling cabinet.\n-- COUNTERTOPS: Remove formica counters. Install soapstone counters & undermount stainless steel sink.\n-- BACKSPLASH: Add backsplash of white 4\" square subway tiles.\n--  FAN/LIGHT: Replace fan/light with modern white fan/light.\n\nCOSTS: Your estimate?\nTIMING:  How long this job would take? \nSCHEDULING: Earliest start date?\nLICENSES: Do you have proper licenses and insurance, required by co-op management company?\n\nHope to hear from you soon.\nThanks very much,\nDidi Goldenhar',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-11 20:48:57','2024-06-11 20:48:57'),(1096,1146,1146,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1458461341',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are looking to renovate our 1,400 sq condo in upper midtown. It’s a duplex with a double L- staircase in the middle of the unit (unfortunately), obscuring the view. We would like to replace this stairs (modern floating-type or helical staircase, budget permitting).  We would like to renovated the kitchen and the 2.5 bathrooms. New flooring is also a must. \n\nThank you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-12 04:51:32','2024-06-12 04:51:32'),(1097,1147,1147,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16464985032',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client wants to install new cabinets, sink counter tops and switch out flooring . Keep existing appliances.  Change backsplash to match the new quartz counter top lay out is staying the same',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-12 16:51:20','2024-06-12 16:51:20'),(1098,1148,1148,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15745270973',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Throughout the entire apartment we need to take out old flooring , level it and replace with laminated wood floors ; as well as replacing all base boards.\nIt’s 500 sq ft studio.\n\nFor the bathroom which currently has a bath tub we will be replacing with a walk in shower with glass doors adding a rain shower head and replacing fixtures .\nWe will have 100% tiles in the wet area and 50% throughout the bathroom, we will be replacing floor tile with some kind of water proof wood looking vynil floors. Currently there is an over the vanity light fixture which should be replaced , currently there is a medicine cabinet which should be replaced with a new medicine cabinet . The sink and vanity should be replaced with a standing single stand alone vanity. The toilet will stay the same .\n\n\nWe need to add a new circuit breaker and change all electrical work through out apartment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-12 17:23:54','2024-06-12 17:23:54'),(1099,1149,1149,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16466234143',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello! I am looking to cut a large pass-through/breakfast bar window between my kitchen and living room. I am also looking to install a new shallow countertop in that window, as well as replace my existing kitchen countertop to match. I would like to repaint the walls of the kitchen and possibly replace existing backsplash with a new backsplash. Was looking for an estimate for this. Thanks!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-12 18:30:30','2024-06-12 18:30:30'),(1100,1150,1150,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13179418422',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kitchen\nChange cabinets through out the entire kitchen\nWith Gold handles and gold fixtures \nChange counter top , to a quartz counter top\nChange all appliances, client not sure if she wants a hood range or a microwave hood range.\nWants floor to be a wood laminate that is water proof \n\nBathroom \nCurrently has a walk in shower wants to keep the current walk I. Shower wants to keep it as a walk in shower but wants to redo all tiles on the floor of the walk in shower marble on 100% of the walls of the entire bathroom glass doors for the walk in shower, replace fixtures with all gold fixtures . \n\nReplace floors with marble .\nReplace standing toilet with a GOLD standing toilet \nReplace vanity and sink with a stand alone vanity with hold fixtures , replace medicine cabinet with a gold trimmed medicine cabinet, replace light fixtures above medicine cabinet with gold light fixtures',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-12 19:08:34','2024-06-12 19:08:34'),(1101,1151,1151,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19085656366',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client has a small bathroom , that she would like to change tiles all around the bathtub are 100%; and 50% through out the rest of the bathroom., there currently is a bath tub that she wants to keep and reglaze, client is keeping toilet . Wants to replace medicine cabinet; the vanity and sink with a stand alone vanity\nAdd recessed lightning  to the bathroom especially above bathtub',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-17 18:35:20','2024-06-17 18:35:20'),(1102,1152,1152,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11646894371',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Convert the half bathroom to a full bathroom by \n1. including the closet in the bedroom;\n2. install a shower.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-17 21:10:52','2024-06-17 21:10:52'),(1103,1153,1153,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15164051176',NULL,NULL,NULL,'1300 sq feet home . Looking to add second floor. On the second floor wants to add master bedroom with a master bathroom including walk in shower and tub, wants to also add a walk in shower ; we will need to add plumbing and electricity to the second floor.\n\n\nThere currently is a Deck space wants to convert into a family room/ sunroom with sliding doors, we need to add lightning and new flooring to that space \n\nConvert current pantry into a powder room, plumbing needs to be added to this room as well\n`',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-20 11:47:08','2024-06-20 11:47:08'),(1104,1154,1154,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15164566355',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client has galley kitchen , in which she would like to replace the vinyl tiles with ceramic tiles on the floor . \nWants to add a narrow cabinet where there currently is a space to add garbage can.\nAdd subway tiles backsplash \nAdd new Quartz counter tops\nAccording to another contractor electrical work needs to be replaced as well as plumbing \nReplace current ceiling fan with another ceiling fan',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-21 15:42:39','2024-06-21 15:42:39'),(1105,1155,1155,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14086447306',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client had a previous contractor who did not finish the work would like to get the bathroom redone , would like to see how much it would cost to add in walk in shower , tiles 100% of the wet areas and 50% through out \nNew toilet , vanity flooring medicine cabinet and recessed lighting \n\nThe kitchen needs new backslash , flooring , counter tops and vanity',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-21 16:54:38','2024-06-21 16:54:38'),(1106,1156,1156,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19178338142',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client wants to makeover the master bathroom, without changing the layout \nWants all fixtures changed including the towel racks \nFor the sink there are currently two separate sinks and vanity , client wants to combine it to one big sink with one stand alone vanity, however with two faucets and change out the medicine cabinet\n\nChange all tiles inside the shower 100% going up and change the tiles inside the shower .\nCurrently there is a walk in shower and we will be keeping it as a walk in shower changing the doors \n\nChanging tiles through out the whole bathroom , tiles 100% on walls through out the bathroom \n\nCurrently there is a wall mounted toilet which client wants to change to a stand alone toilet',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-21 21:31:10','2024-06-21 21:31:10'),(1107,1157,1157,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13123919944',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client is closing in a couple of weeks \n\nBathroom 1 \nCurrently has a bathtub switching it out to walk in shower with full glass doors .\nWe will be adding tiles 100% through out the bathroom \nChanging floor tiles \nAdding new vanity and sink, change medicine cabinets with LED lights \nAdd new toilet \n\n Bathroom 2. \nIt’s currently a walk in shower , keeping it as a walk in shower but replacing all 100 % through out the bathroom \nReplacing