ULL,NULL,'2024-06-24 15:07:31','2024-06-24 15:07:31'),(1111,1161,1161,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13474493033',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We have approval for the loan 2.5 million so I am looking forward for a contractor who can give me an estimate for around 2.3 -2.5 million.\nReady to pull the permits and start construction right away. \n\nI have approved plan from DOB for making new construction on my existing mixed use property located at 150-28 Hillside Ave Jamaica NY 11432.\n\nNow hillside Ave has 7A zone so I got approval from DOB to construct after demolition of the existing building to make 10 unit plus store and office\n\nI am sending you all the approved plans from DOB. Attached are the :\n1. Approved Fence Construction plan\n2. Approved Foundation Plan\n3. Approved street tree plan.\n4. Approved Structural Plan \n5. Approved General Construction plan',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-24 18:11:43','2024-06-24 18:11:43'),(1112,1162,1162,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16464094399',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Referral from Laura Deaner\'s friend. \n\ncoop in the purchasing stage, closing is end of July. \n\nbathroom remodel 5.6 by 7 ft \ntub reglaze or do a standing shower (calculate the shower, provide tub reglaze in the notes)\nAdd corner shelf in a shower \nglass door if shower only (if tub then a curtain rod)\nReplace wall tile wet area \nreplace the floor tile \nreplace all fixtures \nbase mounted fixtures \nreplace the wall light fixture\nwindow no work \nreplace the door and trim\n\nstandard, not too expensive on the renovations \nDesign: lighter color tiles, not sure about the hardware color, maybe black or silver. More modern rather than old school, simple but would like to add cute details like handles \n\nEntire unit:\nreplace the interior doors, 4 total \nrefinish the floors, or replace with laminate floor on top\npaint the walls and smooth out if needed \nchange the light fixture 2 total (has ceiling fan lights, would like to replace with standard lights) \nLiving room - built in shelving, remove',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-25 19:49:05','2024-06-25 19:49:05'),(1113,1163,1163,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15056037797',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Commercial space that needs store front replaced   Store front approximately 21 ft long\n\nThere are currently Stairs in the book stores that need to be blocked band reinforced\n\nBookshelves need to be secured onto the wall\nLights need to be installed in bookshelves \nInstall light fixtures, client already has light fixtures they just need them installed \n\nTrim carpentry \n\n\nBudget mind $35,000\n - immediately',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-25 22:47:34','2024-06-25 22:47:34'),(1114,1164,1164,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19175201537',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Budget $160,000\n\nHouse was bought in 1996 and no work has been done \nIn the Basement \nAdd new floors, new ceilings new recessed lighting \nMove laundry over \nNew walls \nSupply  boiler 75 water heater\nReplace outlets\n\nAdding a half bathroom to basement as well with toilet vanity , medicine cabinet new tiling around the bathroom \n\n1st floor\n\nRemove half bath out and extending the kitchen\nAdding new appliances, dishwasher, wants hood on top of stove \nChange cabinets , and under cabinets \nCounter tops quartz counter top\n Change backsplash \nChange floors to porcelain \nWe will be adding an island and knocking down wall\n \nFamily room redo walls and a half bathroom\nRemove window and add sliding doors to access the outside\nRedoing floors to laminate and adding the half bathroom where the family room  is.\n\n2nd floor\nRemodeling bathroom change bath Ryun to bathtub change vanity sink and medicine cabinet \nChange all the tiles  throughout the bathroom \nChange floors and replace light fixture with recessed lighting \n\nThere is a current family room on the second floor which we are combining with the master bath to create an on suite master bedroom with master bath .\nWe will be building a master bath with walk in shower , walk in shower needs to include bench for sitting and hand held shower system\nTiling 100 percent throughout bathroom \nWe will need to add new plumbing and electrical work',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-25 23:25:53','2024-06-25 23:25:53'),(1115,1165,1165,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'14144263709',NULL,NULL,NULL,'UWS 550 sq ft one bedroom \nprewar walk up 4th floor \n\n76 W 85 street 4A \n414-426-3709\n\ngalley kitchen: \nfull update including cabinets and countertop but possibly not appliances\n\nreuse appliances \nreplace cabinets \nreplace countertops \nreplace backsplash with the tile \nreplace the floors with tile \nno work on the window \nadd under cabinet lights \n\nbathroom: \nfull update including wet area and possibly tub removal for standing shower\n\nreplace for the walk in shower \nglass door \nreplace all fixtures \nadd niche for the shower \n50% wall tile \nrecessed medicine cabinet\nreplace wall light fixture\nno work on the ceiling \ninstall a dimmer lights switch\npossibly refinish the door and replace the hardware \n\nkeep the integrity of the UWS, very neutral and classic, some modern. Close \n\nInstall window banquet - millwork for the size of the window',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-06-26 16:06:06','2024-06-26 16:06:06'),(1116,1166,1166,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1976915856',NULL,NULL,NULL,'New bathroom - maybe need to shift location of bathroom a little.\nNew kitchen - appliances and stove. May try to install dishwasher.\nNeed to add spotlight for ceiling.\nPossible new floors (wood)\nCurrently it’s 3 bedroom but there is no living room so one of the wall between kitchen and bedroom need to be taken down to create a living room - open kitchen concept',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-01 18:32:11','2024-07-01 18:32:11'),(1117,1167,1167,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17605807986',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client would like to gut renovate bathroom, removing tub and converting into walk in shower with glass doors , tiles in 100% of the wet area and 50% through out \nChange vanity, sink medicine cabinet, remove toilet and add a wall hung toilet\nChange floor tiles',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-03 15:29:38','2024-07-03 15:29:38'),(1118,1168,1168,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17739682136',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I\'m interested in replacing the 5 existing kitchen cabinets on my walls and around my fridge. I also want to install a new fridge and over the range microwave. Would also potentially be interested in a new backsplash.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-04 17:58:26','2024-07-04 17:58:26'),(1119,1169,1169,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16467157314',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Total square footage of bathroom is\n49 square feet total\n\nFLOOR:\nI want to rip up floor and replace w new tile (old tile is cracking may need some enforcement?)\nFloor tile:\n\nNew FLOOR tile\nBLACK HERRINGBONE-49 sq ft\nhttps://www.tileshop.com/products/herringbone-gloss-black-porcelain-mosaic-wall-and-floor-tile-681213#specifications\n\n\n\nSHOWER:\nI will need to have the old one ripped out and the new tile out in.  The new tile will be 7ft high on 3 walls. I will be putting in a freestanding tub.  \n\nNew SHOWER WALL tiles\nSUBWAY TILE- 81 sq ft\nhttps://www.tilebar.com/seaport-arctic-2x10-polished-ceramic-tile.html\n\n\nWALLS IN REST OF BATHROOM:\nI will need to add tile on the remaining walls 4 ft up from floor.  \n\nNew HALF WALL tiles\nWHITE HEXAGON-50 sq ft\nhttps://www.tilebar.com/bianco-dolomite-premium-4-hexagon-polished-marble-mosaic-tile.html',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-06 00:08:22','2024-07-06 00:08:22'),(1120,1170,1170,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11208891332',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi , Are you the one to talk about the website? At Key Design Websites, we support businesses such as yours by helping them to get noticed by their ideal customers - with professional custom development and content creation that produces real organic results. May I send you some examples of websites we\'ve built for similar companies to help start our conversation? You can call me directly at 208-891-3324 Cheers, Tom Young CEO | Key Design Websites LLC Boise, ID 83703 or Please fill out my Contact Request Form: https://www.cognitoforms.com/InboxBlastscom/ContactRequestForm105 Thank you and I look forward to speaking to you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-09 10:47:33','2024-07-09 10:47:33'),(1121,1171,1171,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16572822869',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Drop ceiling for the living room, inclusive of installation of electrical, recess lighting, and spot lights.\n\nLiving room includes conv. bedroom (see floor plan).',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-09 19:05:30','2024-07-09 19:05:30'),(1122,1172,1172,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19739781447',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Adding a door/doorframe in a stairway and adding a bookshelf.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-11 17:16:52','2024-07-11 17:16:52'),(1123,1173,1173,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17186008745',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Would like to add a second floor addition to the house . This addition will be its own apartment with bathroom and kitchen . \nWe will need to add electrical work as well as plumbing new floors . \n\nApprox current home 1682 sq ft \n\nNo floor plans available',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-12 19:37:57','2024-07-12 19:37:57'),(1124,1174,1174,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19293061526',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Thank you for responding to my inquiry.  My project is the demolition of 2nd story 1-family home that has 2 small bedrooms and a small bath.  This project does not enlarge the main foot print of the house, its purpose is to \"square off\" the pitched roof angles to give 2nd story rooms a squared balanced look.\n\nI\'m looking for estimates for the following:\n\n1)  DEMOLITION\nProvide demolition as per architect\'s plans for 2nd story\nDemolish 2 staircases:  first floor staircase leading to second floor and first floor staircase leading to basement (at side door entrance)\n\n2)  FRAMING\nTo include necessary floor joists,\nstuds for interior walls, rafters, house wrap, etc.\nas provided in architect\'s drawings\nEstimate should include all material/labor\nInstall 2 staircases as per architect\'s plans\n\n3) ROOFING\nProvide and Install 3/4 rated asphalt roof shingles Class C (Certain\nTeed or similar), etc. as provided in architect\'s drawings\nEstimate should include all material/labor\n\n4) ELECTRICAL\nUpgrade panel in basement\nSupply and install recessed lighting throughout\n(Kitchen-6, LR- 6, Stairway-2,bedrooms-4 each, hallways - 4)\nSupply and install lighting in both staircase steps\nEstimate should include all material/labor\n\n5) WINDOWS (total 14 + patio door)\nSupply and install windows to 2nd floor\nSupply and install windows on 1st floor\nInstall patio door in kitchen\nEstimate should include all material/labor\n\nFollowing pics are what house looks like now and should look after',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-14 18:28:16','2024-07-14 18:28:16'),(1125,1175,1175,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13057725326',NULL,NULL,NULL,'build a med spa clinic, commercial space  2300 sq ft, 16 ft ceilings in some areas. \n\nshell condition, has the floor plans and renderings, need construction work.  The space will have a reception, and rooms for procedures like IV, infra red sauna, spa, etc. \n\nlease allows up to 8 months for construction, but want it to have it done sooner. $200K budget',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-15 20:35:25','2024-07-15 20:35:25'),(1126,1176,1176,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16466757825',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Renovation Plan Summary:\n\nKitchen:\n- Remove a wall to create space for an island\n- Replace cabinets and backsplash\n- Keep existing appliances\n- Install new floors and countertops\n\nApartment:\n- Refinish all floors\n- Redo baseboards\nReplace all doors through out the apt\n\nEntrance:\n- Add recessed lighting',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-17 16:39:23','2024-07-17 16:39:23'),(1127,1177,1177,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19176001092',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Test Matvei',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-18 18:16:12','2024-07-18 18:16:12'),(1128,1178,1178,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15187636243',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kitchen remodel \n\nreplace appliances \nreplace cabinets \nreplace the floors, no preference \n\nClient is in the purchasing stage. Will send the floor plans and additional details for the estimate - DO NOT QUALIFY until the details are received',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-18 20:24:23','2024-07-18 20:24:23'),(1129,1179,1179,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'18622857096',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Drop ceilings for a restaurant and also looking to have a dome shape ceilings. Have drawings for suspended ceiling details',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-19 20:07:42','2024-07-19 20:07:42'),(1130,1180,1180,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19174191567',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I want to close an open DOB permit from 2003. Permit details are at https://a810-bisweb.nyc.gov/bisweb/JobsQueryByNumberServlet?requestid=3&passjobnumber=103349841&passdocnumber=01 \n\nI\'d appreciate a quote on this.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-20 15:32:16','2024-07-20 15:32:16'),(1131,1181,1181,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16466443159',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are partially remodeling the bathroom \nKeeping the tub and curtain rod \nReplacing toilet with floor mounted toilet \n\nReplacing tiles in wet area 100%\nAnd 50% through out the bathroom\nReplacing floor tiles and medicine cabinet \nKeeping exsisting vanity and sink \nAdding recessed lighting',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-22 15:50:29','2024-07-22 15:50:29'),(1132,1182,1182,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19177966581',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Redoing kitchen new cabinets and appliances\nAdding electric stove and oven \n\nNew counter tops and new backsplash add me floor tiles and under cabinet lighting \n\nRedo bathroom change tub to walk in shower tiles 100% of the the shower , change sink and cabinets remove over the medicine cabinet lighting \nNew toilet \nAnd new medicine cabinet',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-22 16:31:07','2024-07-22 16:31:07'),(1133,1183,1183,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16178698995',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Interior painting in all rooms, new hardwood flooring in living room and bedroom, and replace bathroom sink, medicine cabinet and lighting.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-22 18:05:04','2024-07-22 18:05:04'),(1134,1184,1184,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13058776378',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello,\nI would like to upgrade my bathroom, bedroom and leaving room.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-23 00:14:42','2024-07-23 00:14:42'),(1135,1185,1185,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16318851369',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Needs bathroom gut renovated, replace tub with walk in shower and shower doors new wall mounted vanity and sink.\nStanding toilet.\nNew medicine cabinets with LED lights \nTiles 100% of the walls and new floor tiles \nUpdate electrical work recessed lighting',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-23 18:45:11','2024-07-23 18:45:11'),(1136,1186,1186,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11111111111',NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are looking to have some work done in our co-op. MUST HAVE COI AND HOME IMPROVEMENT LICENSE. \n\nFor bedroom/bathroom work is it the second bedroom/ bathroom, not the master. Scope of work- \nRemove wallpaper from entrance foyer walls \nRemove wallpaper from adjacent wall to foyer \nPlaster repair living room walls \nPlaster repair living room ceiling ceiling \nPlaster repair dining room wall \nPlaster repair anywhere needed \nSkim coat foyer walls \nSkimcoat adjacent wall to foyer \nSkimcoat bedroom hallway \nSkill coat repair anywhere needed \nPaint entrance foyer walls \nPaint entrance foyer ceilings \nPrimer coat living room walls \nPaint living room walls \nPaint living room ceiling \nPaint living room furnace \nPaint dining room \nPrimer coat bedroom walls \nPaint bedroom hallway walls \nPaint bedroom hallway ceilings \nPaint bedroom walls \nPaint bedroom ceiling \nPaint bedroom closet doors \nPaint bedroom furnace \nPaint bathroom ceiling \nNot included- All Oak to remain the same, base boards, doors \nIncluded- Two coats of paint All paint (Benjamin Moore Regal) \nAll plaster and compound \nAll skim coat material \nAll protection (cloth and plastic) \nAll tools \nMinor clean up \nReplacing 3 light fixtures \n\nBathroom scope of work: \n1. Remove shower floor tiles and contents down to the leaky lead pan. Leave threshold, glass doors and wall tiles alone. \nApply waterproofing to the lead pan to stop all leaks. \nPrepare a new mud job (sand and cement) and pitch towards the drain. Install new 2” x 2” shower floor tiles on a mesh. \n2. Remove old grout and caulk for 3 walls up to the designer wall tile above, the inside threshold, and old caulk by the glass shower doors. Apply new clear caulk on the shower glass doors and bone color grout and caulk for the three walls and new shower floor tiles. \n\nFloor plan of the co-op https://kennedyhouseowners.com/wp-content/gallery/floorplans/C-Line-FloorPlan.jpg\n\nHere is a google video of the scope of the work\nhttps://photos.app.goo.gl/v5hyFknhVTtzZ4337',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-24 15:29:04','2024-07-24 15:29:04'),(1137,1187,1187,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17033463709',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-07-31 09:42:08','2024-07-31 09:42:08'),(1138,1188,1188,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11281509932',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Do you need quantity take-off!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-06 21:06:32','2024-08-06 21:06:32'),(1139,1189,1189,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12017026951',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Replace shower piping for the valve (with rough in) and shower system I bought. So don’t include these materials shown on pictures for the estimate please.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-07 22:13:31','2024-08-07 22:13:31'),(1140,1190,1190,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12404372006',NULL,NULL,NULL,'My scope of work is: \n- Full gut rehab \n- New mechanicals, electrical, and plumbing\n- New HVAC\n- New Kitchen \n- New Bathrooms \n- Increase Bathroom count to 5 Bathrooms \n- Add roof deck\n\nCurrently the property has 6 bedrooms and 2 baths and I would like for it to have 5 bedrooms and 5 bathrooms. It has 3.6k square feet and is 3 stories tall. The lot size is 1514 sqft.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-09 12:19:36','2024-08-09 12:19:36'),(1141,1191,1191,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19172326407',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Floors need to be refinished if possible and would need the wall knocked down that divides the office from the living room',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-09 12:33:42','2024-08-09 12:33:42'),(1142,1192,1192,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13152827730',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client needs electrical rewiring done , bathtub reglaze , door way repaired . Full kitchen remodel new appliances keeping the same layout . New cabinets ,  new back splash as well as counter tops.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-12 13:19:06','2024-08-12 13:19:06'),(1143,1193,1193,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12126861707',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client wants to redo very small bathroom , she wants to find a way to make it more spaces. We will be replacing toilet, wall and floor tiles vanity and sink. Keeping bathtub',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-12 16:59:49','2024-08-12 16:59:49'),(1144,1194,1194,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12013128757',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi! My name is Mary and I recently purchased a one bedroom co-op in Manhattan. There is also a dining alcove that I am hoping to temporarily close off from the kitchen to make an office. The space that currently exists between the kitchen and dining alcove is 55”x92” and my handyman said that he would be able to cover the space using Sheetrock. My building told me that in order to do this I need to file this as an alteration type II which requires drawings from an architect. Can you please let me know if this is something you would be able to do and how much it would be? Thank you!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-12 19:47:12','2024-08-12 19:47:12'),(1145,1195,1195,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16177592448',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Full bathroom reno \n5x8 with high ceilings \nreplace the tub with a shower \nreplace the toilet with a toilet with no indents (modern), base \nreplace wall tile 100%\ninstall shower niche \nAdd handheld shower feature\nreplace floor tile \nhas 2 recessed medicine cabinets separated by the outlet, replace with a new medicine cabinet \nreplace a vanity with a 36 inch, base\nlooking to add more storage \ninstall grab bar in the shower \nReplace recessed toilet paper holder \nReplace recessed hamper\nReplace the door and trim. Flat panel \nmove the light switch to inside the bathroom (it is in the hallway now)\nAdd drop ceiling (to reduce height, may want to add ceiling light later)\nno window \nreplace the vent if possible \n\nDesign:\nmatte black shower fixtures and accessories, square shower head \nLarge format tiles on walls and floor \nLight color tiles\nOpen to darker vanity\nMore modern design overall',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-16 21:45:09','2024-08-16 21:45:09'),(1146,1197,1197,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12122490976',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Replace a Bathtub with walk-in shower.\ninstal safety bars (client has ones). \nPermanent bench if passible ( need see in person).\nTiles replacement partially.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-22 20:31:11','2024-08-22 20:31:11'),(1147,1198,1198,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19178864409',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bathroom remodel:  replace vanity, toilet, light fixture, tile floor, paint walls and install shower door on bathtub.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-26 13:34:34','2024-08-26 13:34:34'),(1148,1199,1199,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19175864346',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Trying to do a conversion of a two family into a three family in Brooklyn , client needs assistance in all the major steps , needs to legalize the basement',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-26 18:30:07','2024-08-26 18:30:07'),(1149,1200,1200,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19173318938',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client had recent water damage in the bathroom which created mold and had to be removed . Client will need new plywood installed and new tiles on all the walls , needs the sink and vanity replaced as well as the light above the medicine cabinet replaced .\nClient would like to replace bathtub .',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-26 19:07:08','2024-08-26 19:07:08'),(1150,1201,1201,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19175872720',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Turn demolished basement into a live in apartment , with a full kitchen , dishwasher and all new appliances and cabinets . Bathroom with walk in shower . Recessed lighting through out the new apt . New flooring engineered wood .  \nNew outlets, and light dimmers',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-28 19:46:50','2024-08-28 19:46:50'),(1151,1202,1202,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'16789258153',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Referral from previous client in the area Jessica \n\nClient is in the process of purchase, contract not signed yet. \n1 bed coop in Gramercy 900 sq ft\n\nkitchen \nfull remodel, size 10 by 7\nreplace tile floor. calculate two options one with tile, one with LVP\nreplace cabinets, countertop, appliances \nTile backsplash \nremove the door frame to make a galley layout like on a design inspiration \n\nBathroom \nfull remodel \nreglaze the tub (get a s second estimate for a replacement of the tub)\nreplace all other fixtures\ntile wet area +50%\nbase mounted fixtures\nRefer to design inspiration, simple light colors, classic design\n\nEntire unit: \n-Refinish all walls and ceilings (may be water damage on the walls under the AC in the bedroom)\n-Replace parquet floors with LVP. May be asbestos under, unsure, in this case may lay the floors over - parquet is squeaky, slight gaps in certain places, water damage on the floors under the ACs. \n-refinish the doors \n-replace foyer doors with the sliding doors \n-make a walk in closet larger by combining it with a second small closet',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-08-28 21:03:01','2024-08-28 21:03:01'),(1152,1203,1203,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17813212537',NULL,NULL,NULL,'None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-01 17:59:17','2024-09-01 17:59:17'),(1153,1204,1204,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12122214500',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client has two bathrooms that he would like to add recessed lighting to , replace sink and vanity on both, as well as the medicine cabinets \n\nWants to change the shower doors on both bathrooms \n\nNo work being done to marble would like to polish the marble on the floor and walls',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-03 18:29:59','2024-09-03 18:29:59'),(1154,1205,1205,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'19088922401',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bathroom closet opening to be expanded\nHot water tank to be removed\nTankless hot water heater to be installed (already purchased)\nAdjustable water flow regulator to be installed\nStackable washer and dryer units to be installed (already purchased)\nNew plumbing and electrical lines to be installed',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-03 20:19:22','2024-09-03 20:19:22'),(1155,1206,1206,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'17068810460',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client would like to 1) install a new HVAC system (split systems but with some ducting) in a 1300 sqft apartment. 2) do drywall work related to the hvac and small walls , 3) change the wiring of some lighting and upgrade exsisting recessed lights , 4 ) remove existing radiators stubs and window acs, 5 ) remove a lead paint baseboard (small section). We’re flexible with project scheduling .',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-05 16:03:49','2024-09-05 16:03:49'),(1156,1207,1207,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'12122039481',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bathroom: full remodel, tub removal, shower only. Updated vanity, toilet, etc.\nKitchen: full remodel. New appliances, new counter tops, back splashes, adding storage\n\nCloset: expand closet space so there’s enough space for 2 people, built in dressers, basically anything to maximize the space',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-11 02:18:26','2024-09-11 02:18:26'),(1157,1208,1208,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15513639398',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Good morning,\n\nMy name’s April and I’d like to convert the space that I have to a daycare. Per licensing rep, the half bath needs 2 child-size toilets in order to accomodate the maximum allowed capacity. Attached pictures for your reference. First is the current bath. If this is something you can help with, I’d like to discuss it with you over the phone. Thank you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-17 14:43:41','2024-09-17 14:43:41');
