nerally require coordination/approval from the board, and do you handle that directly with them?\n\nWhat would the post-closing timeline be for the above work? We are expecting a late-January close, and would want to delay our move until the above work is completed.\n\nCould we also get a rough estimate of what it would cost to renovate the kitchen and bathroom (with prices reflecting both mid and high end finishes), at a future date? The bathroom would most likely retain the same layout. The kitchen would involve a bit more, and we would want your input and discussion, but some initial ideas:\n		• replacing everything - cabinets, tiles, counters, floors, sink, appliances\n		• open it up, add an island, or just a pass through\n		• take some space from the closet to the left of the front door, perhaps moving the fridge to that side\n		• new appliances, including fridge with ice machine\n\nI’m also attaching a layout to the unit above ours (same line), to demonstrate the above kitchen configuration. One of them also shows the heating/AC custom cover we’re thinking of, structurally.',NULL,'2022-10-26 14:43:25','2022-10-26 14:43:25',NULL,'Preferred kitchen layout attached below'),(794,456,127,1,'0','0','8','See attached scope of work, architectural drawings and design visualization\n\nhttps://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1pH7mEIBjKHJe2uyKVEqc_kdiOl791buAh_4UKbVQY8k/edit#slide=id.g14646bb1b5c_0_39\n\nHas an architect, looking for GC services only\n\nRenovate kitchen \nTake down the wall \nKeep Water and gas in place \n\nBathroom \nNo plumbing conversion \nKeep the tub, réglaze it \n\nBedroom \nBuild out a closet 2 feet \n\nPartition wall - move entrance from the living room to the hallway, \n\nLarge closet open up and turn into a mini bedroom - just opening the wall \n\nRadiator heater covers - \nWall unit ac \nInstall Millwork over',NULL,'2022-10-26 15:16:34','2022-10-26 15:16:34',NULL,NULL),(795,457,122,1,'7','5','8','Water damage now\n\nInterior designer has already