, countertop, backsplash, \n\nreuse the appliances \n\nreplace the laminate floor (maybe wood underneath and would like to keep), or replace with waterproof wood or tile \n\n2 windows and 1 doorway - no work\n\nreplace the light fixture \n\ninstall under the cabinet lights \n\nremove the soffit and crawl space from the ceiling to extend the height \n\nRemove part of the wall, expand the second doorway into the dining room \n\nremove the peninsula, and install a new one facing the other side towards the dining room from the stove (mid wall)\n\nReconfigure the layout of the appliances, refer to the sketch. Install stove where the fridge is, sink where the stove is, make an arch over the stove side\n\nremove the pantry, install base and wall cabinets with backsplash on that wall \n\n flexible on the cabinet style, just needs neutral colors, white quartz with grey veins looks good, gold hardware, refer to attached photos',NULL,'2023-04-07 19:26:47','2023-04-07 19:26:47',NULL,NULL),(1030,621,122,1,'8','5','8','Hi! \nI am looking to have my bathroom remodeled. I will have the vanity and toilet on site. Also, the coop requires specific insurance. \n\nIt’s a smallish job but there are some nuances - mainly I only have on bathroom so this needs to get done in 2-3 days and there are tiles stuck to the wall with foam adhesive which might complicate the job.',NULL,'2023-04-11 03:24:22','2023-04-11 03:24:22',NULL,'Remove wall tiles, repair and paint wall, replace vanity and toilet. Remove shower door.\nAll design decisions are done'),(1031,622,122,1,'8','5','8','Hi! \nI am looking to have my bathroom remodeled. I will have the vanity and toilet on site. Also, the coop requires specific insurance. \n\nIt’s a smallish job but there are some nuances - mainly I only have on bathroom so this needs to get done in 2-3 days and there are tiles stuck to the wall with foam adhesive which might complicate the job.',NULL,'2023-04-11 03:24:24','2023-04-11 03:24:24',NULL,'Remove wall tiles, repair and paint wall, replace vanity and toilet. Remove shower door.\nAll design decisions are done'),(1032,623,121,1,'8','8','7','Full kitchen remodel - install new cabinets and new countertops; possible replacement of appliances; repaint walls and ceiling; possibly taking down one of the walls.',NULL,'2023-04-11 04:14:52','2023-04-11 04:14:52',NULL,'Simple, modern, classic, clean lines, practical'),(1033,624,123,1,'0','0','8','Refinish walls and ceilings \n\nreplace or refinish the floors, replace baseboards \n\nReplace millwork with an LCD glass wall with the door \n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/167-perry-street-new_york/6m',NULL,'2023-04-11 17:01:36','2023-04-11 17:01:36',NULL,NULL),(1034,624,121,1,'0','0','8','Full kitchen remodel \n\nRemove the wall to make the kitchen open',NULL,'2023-04-11 17:01:36','2023-04-11 17:01:36',NULL,NULL),(1035,625,123,1,'0','0','8','We are working on a home remodel project in Manhattan, which needs a general contractor, and please find the project details below.\n\n1. Brief project description:\n\nLocation - 368 3rd Ave, New York, NY 10016\nSubject - home remodel\nAnticipated project commencement - June 2023\n\n2. The existing photos are HERE https://photos.google.com/share/AF1QipMp1oAmK2tKSUh6qr-53gHSXf53_T-VeVRc5_eca23GMKa8tRL1E-R-BEG8Yi_GGw?pli=1&key=N1JfX2RZSUNBQXBVT0xjekFwOWstcnNkT3E3aHp3\n and the existing floor plan is HERE: https://www.dropbox.com/s/lhk194dwjvb9rdo/Existing%20floorplan.pdf?dl=0\n\n3. The approved design concept is HERE: https://www.dropbox.com/sh/kks09tifp41a1l7/AADWX85jlL_Ucp0eaYdQ0YCMa?dl=0  \n- these are true-to-life images developed by us and approved with the client that we need to make a reality now.\n\n4. The architectural drawings are HERE: https://www.dropbox.com/sh/h4nvvk5ckkghj8n/AAA457_8pWyDSPfzAdsqdLwka?dl=0\n\n A detailed set of renovation blueprints is being developed, but the architectural drawings should give you a good idea.\n\n5. All the interior finishing and furnishing will be supplied by us.\n\n6. Scope of work: minor demo, repurposing one of the bathrooms into a WIC / relocation of the door / new flooring, three concealed doors in the entryway, quartz and glass panels in the entryway, some electrical work, partially new lighting, including recessed LED channels, drywall work in the living room (bio fireplace / TV wall), firebox installation, decorative wall moldings in the master bedroom and wall panels in the living room, powder room renovation (floor tiles, wallpaper, wall mirror, vanity, sink, faucet, etc. - images 16-19 of the approved concept), other two bathrooms remain as is for now (!), new kitchen cabinets (Ikea) and stone, minor plaster, wall paint throughout, final cleaning, minor decor and some furniture staging (furniture, rugs, pillows).\n\nExtra work: two more bathrooms (images 67-72 and 84-90) will be remodeled at a later time.',NULL,'2023-04-11 18:16:18','2023-04-11 18:16:18',NULL,NULL),(1036,626,123,1,'0','0','8','I am contemplating making an offer on a Manhattan co-op that is approximately 1600 square feet. The apartment is a combined one bed and studio. The project would be a gut renovation that covers a kitchen, 2 baths, adding laundry, running electrical and cat5 network cable, moving and putting up multiple walls and custom closets/storage. Finishes should be good but do not need to be ultra luxury (i.e. Wolfe or Viking ranges are unnecessary and extremely fancy marble, etc. not needed), some customization may be required. Modern and sleek look is expected, lighter colors, clean lines, modern style.  I currently have a mock up of a floor plan I\'d would desire if it is achievable and I also have a copy of the existing floor plan. Scheduling time to evaluate in person at an open house is doable. I need confirmation that the desired layout is possible and what budget to expect.',NULL,'2023-04-22 01:19:51','2023-04-22 01:19:51',NULL,NULL),(1037,627,123,1,'0','0','8','I am contemplating making an offer on a Manhattan co-op that is approximately 1600 square feet. The apartment is a combined one bed and studio. The project would be a gut renovation that covers a kitchen, 2 baths, adding laundry, running electrical and cat5 network cable, moving and putting up multiple walls and custom closets/storage. Finishes should be good but do not need to be ultra luxury (i.e. Wolfe or Viking ranges are unnecessary and extremely fancy marble, etc. not needed), some customization may be required. Modern and sleek look is expected, lighter colors, clean lines, modern style.  I currently have a mock up of a floor plan I\'d would desire if it is achievable and I also have a copy of the existing floor plan. Scheduling time to evaluate in person at an open house is doable. I need confirmation that the desired layout is possible and what budget to expect.',NULL,'2023-04-22 01:19:53','2023-04-22 01:19:53',NULL,NULL),(1038,628,127,1,'14','14','8','Have a detached garage for my house that is falling apart.  Was wondering if it would be possible to make it a little higher and change the pitched roof to a flat one so that my family can enjoy a meal outdoors every now and then.  I see others in the neighborhood who have it done but I\'m not sure what\'s involved.',NULL,'2023-04-22 05:00:03','2023-04-22 05:00:03',NULL,'Ideally I would like the ceiling to be higher so that we can use it as an exercise room.  Then change the roof to a flat one with stairs (external) leading up to the roof so that we can enjoy a meal outdoors.\n\nI real dream would be to put a room on top of the garage but I\'m not sure that\'s even possible even though I see many people in my neighborhood have one.'),(1039,629,121,1,'9','8','8.5','Fix water leak damage on right side of kitchen and any other damage that may be found\nnew cabinets, floor, appliances, painting, install crown molding\nbring electric up to code (bldg built in 1942)',NULL,'2023-04-22 14:10:03','2023-04-22 14:10:03',NULL,'Modern classic\nWhite shaker cabinets, black knurled pulls and handles\nCrown molding\nWhite quartz countertop and backsplash\nVinyl plank flooring throughout, kitchen only, light color wood look that can be match red oak flooring in rest of apartment. Possibly use herringbone flooring\nNew black appliances\nNew undermount sink\nUndercabinet lighting\nrecessed lighting in kitchen and eat in are of kitchen'),(1040,631,122,1,'8','4.8','8.7','Replace wall and tile, refurnish standing shower, remove tub and update to a larger vanity (single sink on the left side)',NULL,'2023-04-24 00:53:10','2023-04-24 00:53:10',NULL,NULL),(1041,631,121,1,'9','8','8.7','Cabinet repaint color\nRemodel kitchen island: change the two tier island to a flat island surface \nChange the counter top \nChange Hardwares \nLighting',NULL,'2023-04-24 00:53:10','2023-04-24 00:53:10',NULL,NULL),(1042,631,123,1,'19','17.6','8','Replace flooring and paint wall',NULL,'2023-04-24 00:53:10','2023-04-24 00:53:10',NULL,NULL),(1043,631,124,1,'15','11.3','8.7','Replace floor, paint wall',NULL,'2023-04-24 00:53:10','2023-04-24 00:53:10',NULL,NULL),(1044,631,125,1,'11.4','12.3','8.7','replace floor, paint wall',NULL,'2023-04-24 00:53:10','2023-04-24 00:53:10',NULL,NULL),(1045,631,128,1,'12','5','8.7','replace flooring, paint wall',NULL,'2023-04-24 00:53:10','2023-04-24 00:53:10',NULL,NULL),(1046,632,122,1,'8','4.8','8.7','Replace wall and tile, refurnish standing shower, remove tub and update to a larger vanity (single sink on the left side)',NULL,'2023-04-24 00:53:12','2023-04-24 00:53:12',NULL,NULL),(1047,632,121,1,'9','8','8.7','Cabinet repaint color\nRemodel kitchen island: change the two tier island to a flat island surface \nChange the counter top \nChange Hardwares \nLighting',NULL,'2023-04-24 00:53:12','2023-04-24 00:53:12',NULL,NULL),(1048,632,123,1,'19','17.6','8','Replace flooring and paint wall',NULL,'2023-04-24 00:53:12','2023-04-24 00:53:12',NULL,NULL),(1049,632,124,1,'15','11.3','8.7','Replace floor, paint wall',NULL,'2023-04-24 00:53:12','20