droom as needed',NULL,'2023-05-01 14:57:09','2023-05-01 14:57:09',NULL,'no particular reference. just like the limewash in attached picture, but would probably prefer a more vibrant color. open to also painting master bedroom walls in limewash.'),(1057,637,121,1,'0','0','8','Extension of kitchen area',NULL,'2023-05-03 10:48:03','2023-05-03 10:48:03',NULL,NULL),(1058,637,123,1,'0','0','8','Extension of living area',NULL,'2023-05-03 10:48:03','2023-05-03 10:48:03',NULL,NULL),(1059,639,123,1,'0','0','8','Matvei has the scope of work',NULL,'2023-05-04 23:18:56','2023-05-04 23:18:56',NULL,NULL),(1060,640,122,1,'7','5','8','I\'m looking for an estimate for labor and construction materials. All finished materials will be provided. I understand you may want to see the job but we are not having site visits at this time. Please provide a rough estimate of where you think you could be and then we can schedule a site visit if you are within our range.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions.\n\nBuilding requirements \n\nMust submit co op renovation request with a copy of the contractors proposal\nContractor must submit copy of their license and very of liability insurance, all plumbing/electrical work must be done by licensed professional and copies of their licenses and liability insurance also must be submitted \nThey require very specific wording on cert of liability- naming Talbot apartments inc. And vision enterprises management LLC they will not accept any additional verbiage as in subject to terms, conditions exclusions in the description of operations section. \nClient must submit $1000 bond which will be refunded upon final inspection- any structural changes will require a letter from licensed architect or professional engineer.\nCo-op owner must also include a copy of their homeowner insurance policy \nWork hours are Monday-Friday 9-4:30pm\nContractor to submit: general liability insurance, workers comp, indemnification/hold harmless\nSee paperwork attached.',NULL,'2023-05-05 13:47:07','2023-05-05 13:47:07',NULL,NULL),(1061,641,122,1,'5','5','8','Full gut',NULL,'2023-05-09 15:08:48','2023-05-09 15:08:48',NULL,'clean and basic'),(1062,642,121,1,'0','0','8','gut renovation',NULL,'2023-05-09 15:17:25','2023-05-09 15:17:25',NULL,NULL),(1063,642,122,1,'7','5','8','gut renovation',NULL,'2023-05-09 15:17:25','2023-05-09 15:17:25',NULL,NULL),(1064,642,123,1,'0','0','8','painting, floors, drywall',NULL,'2023-05-09 15:17:25','2023-05-09 15:17:25',NULL,NULL),(1065,642,124,1,'0','0','8','painting, floors, drywall',NULL,'2023-05-09 15:17:25','2023-05-09 15:17:25',NULL,NULL),(1066,642,125,1,'0','0','8','painting, floors, drywall',NULL,'2023-05-09 15:17:25','2023-05-09 15:17:25',NULL,NULL),(1067,643,122,1,'7','5','8','Plan A: New floor and wall tile, new fixtures, new under-sink cabinet, and the removal of my current bathtub, installing a smaller tub, and creating some shelving with that extra space. \nPlan B: New floor and wall tile, new fixtures, new under sink cabinet, and the refinishing of my current bathtub\n\nI\'d like estimates for both plans.',NULL,'2023-05-10 21:58:11','2023-05-10 21:58:11',NULL,'Contemporary, Scandinavian. Subway tile, maybe a dark floor. One or two funky pops of color (maybe the vanity and/or the fixtures)'),(1068,645,122,1,'8','6','7.5','Provide material & build a brand new 3-piece bathroom in a full-size stand-up attic.  The Interior should be tiled from the ground up to the ceiling.  The front of the bath stall should be a sliding glass door.  Sliding door to the bathroom.  Exhaust fan to the roof.  Install ceiling lights and vanity lights.  Remove debris.',NULL,'2023-05-12 20:28:32','2023-05-12 20:28:32',NULL,NULL),(1069,645,127,1,'0','0','8','Provide materials and install one full-size stair from the second floor to the attic.  The ceiling high is 8 feet.  The clearance for stair installation is the same as the standard stair.  Patch up sheetrock and touch up the paint where required.  Remove all debris.',NUL