L,'2023-05-16 15:35:18','2023-05-16 15:35:18',NULL,NULL),(1077,654,123,1,'0','0','8','Entire unit: \n\nSomfy motorized shades throughout the apartment (hard wired)\n\nRemove ceiling molding throughout the apartment\n\nPaint entire apartment\n\nReplace folding closet doors throughout the apartment and replace with real doors/sliders, as needed\n\nPTACs – Replace PTAC covers with streamlined cabinets (with storage on each side, space permitting)\n\nWood floors – Please quote prices to refinish vs. replace the existing wood floors (see samples for type/color).\n\nEntryway between living room and dining room – Please quote price to expand entryway between the rooms (appears to be short barriers on each side of the wall and ceiling that can be removed).',NULL,'2023-05-16 15:35:18','2023-05-16 15:35:18',NULL,NULL),(1078,656,127,1,'0','0','8','I am looking to have a one bedroom, one bathroom wheelchair accessible addition to the rear of my home in Queens, NY. Need plans, permits etc.',NULL,'2023-05-16 18:12:12','2023-05-16 18:12:12',NULL,NULL),(1079,657,121,1,'0','0','8','58 sqft of total kitchen space (floor plans attached with measurements).\n- entire kitchen to be removed : includes all cabinets, countertops, appliances, flooring and drywall\n- wall separating kitchen and living room to be removed \n- new electrical panel to be installed and new wiring for the kitchen\nwires to be run to separate all major appliances in the kitchen \n- cabinet lighting\n- gas line to be relocated for new stove location\n- new drywall to be installed and finished smooth for painting\n- new tile floor to be installed and grouted\n- new quartz countertops to be installed with water peninsula end\n- quartz backsplash to be installed\n- new cabinets to be installed (already purchased)',NULL,'2023-05-16 20:28:50','2023-05-16 20:28:50',NULL,NULL),(1080,658,121,1,'0','0','8','58 sqft of total kitchen space (floor plans attached with measurements).\n- entire kitchen to be removed : includes all cabinets, countertops, appliances, flooring and drywall\n- wall separating kitchen and living room to be removed \n- new electrical panel to be installed and new wiring for the kitchen\nwires to be run to separate all major appliances in the kitchen \n- cabinet lighting\n- gas line to be relocated for new stove location\n- new drywall to be installed and finished smooth for painting\n- new tile floor to be installed and grouted\n- new quartz countertops to be installed with water peninsula end\n- quartz backsplash to be installed\n- new cabinets to be installed (already purchased)',NULL,'2023-05-16 20:28:51','2023-05-16 20:28:51',NULL,NULL),(1081,659,122,1,'7','5','8','Attached is the plans. I have also attached a picture of the current space for reference. The floor tiles in the patio picture are on sand which I am in the process of removing. So it will be bare cement slab to work with.\n\nI would not worry too much about the bathroom finishing touches at this point (vanity, shower, tiles, etc). We can do the finishing touches seperately.  Just give me a quote for building out the room per the plans. For reference, I did include a pic of an existing bathroom we have as it would be similar.',NULL,'2023-05-17 18:33:47','2023-05-17 18:33:47',NULL,NULL),(1082,660,122,1,'7','5','8','Attached is the plans. I have also attached a picture of the current space for reference. The floor tiles in the patio picture are on sand which I am in the process of removing. So it will be bare cement slab to work with.\n\nI would not worry too much about the bathroom finishing touches at this point (vanity, shower, tiles, etc). We can do the finishing touches seperately.  Just give me a quote for building out the room per the plans. For reference, I did include a pic of an existing bathroom we have as it would be similar.',NULL,'2023-05-17 18:33:49','2023-05-17 18:33:49',NULL,NULL),(1083,662,122,1,'7','5','8','See drawings attached',NULL,'2023-05-18 14:50:26','2023-05-18 14:50:26',NULL,NULL),(1084,663,121,1,'0','0','8','To whom it may concern,\n\n\nI am writing to request a proposal for an open concept kitchen renovation, as per the attached DOB-approved architect\'s drawings. \n\n\nWe would like to avoid having to construct any additional soffits or external channels for electric wiring. If you have to install any of these, I would like to know how many, as well as their size and location.\n\n\nAlso, we are on a budget and must keep expenses as low as possible.\n\n\nWhat we have already done and/or do not want included in the proposal:\n\n\nThe architect\'s drawings have already been approved by the DOB \n\n\nOur expeditor has already obtained DOB approval for construction, electric and plumbing permits. Expeditor will assist the contractor and plumber in obtaining permits. \n\n\nWe already have a flooring contractor who will patch the floor so we do not want to include this in the proposal.\n\n\nCan you please provide a proposal for everything shown in the architect\'s drawings EXCEPT the following:\n\nWe will not open up the hall closet near the bathroom for new doors.\n\nWe do not want the installation of the ice-maker and insta-hot to be part of the proposal.\n\n\nWe WOULD like to include the rest of the plans in architect\'s drawings, described below:\n\n\nRemove butt wall at the entrance to the living room area. There is a light switch on this wall. Switch should be relocated onto the adjacent wall, 24” left of the column.\n\n                  \n\nRemove the entrance closet completely.         \n\n\nRemove the kitchen front wall and door frame completely. There is a light switch on this wall. Light switch should be relocated to the light switch wall plate immediately to the right of the apartment entrance.\n\n\nRemove the doorway and wall at the hallway entrance to bedrooms. Rebuild affected walls and ceiling areas. \n\n\nRemove hallway linen closet and bedroom closet front and back walls. Dig floor and ceiling for electrical connection boxes. Skim and refinish ceiling areas.\n\n\nPlease note that there is a soffit along the ceiling and this front linen/bedroom closet wall, as well as the portion of wall above the bedroom door, forms the back of the soffit. The soffit is 9 in x 10 in x 12 ft. Therefore, the back of the soffit will need to be rebuilt.\n\n\nThere is an outlet and corresponding light switch on the bedroom closet front wall. Outlet and corresponding switch should be relocated to the column that is currently in the bedroom closet. (On the side of the column that is facing the kitchen window.) Column should be built out to hide wiring.\n\n\nThere is another outlet on the bedroom closet back wall. Outlet should be relocated to the same column (that is currently in the bedroom closet) on the side of the column that is facing the kitchen window. A corresponding light switch should be installed.\n\n\nRemove the dividing wall between bedroom and kitchen. Please note that there is another soffit along the ceiling (on the bedroom side) and the wall to be demolished forms the back of the soffit. The soffit is 9 in x 10 in x 12 ft. Therefore, this side wall of the soffit will need to be reconstructed.\n\n\nRefinish affected walls, ceiling and soffit.\n\n\nDividing wall between bedroom and kitchen has two outlets. Outlets should be relocated to kitchen island. Dig floor and ceilings for electrical connection boxes.    \n\n\nWe would like additional outlets:\n\n\n1. Under the counter for the dishwasher and insta-hot\n\n\n2. Above the counter to the right of the sink\n\n\n3. Behind the refrigerator \n\n\nInstall new circuit breaker panel, power to come from existing riser. Wiring may not work on arc fault breakers. Circuit breaker currently has four circuits, and is located on the bedroom hallway wall parallel to the entrance of the master bedroom.\n\n\nCabinets:\n\n\nKitchen island\n\nKitchen island (standard height) 91 in long by 44 in wide. Kitchen island will have a 30-in wide slide-in gas stove, with an electric outlet beneath counter height, accessible to the stove. There will be another outlet accessible for small appliances and laptops.\n\n\nTo the right of the stove will be a 30-in cabinet with a 6-in drawer and two 12-in drawers. To the right of that will be a 14-in overhang. On the non-stove side of the island is a 42-in long by 15 inch wide overhang. To the right of that (behind the stove) is a cabinet with three shelves that is 30 in wide and 16 in deep. At the end of the island is a cabinet with three shelves that is 42 inches wide and 14 in deep.\n\n\nBase and upper cabinets\n\n140 inches of base and upper cabinets from the window wall to the refrigerator. The base cabinets would be two and a half inches lower than standard height, and the upper cabinets would be hung two and a half inches lower than standard height. The base cabinets would have a dishwasher on the right, then a sink, and then drawers. Although the first 91 inches of wall is recessed by 9 inches, all cabinets and counters would come out to the same depth, so 25 and 1/2 inches in the recessed area and 34 and 1/2 inches in the non-recessed area.',NULL,'2023-05-18 14:57:13','2023-05-18 14:57:13',NULL,NULL),(1085,664,122,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I would like to update tub to shower with glass door. Remove old vanity and mirror. Possibly change lighting and wall. New tile throughout.',NULL,'2023-05-19 15:50:35','2023-05-19 15:50:35',NULL,'Boho design.'),(1086,664,121,1,'0','0',NULL,'Extend kitchen into current pantry to add washer and dryer in the unit. Create an island, add additional electrical outlets, add garbage disposal in the sink. Remove crown moldings on the ceiling. New wood cabinets-  with granite countertops (I would love wood but depends on price and functionality) and new backslash. possibly new lighting.',NULL,'2023-05-19 15:50:35','2023-05-19 15:50:35',NULL,'Boho, classic - woods and light tones. I don’t want a white kitchen I think that style is overdone I can combine colors with white but I don’t want a fully white kitchen'),(1087,665,122,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I would like to update tub to shower with glass door. Remove old vanity and mirror. Possibly change lighting and wall. New tile throughout.',NULL,'2023-05-19 15:50:37','2023-05-19 15:50:37',NULL,'Boho design.'),(1088,665,121,1,'0','0',NULL,'Extend kitchen into current pantry to add washer and dryer in the unit. Create an island, add additional electrical outlets, add garbage disposal in the sink. Remove crown moldings on the ceiling. New wood cabinets-  with granite countertops (I would love wood but depends on price and functionality) and new backslash. possibly new lighting.',NULL,'2023-05-19 15:50:37','2023-05-19 15:50:37',NULL,'Boho, classic - woods and light tones. I don’t want a white kitchen I think that style is overdone I can combine colors with white but I don’t want a fully white kitchen'),(1089,666,125,1,'12','12','8','fdfdsfgsf',NULL,'2023-05-21 19:42:22','2023-05-21 19:42:22',NULL,'dsfsfdsfds'),(1090,667,125,1,'433','434','8','tfdsgfd',NULL,'2023-05-21 19:43:33','2023-05-21 19:43:33',NULL,'gffdgfdg'),(1091,668,125,1,'433','434','8','tfdsgfd',NULL,'2023-05-21 19:43:34','2023-05-21 19:43:34',NULL,'gffdgfdg'),(1092,669,125,1,'543','54','8','tregfegfd',NULL,'2023-05-21 20:01:42','2023-05-21 20:01:42',NULL,'gfdgfdgfd'),(1093,670,121,1,'8','7','8','Hello, I\'m looking to renovate my small apartment kitchen. I would like to change the cabinets, tiles, flooring and to redo the kitchen island.',NULL,'2023-05-22 20:07:55','2023-05-22 20:07:55',NULL,'I\'m looking for something potentially Scandinavian-inspired, with clean lines and just a little bit of color. I\'d like to maximize the counter space since my space is small and make the existing cabinets and storage more ergonomic and efficient. I\'d also like to build a bit of separation between the fridge and stove.'),(1094,671,124,1,'12.5','10','8','add layer of quietrock and green glue on wall (opposite from door) no demolition of existing wall, on top of existing drywall\nattached picture is from model unit, actual unit wall has paint only\nmove electric outlet to fit the new wall depth',NULL,'2023-05-23 05:31:33','2023-05-23 05:31:33',NULL,NULL),(1095,671,122,1,'7','5','8','add outlet for toilet',NULL,'2023-05-23 05:31:33','2023-05-23 05:31:33',NULL,NULL),(1096,673,123,1,'0','0','8','https://streeteasy.com/property/1641007-433-west-34-street-2j\n\nThis is a small (600 sq ft) one bedroom pre-war coop apartment. This requires coop approval. \n\nNew wood floors throughout\n\n3 closets need new interiors \n\n6 new doors (wood) \n\nfinish 2 radiator covering (metal) need paint off to original finish \n\nSkim coat/paint walls and ceilings \n\nNew center lighting fixture in living room ceiling\n\nupgrade the electrical panel',NULL,'2023-05-24 18:19:12','2023-05-24 18:19:12',NULL,NULL),(1097,673,122,1,'7','5','8','Tiny Bathroom - \n\nkeep tub (reglaze), \n\nnew toilet, new sink, new tiles and paint,\n\nold bathroom radiator needs paint off to original \n\nWill be a rental unit, not expensive finishes, white subway tiles or similar',NULL,'2023-05-24 18:19:12','2023-05-24 18:19:12',NULL,NULL),(1098,673,121,1,'0','0','8','Kitchen - narrow galley kitchen (very small) total upgrade\n\n floor and wall tiles, new sink, new cabinets, granite countertop, \n\nnew fridge, gas stove, dishwasher \n\nUpgrade electric panel',NULL,'2023-05-24 18:19:12','2023-05-24 18:19:12',NULL,NULL),(1099,674,127,1,'0','0','8','https://streeteasy.com/building/277-6-street-brooklyn/3fam\n\nThird Floor:\n\nPaint the entire floor, walls and ceilings, inside the closets',NULL,'2023-05-24 19:16:24','2023-05-24 19:16:24',NULL,NULL),(1100,674,127,1,'0','0','8','Second floor: \nRemove the existing kitchen, and covert into a bedroom\nBuild a walk in closet in the bedroom where the living room space is (will not need the living room at all, will be only bedrooms on this floor)',NULL,'2023-05-24 19:16:24','2023-05-24 19:16:24',NULL,NULL),(1101,674,127,1,'0','0','8','First floor (garden floor):\n\nremove all walls including the staircase wall to make one large open area. Substitute with columns if any walls are structural. Repair and match the hardwood floor to the rest of the floor after the demo \n\nUpgrade the electrical panel. Has three now, consult if all three are needed or can consolidate and upgrade differently.\n\nInstall central air AC throughout the house \n\nNeed architectural drawings and construction services \nCurrently a three family home, will convert it to a single family',NULL,'2023-05-24 19:16:24','2023-05-24 19:16:24',NULL,NULL),(1102,676,122,1,'10','8','8','New shower room, bathroom table top cabinet, toilet',NULL,'2023-05-27 19:01:32','2023-05-27 19:01:32',NULL,'don\'t have an idea now'),(1103,678,122,1,'7','5','8','I’ve attached a concept sketch of the project, photo of our existing bathroom, desired scope of work, and photo of remodeled bathroom in downstair neighbor (similar floor plan)',NULL,'2023-05-31 01:27:28','2023-05-31 01:27:28',NULL,NULL),(1104,679,127,1,'0','0','8','Bungalow type house now, wants to do a building extension, make it an L-shaped house. \n\nAdd a garage. \n\nReplace parts of the existing wall with ftc windows\n\nInterior remodel of the entire house, layout changes.\n  \nredo electrical, plumbing, and mechanical change the layout',NULL,'2023-06-05 19:56:37','2023-06-05 19:56:37',NULL,'Need both, architectural and construction services \n\nbungalow type house now, want to add an extension to turn into an L-shaped house\n\nbuild out a garage \n\nreplace parts of the existing walls with ftc windows \n\nredo electrical, plumbing, and mechanical work throughout the house \n\nLayout change in the house\n\nFull interior remodel, including bathrooms and kitchen. \n\nBudget $250K all in'),(1105,680,127,1,'0','0','8','Property address is 9670 SW 96th Court, Miami, FL\nThe property is 0.58 acres and the house itself is about 3600 square feet\n\nHere are the projects I am considering:\n\n- New fence and driveway gates that are a mix of concrete & wood (something like this style or this) all the way around the property\n- New flooring inside\n- Impact windows and doors throughout (and some with ideally a larger opening)\n- Driveway resurfacing\n- Taking down a couple of walls inside (if they\'re not load bearing)\n- Painting all of the interior and resurfacing the ceilings / skim coat\n\n\nI have attached a plan with the dimensions of the lot and the house exterior for reference',NULL,'2023-06-05 21:27:19','2023-06-05 21:27:19',NULL,'Property address is 9670 SW 96th Court, Miami, FL\nThe property is 0.58 acres and the house itself is about 3600 square feet\n\nHere are the projects I am considering:\n\n- New fence and driveway gates that are a mix of concrete & wood (something like this style or this) all the way around the property\n- New flooring inside\n- Impact windows and doors throughout (and some with ideally a larger opening)\n- Driveway resurfacing\n- Taking down a couple of walls inside (if they\'re not load bearing)\n- Painting all of the interior and resurfacing the ceilings / skim coat/popcorn removal \n\nPotentially down the road I need kitchen and bathroom remodeling as well\n\nI have attached a plan with the dimensions of the lot and the house exterior for reference'),(1106,681,121,1,'0','0','8','Full remodel \n\nReplace cabinets, prefers IKEA, white color\n\nReuse appliances \n\nReplace tile floor with wood \n\nPaint walls and ceilings \n\nUpdate the electrical',NULL,'2023-06-05 22:21:56','2023-06-05 22:21:56',NULL,NULL),(1107,681,123,1,'0','0','8','Paint walls and ceilings \n\nReplace the floors with wood \n\nreplace outlets and light switches, update electrical \n\nrefinish closets inside \n\nBalcony work - if needed anything, determine during the walkthrough \n\nNeeds the cheapest possible option',NULL,'2023-06-05 22:21:56','2023-06-05 22:21:56',NULL,NULL),(1108,682,124,1,'13','9','9.5','Hi! I am interested in having a renovation done within my 588 square foot condo apartment.\n\nI would like to have the bedroom flipped to the bottom of the living room (opposite side of the bedroom).\n\nAnd where the bedroom currently sits, I would like to put my art studio / home office which would be the new entry way to the bathroom - not through my current bedroom. \n\nWhere the new bedroom would be, I would like to have floor to ceiling sliding glass doors (with ceiling to floor heavy curtains for privacy) and I would like to have the current closet (in the current bedroom) custom designed, expanded, and have the current side closed and the new opening to be on the side of the new bedroom. \n\nI may also be interested in having a new vanity put in the bathroom and have the toilet replaced with a new one.\nKayelyn Wright 917-403-9302',NULL,'2023-06-06 17:55:55','2023-06-06 17:55:55',NULL,NULL),(1109,682,123,1,'18.9','12.6','9.5',NULL,NULL,'2023-06-06 17:55:55','2023-06-06 17:55:55',NULL,'Hi! I am interested in having a renovation done within my 588 square foot condo apartment.\n\nI would like to have the bedroom flipped to the bottom of the living room (opposite side of the bedroom).\n\nAnd where the bedroom currently sits, I would like to put my art studio / home office which would be the new entry way to the bathroom - not through my current bedroom. \n\nWhere the new bedroom would be, I would like to have floor to ceiling sliding glass doors (with ceiling to floor heavy curtains for privacy) and I would like to have the current closet (in the current bedroom) custom designed, expanded, and have the current side closed and the new opening to be on the side of the new bedroom. \n\nI may also be interested in having a new vanity put in the bathroom and have the toilet replaced with a new one.\nKayelyn Wright 917-403-9302'),(1110,683,121,1,'0','0','8','Below is the description of the project and what is needed\n\nAs part of the remodeling project, the homeowner will be installing a shelf above the stove next to the refrigerator and replacing all lower cabinets. The plumbing will remain in its current location, but additional storage space will be added by attaching it to the wall. The homeowner also plans to add a dishwasher and new tile work, including a backsplash and floor tiles. \n\nWe also have to pull permits for this project with North Bay Village. One of the requests is a plumbing license. I was curious would you happen to have a plumber\'s license?',NULL,'2023-06-07 20:47:05','2023-06-07 20:47:05',NULL,NULL),(1111,684,123,1,'0','0','8','Scope of work\n\n\nGeneral:\n\nChange baseboard throughout \n\nCheck and replace electrical where necessary \n\nPaint \n\n\n\nFoyer \n\nInstall led light strip in front closet (provided by MG) \n\nFull redo and paint of walls and ceiling \n\nRedo ceiling \n\nAdd 3-4 recessed lights \n\n\n\nLaundry room \n\nRedo ceiling, remove washer drier and clean \n\n\n\nMaster bedroom\n\n\n\nRedo bottom corner of one wall \n\nRedo left corner of outside of closet \n\nRedo part of ceiling and wall area \n\nRedo whole closet walls and ceiling \n\nDemo/Replace center of outside of main closet with two doors \n\nChange all closet doors to be hingeless \n\n\n\n\n\nMaster bedroom small closet \n\nMay need to check for mold \n\nRepaint walls \n\n\n\n\n\nLiving and dining room \n\nFix two small areas of ceiling\n\nKnock out space behind living room wall and install Sanus wall box. Run power to it \n\n\n\nMaster bath:\n\n\n\nRedo ceiling and part of one wall\n\nReplace floor with new floor \n\nReplace sink, counter and vanity with new ones (mg provided) \n\nCheck and replace all electrical \n\nAdd outlet for smart toilet \n\nReplace toilet with smart toilet \n\nadd 3 recessed ceiling lights (mg provided) \n\n\n\nSecond bedroom \n\nRedo bottom of one wall \n\nRedo window areas of two windows \n\nRedo left center side of main closet \n\nFix led lighting in second bedroom, likely just replacing transformer for closet \n\n\n\nSecond bathroom \n\nRedo ceiling and wall behind sink \n\nReattach medicine cabinet \n\nInstall two new recessed lights \n\nCheck and replace electrical',NULL,'2023-06-10 15:32:32','2023-06-10 15:32:32',NULL,NULL),(1112,689,125,1,'0','0','8','test',NULL,'2023-06-11 18:51:29','2023-06-11 18:51:29',NULL,NULL);
