t will be replaced by a LED lighted mirror hung vertically. I will still need lighting above this mirror. The bathtub would be replaced with a jetted air tub. I would need a niche for storing items in the shower, grab bars, and possibly a folding shower seat. The showerhead would be mounted on the wall as well as handheld. I want to remove this closet hamper combination and instead of filling in the wall I would replace it with a full length cabinet.  I would need some kind of exhaust fan and possibly heat. And possibly some kind of lighting in the shower alcove. I would like subway tiles on the wall and penny tiles for the floor.',5,NULL,'2023-07-06 13:25:34','2023-07-06 13:25:34',NULL,13),(769,729,729,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'3289 Poplar Lane',NULL,NULL,'2023-07-06 15:45:27','2023-07-06 15:45:27',NULL,13),(770,730,730,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Attached rowhome in Jersey City located at 257 Randolph Ave.  in need of bright, modern, and thoughtful updates that maximize usage of limited space.  The home is a narrow, prewar wood frame home with a brick foundation.  \n\n1. The first floor is an open layout with living room and dining room with kitchen in back leading to a small backyard.\n\n- This space will need lighting and a new floor. The floor is currently carpet covering the original heart pine floor/subfloor. I like the idea of using this floor as the actual floor, but I’m not sure if it’s possible or energy efficient. The floor is attached directly to the joists\n- I would also like to change the dining area into an eat-in kitchen, moving it from the dark back area into the front room. I love to cook so a larger space to do so would be appreciated. Space in need of new window.\n-A coat closet separates the living room space from the dining room space. I would like to have this become a powder room for guests.\n-The back room, currently the kitchen, has no natural light and feels closed in. I would like to brighten this space by replacing the back door which leads to the back yard with something that will brighten the space. The floor has a slope to one corner due to settlement.\n\n2. The second floor has 3 bedrooms and 1 bathroom\n-New flooring. The stairs leading up and the floor throughout was covered with carpet of the original heart pine floor/subfloor.\n-Main bathroom. The main bathroom is small (30-35sq ft) and cramped with no ventilation and in need of thoughtful updates. I would like a pocket door as the current door when opened takes up nearly half the space. Maybe borrowing space from the adjacent closet of the middle bedroom. The bathroom has a skylight in good condition covered by a drop ceiling. The drop ceiling will need to be removed and the drywall repaired.\n-Middle bedroom. In need of flooring refresh and new window. May need drywall refresh as walls and ceiling show signs of previous repair. The space has a recessed closet behind the door whose space could be used to add sq footage to the bathroom.\n-Back bedroom. Situated above the current kitchen. Floor has a slope due to settlement. Will need floor, new window, and drywall refresh.\n-Master bedroom. Currently the  room in the best condition. May need a paint refresh.\n\n3. The Backyard is small, but I love gardening and would like a space for entertaining and relaxing.\n -The backyard has an old deck that is falling apart and will need to be replaced. The yard itself is covered in mulch.\n\n4. The basement is unfinished with a concrete floor\n -The basement has the second bathroom and laundry.\n -In the future, I would like to turn this into living space. It will require digging out as the ceiling is roughly 6’4” high.',2,NULL,'2023-07-06 17:02:31','2023-07-06 17:02:31',NULL,13),(771,731,731,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,NULL,'2023-07-07 08:07:04','2023-07-07 08:07:04',NULL,13),(772,732,732,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,NULL,'2023-07-07 09:50:05','2023-07-07 09:50:05',NULL,13),(773,733,733,1,NULL,N