 on the ceilings), prep the skim coated for the “picture\nframe” moldings installation. Size, design, and calculation of the frames will\nbe discussed with the client.\n- Doors. Replace 6 (six) room doors in the apartment, install new pre-\nfinished doors. All the door jambs will remain as is, replace the door \nlocks/handles and the hinges if needed. Replace tall closet double doors in the\nliving room, if necessary, replace the frame/jamb unit for it, as well.\n- Paint entire apartment walls, ceilings, trim works, and existing doors\n(not pre-finished), new picture frames and crown moldings. No painting in the\nbedrooms, bathrooms, closets is proposed per client’s request. Patch/fix and\npaint the entire apartment walls, ceilings, trims, etc with the low VOC primer\nand paints; patch all the holes and cracks where needed.\nAll the existing hardwood floor planks and the base moldings will remain\nas is, cover/protect them during the work.\n\n\nKitchen and pantry (next few months due to lead time)\n- Full demo in the kitchen and the pantry rooms. Remove existing kitchen\ncabinets, countertops, appliances and sink, flooring in kitchen and the pantry\nareas; inspect the subfloor, repair as needed, and provided waterproofing\nmembrane (or other) before floor installation (All the buildings and Board\nrequirements). Remove the partition wall top near the doorway to the kitchen,\nopen it up to the ceiling.\n\n2.- Design the kitchen cabinetry with the same layout/locations of the\nappliances, fixtures and cabinets. Optional: see the possibility to relocate and\ncombine washer and dryer units next to the kitchen sink and make them\nstackable if possible. Or move the refrigerator to the middle of the pantry area\n- Electrical work. Bring all the electrical connection to the code. Provide\nelectrical work in the kitchen, update all the outlets and switches, and provide\nthe power lines for the under-cabinet lights if needed.\n- Prep the area for the rough plumbing, replace and update the\nsink/dishwasher water valves and drain pipes. Patch and paint all walls and\nceilings in new kitchen;\n- Install new tile or hardwood flooring, new kitchen cabinets, light\nfixtures, dishwasher, stove, fridge, hood, double oven/microwave units,\nwasher/dryer, etc;\n- Install new kitchen sink and the faucet, and finish kitchen plumbing\nafter installing stone countertop and the backsplash.',2,NULL,'2023-08-07 20:04:37','2023-08-07 20:04:37',NULL,13),(845,805,805,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1bd renovation at East River Coop 455 FDR Dr B1904\nRemove wall between living space and kitchen (requires architect). Renovate kitchen  new cabinets/countertop/peninsula. \nMake flooring consistent across living space, bedroom, kitchen, and closets. \nBathroom renovation. Replace alcove tub, flooring, walls, toilet, vanity, recessed mirror. Install washlet. \nBring electrical up to code.',NULL,NULL,'2023-08-08 18:06:28','2023-08-08 18:06:28',NULL,13),(846,806,806,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'i need you to fully furnished my house',5,NULL,'2023-08-09 04:59:20','2023-08-09 04:59:20',NULL,13),(847,807,807,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello! I own a store in Brooklyn.\nThe store is need of repairs.\nCeiling needs fixing or replacing, 800ish of flooring needs installing.\nfront of store needs repairs. Basement stairs and entire ceiling need fixing or replacing.\nA wall needs to be removed and replace with new wall.\n\nI am not opposed to design service as well. Thanks!',2,NULL,'2023-08-09 15:50:45','2023-08-09 15:50:45',NULL,13),(848,808,808,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Actually I just reviewed your business, and I thought that professional and eye catching logo would be the great additon for your business? We will design 3 eye catching logo concepts for you and will show you the logos within couple of hours today and if you like it then you may pay us only $50 if not that\'s fine.And it means that you have not to pay until you like t