eve it needs a sand/buff and refinish) as well as repaint our entire unit. We are in a one bedroom apartment',5,NULL,'2023-08-17 14:42:21','2023-08-17 14:42:21',NULL,13),(858,818,818,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are looking to maximize the living space by opening the kitchen/living room areas, add master bedroom.',5,NULL,'2023-08-17 20:14:50','2023-08-17 20:14:50',NULL,13),(859,819,819,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bathroom Remodel 1:\nRe tile floor and walls to ceiling\nRemove bath tub /Shower installation \nRemove toilet/ New toilet installation\nMillwork for 2 cabinets and heater cover\nRefinish current vanity and keep current marble countertop\nChange out fixtures and lighting\n\nBathroom Remodel 2:\nRe tile floor and walls to ceiling\nRemove pedestal sink/ New pedestal sink installation\nRemove toilet/ New toilet installation\nMillwork for 1 cabinet and heater cover\nChange out fixtures and lighting\nFix window\n\nPrimary Bedroom:\nElectrical to add second sconce and outlets for each side of bed\nMillwork for wall built in unitMillwork for heat and AC cover\nMillwork for closet doorShelving for small walk in closet\nRepainting\n\nHome Office:\nMillwork for heat and AC cover\nShelving for closet\n\nLiving Room:\nElectrical to install second sconce on other side of couch\nMillwork for heat and AC cover\n\nKitchen:\nRemodel cabinets\nNew countertop, backsplash, sink, fixtures\nNew appliances',2,NULL,'2023-08-17 22:27:02','2023-08-17 22:27:02',NULL,13),(860,820,820,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi - I am closing on a condo at The Windsor (107-24 71st Rd, Queens, NY 11375) apartment #10B. I am looking to renovate the kitchen, paint the walls, change the doors and handles, update shades, update light fixtures, replace floors, and renovate the primary bathroom. The apartment is 1,300 square feet - a 2 bedroom and 2 bathroom space. You can find pictures of its current condition here: https://photos.google.com/share/AF1QipNhEoV12uVl10c3zfA9U1Q5i9MpKz3qCcmWnir0Ftzy1gh7ZECl3DJx1GeCD-27Fg?key=aU50aGYyT21sSldkNmVrdnJMYzhjSl9MN2ZHV3pB\n\nI look forward to hearing from you. Thank you!',5,NULL,'2023-08-18 02:22:30','2023-08-18 02:22:30',NULL,13),(861,821,821,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello, I was wondering if you could help me the last week of August with four small jobs, about one day\'s work (but requiring two visits).  I\'ve attached pictures.\n\n    The insulation around my metal door frame is crumbling into dust.  I would like it removed, but it is screwed in, so the holes have to be filled in and painted over.  I have the paint color for the door frame (it will also need a metal primer).\n\n    The metal door has a scratch.  Can you touch it up without repainting the whole door?  It was last painted in 2016.  I have the paint color for the door (it will also need a metal primer).  This is low priority.\n\n    My newly refinished tub was caulked with GE Advanced Silicone 2 (white).  But after a couple of weeks, I gently wiped it, and the caulk just peeled up like paper.  Apparently it wasn\'t really sealed, and as soon as you touched it, the unsealing spread.  To avoid damaging the new paint, the caulk was removed with a plastic razor, we let it dry for 24 hours, wiped lightly with alcohol and let dry another 30 minutes, then recaulked, and I didn\'t use it for 36 hours.  But the same problem happened again.  I need recaulking, but am showering with the failed seal for now and just wiping it dry with a paper towel afterwards.  I prefer to remove the caulk, wait a couple of days to make sure it is dry, then recaulk.  This is a priority.\n\n    The granite kitchen counter needs to be caulked.  The brown grout along the backsplash washed out (reno was 15 years ago but in good condition), and a painter painted over the caulk along the side, which gets a little wet from the sink.  The paint along the edge needs to be scraped and touched up, and the area recaulked--do you recommend clear silicone, or brown or gray caulk? I have the wall paint for this.\n\nI am going on vacation Aug. 20-27, and hope to have this done Aug. 30-Sept. 1.  This is because my office is allowing remote work that week, so it\'s convenient, and also since I am showering with failed caulk, I want to fix that as soon as possible.  I know these are small jobs, but if you can help, please let me know an estimate breakdown and if you prefer I provide supplies.\n\nThanks so much,\nAnnie\n415-425-2049',2,NULL,'2023-08-18 15:36:47','2023-08-18 15:36:47',NULL,13),(862,822,822,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi! Here are my renovations in list of priority. I spoke to Daniel on the phone a little bit about them. It is a new building currently finishing up and I want to switch up the finishes and potentially add some space. \n\n1. ADD CLOSET\n- in the space between the bathroom and the W/D, create a skinny, deep linen closet \n- Add shelving \n\n2. BATHROOM \n- Demo whole bathroom interior \n- paint, new vanity, new toilet, new tiles, new everything \n- make space smaller (shave off room for linen closet) \n\n3. BEHIND THE FRONT DOOR \n- add sliding door or some door to create a closet in that tiny sliver. \n- add shelving possibly\n\n4. BEDROOM\n- Tear out current closet + make wall flat \n- on one of the longer walls create a floor to ceiling wardrobe wall \n- to shave off costs, use IKEA PAX carcass as base\n- paint and simple crown molding in whole bedroom \n\n5. KITCHEN \n- Paint cabinets beige and add paneling to cabinets like inspo',5,NULL,'2023-08-19 17:25:50','2023-08-19 17:25:50',NULL,13),(863,823,823,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'The support posts are leaning in the crawlspace and the main beam towards the front is starting to dip and twist. \n\nThe deck has some rusted teko straps Item 1(Picture) and and area shored up unprofessionally Item 2(Picture). There is also a large hole in the rear where a possible staircase might go Item 4(Picture). There is also a footing that is cracked. Item 5(Picture). Some of the decking is loose and needs to be screwed down Item 3(Picture). Recommend having all repaired by a licensed contractor.',NULL,NULL,'2023-08-19 20:29:34','2023-08-19 20:29:34',NULL,13),(864,824,824,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'We recently purchased a 2 bedroom coop in the uws.  Looking to have it renovated. Please call to discuss details. Thank you',2,NULL,'2023-08-20 16:18:41','2023-08-20 16:18:41',NULL,13),(865,825,825,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello, I would like to schedule a consultation to renovate my bathroom and kitchen.',5,NULL,'2023-08-22 18:39:37','2023-08-22 18:39:37',NULL,13),(866,826,826,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'2023-08-23 18:15:37','2023-08-23 18:15:37',NULL,13),(867,827,827,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello, my name is Paul and Id like to have my guest bathroom remodeled.  I want a minimal modern look.  Id like white subway tile with black grout and black hex tile on the floor.  Tub will be replaced with walk in shower even floor with full room.  \n\nAll other fixtures including toilet and showerhead and sink vanity will be replaced.  I will supply the replacements to be installed.  \n\nI can tell you morw details during a walk through.  I would like to have you come out to site on friday or monday.  Preferrably friday if possible.  My number is 917-533-6745.  \n\nI can provide pictures via text from that number as the upload feature here does not seem to be working.',2,NULL,'2023-08-24 04:50:44','2023-08-24 04:50:44',NULL,13),(868,828,828,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hey\nI would like to offer some suggestions for your site. No commitment for future work, fine print, or hidden anything - just an opportunity for you to see how we can improve your site and leads.\n\nWould it be ok to send you the suggestions I have in mind?\n\nPlease let me know.\nRegards,\nSteve Johnson',5,NULL,'2023-08-24 04:52:43','2023-08-24 04:52:43',NULL,13),(869,829,829,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'no',2,NULL,'2023-08-25 01:51:29','2023-08-25 01:51:29',NULL,13),(870,830,830,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello,\n\nWe live in the west village, and we have a couple items in our two bathrooms that we\'d like fixed/renovated: \n\n1. Our glass shower door recently fell off - we\'d like to completely replace this with a sliding glass door. It\'s a floor to ceiling shower(no bathtub), and the aesthetic of the house is quite bare and modern. The drainage system is also quite finicky and gets dirty/clogged very easily, so we\'d love to replace that with something more practical as well.\n\n2. Our downstairs bathroom shower/bath plumbing has always been a little strange. The temperature knob doesn\'t work and it\'s not possible to switch between the bath faucet and the showerhead. We\'d like to re-do the system so that it works, and perhaps install a door or splash guard as well. (There\'s a curtain on there right now)\n\n3. We need a closet door fixed/replaced\n\nPlease let us know if you can give us a quote, or if you need more information/pictures. Thanks so much for your time. \n\nBest,\nJae',2,NULL,'2023-08-28 22:13:24','2023-08-28 22:13:24',NULL,13),(871,831,831,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Basement full assessment: - Frame and close off the washer dryer and hvac with walls and separate doors – Install recessed lights throughout the space and new electrical outlets and light switches – Close the ceiling with sheetrock Install new vinyl floors throughout - Install heating, baseboard radiators - Paint everything 1 st Floor: - Paint everything - Cover the popcorn ceilings by laminating with sheetrock over all areas where there are pop-corn ceilings - Install Recessed lights everywhere (entry, hallway, living / dining room). (The kitchen already has lights.) – Remove all interior doors and install new, and new door handles – Remove existing and install all new closet doors - Install new backyard door – Remove the current baseboards - Install all new vinyl flooring above the existing (the current floors are straight and sturdy, no squeaks or gaps, great to serve as base.) - Install new baseboards Replace floor in the bathroom Replace radiator - Kitchen: Existing kitchen cabinets will be removed, sand and paint Install new sink and new countertops - Install new Backsplash Create some type of venting system to outside from the kitchen Run electrical line and install outlet on the island 2 nd Floor: - Cap the stairs or stain them to have the same or similar floor finish look as the new flooring from downstairs (or upstairs. Client will decide on the final floor finish). – Gut renovates the bathrooms Install a few hallway lights (recessed or regular ceiling lights) – Close off one room from the rest (with sheetrock, or shelf, TBD) Replace radiator Soundproof room and bathroom Within the room install small kitchenette instead of the closet (bathroom is at the back, to take water from and run pluming lines) – Laminate the ceilings where there is pop-corn with sheetrock, so it’s new and straight - Convert the primary bathroom from tub to standing shower - Paint everything (hallway, room, hallway between room and bathroom and bathroom) Fix and repair all closets on the second (all new closet doors) Tenant entry Replace the two doors Remove carpet and install vinyl wood on the stairs Paint the hallway Replace radiator Change lights in the hallway Other exterior repair Ground floor: replace black door Fix siding change rotten wood Sand and prime, fill and fix and paint – Fix the exterior 3 steps that are cracking- epoxy stairs crack - Power-wash the stairs - And then paint stairs with exterior hard paint backyard Install small awning above the backyard door so the rain doesn’t come in',3,NULL,'2023-08-29 17:37:53','2023-08-29 17:37:53',NULL,13),(872,832,832,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'After fire incident, restoration work is underway. Almost completed. Need to start work for new kitchen, floor, paint.',NULL,NULL,'2023-08-30 18:03:18','2023-08-30 18:03:18',NULL,13),(873,833,833,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Remove the closet, which was built on top of the floor and has electricity box in it, add two real walls to make it a real bedroom (right hand side of the living room from floor plan, Electrical box shall be embedded in the wall), however the floor is now fully covered by wooden floor.',NULL,NULL,'2023-08-31 17:38:16','2023-08-31 17:38:16',NULL,13),(874,834,834,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello,\n\nmy name is Tim Ioannidis and I\'m the owner of a small studio apartment at 240E 46th St in Manhattan (post-war, well-maintained building). \n\nI found your contact information online since I would like to plan a renovation project to replace the kitchen and bathroom (and potentially some closet space as well), ideally sometime this fall. It will require bringing down a wall to open up the kitchen area.\n\nIs that something you can potentially help me with? What\'s the usual process?\n\nThanks,\nTim Ioannidis',2,NULL,'2023-09-01 16:55:07','2023-09-01 16:55:07',NULL,13),(875,835,835,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I\'m looking to get a ball park range quote for build out of bar in LIC/Astoria area ~2500 square feet.\n\nhi it will be approx 10 room karaoke bar with an open bar area up front',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-02 13:37:45','2023-09-02 13:37:45',NULL,13),(876,836,836,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello,\n\nLooking to fully renovate our kitchen. All cabinets, countertops, backsplashes & floor.\n\nAprox. 10 ft long x 8 ft wide\n\nPlease do let us know what other information is necessary to provide with a rough estimation.\n\nThanks,',2,NULL,'2023-09-03 00:46:06','2023-09-03 00:46:06',NULL,13),(877,837,837,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am interested in creating a media unit with a built in electric fire place and bookcases built in a coop in Queens.\n\nThe space is 8 feet 8 inches wide, 1 foot deep.',5,NULL,'2023-09-05 01:54:05','2023-09-05 01:54:05',NULL,13),(878,838,838,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Design, choose furniture and suppliers, purchase and install.',2,NULL,'2023-09-06 12:11:39','2023-09-06 12:11:39',NULL,13),(879,839,839,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'We need help we the city riquirements as follow Structural\n\n1. CLARIFY SCOPE OF WORK. CLEARLY IDENTIFY ALL NEW WORK TO BE PERFORMED AND ALL EXISTING CONSTRUCTION AND OTHER PLAN ELEMENTS. PROVIDE ALL NECESSARY DRAWINGS AND OTHER INFORMATION. DRAWINGS MUST BE OF SUFFICIENT CLARITY AND QUALITY TO EFFECTIVELY CONVEY THE NATURE AND SCOPE OF THE PROPOSED WORK. \n\n2. PROVIDE DIGITALLY SIGNED/SEALED PLANS AND DOCUMENTATION OR SUBMIT MANUALLY SIGNED/SEALED/DATED (IN ORIGINAL) PLANS AND DOCUMENTATION AT THE BLDG. DEPT., FOR PROCESSING/SCANNING INTO OUR SYSTEM.\n\nElectrical\n\n1.PROVIDE LIGHT POLE MANUFACTURE SPECIFICATIONS (CUT SHEETS). FBC 107. 2.PROVIDE LIGHT POLE BRANCH CIRCUIT INFORMATION, SUCH AS CONDUIT, CONDUCTORS   AND OCPD SIZE. 3.PROVIDE GFCI RECEPTACLE @BATHROOM 3\' FROM SINK. NEC 210.52(D). 4.TAMPER RESISTAN RECEPTACLE REQUIRED. NEC 406.12. ADD NOTE ON PLAN. 5.PROVIDE/DEPICT ILLUMINATION @BATHROOM (LIGHT & SWITCH). NEC 210.70. 6.SMOKE ALARM REQUIRED INSIDE AND OUTSIDE ALL SLEEPING UNITS. FBC 907. 7.DRAWINGS TO BE SIGNED BY ELECTRICAL QUALIFIER AND NOTARIZED. FS 489.505.12. REVIEWER: SANTANA CAICEDO, PHONE# 786-315-2269. EMAIL: CAICEDO@MIAMIDADE.GOV THIS PLANS ARE INCOMPLETE. RESPONSE TO ABOVE COMMENTS MAY GENERATE ADDITIONAL  COMMENTS AT NEXT REVIEW.\n\nPROVIDE MANUFACTURER SPECIFICATIONS SHEETS. FBC 107\nPROVIDE PANEL SCHEDULE - CIRCUIT/CONDUCTORRACEWAY/OCPD/VA, SIZES. NEC 220.14,   NEC 240.4\nMISSING GFCI FOR ACCESSORY BUILDINGS, BATHROOM, GARAGE, KITCHEN, OUTSIDE,       SINKS, AND WITHIN 25\' OF AC UNITS. NEC 210.8 & NEC 210.63\nPROVIDE NOTE ON PLAN FOR TAMPER RESISTANT RECEPTACLE OUTLETS REQUIRED. NEC      406.12\nSMOKE ALARMS REQUIRED INSIDE & OUTSIDE ALL SLEEPING AREAS. FBC 907\nDRAWINGS TO BE SIGNED BY ALARM OR ELECTRICAL QUALIFIER AND NOTARIZED. FS        489.505.12\nREQUIRE NEW ELECTRICAL SHEETS. FBC 10728\nPLEASE PROVIDE A RESPONSE SHEET. FBC 107\n\nPlumbing\n\nTHIS REVIEW IS FOR: BATHROOM RENOVATION, 1-PROVIDE COMPLETE PROPOSED ARCHITECTURAL FLOOR PLAN AND SITE PLAN INDICATING THE AREA OF WORK (FBC/B107.3.5). 2-PROVIDE SANITARY AND WATER PIPE LAYOUT/CONNECTION TO THE EXISTING FOR THE BATHROOM RECONFIGURATION (FBC/B107.3.5). 3-PLEASE ADD/PROVIDE PLUMBING FIXTURES CLEARANCES PER FBCR P2705.1 4- THE PLAN MUST BE SEALED, SIGNED AND DATED BY THE DESIGN PROFESSIONAL OR HAVE THE CONTRACTOR QUALIFIERS NUMBER WITH THE PRINTED NAME OF THE QUALIFIER, THEN SIGNED BY THE QUALIFIER, DATED AND NOTARIZED. IT MUST ALSO INCLUDE THE OWNERS NAME AND JOB ADDRESS ON ALL PAGES. FOR QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS REVIEW COMMENTS, YOU CAN EMAIL ME AT CLAY.DENNIS@MIAMIDADE.GOV .\n\nZoning\n\n1. PLANS ARE INCOMPLETE AND A THOROUGH REVIEW IS NOT POSSIBLE AT THIS TIME. 2.  SCOPE OF WORK IS FOR A RAMP/BATH, A DETAILED FLOOR PLAN AND SITE PLAN WILL BE REQUIRED SHOWING SCOPE OF WORK AND LOCATION. 3. OTHER COMMENTS MAY FOLLOW. 4.EMAIL JESSE.HERNANDEZ@MIAMIDADE.GOV IF YOU HAVE ANY QUESTIONS\n\nBuilding\n\n1-CONSTRUCTION DOCUMENTS SHALL BE OF SUFFICIENT CLARITY TO INDICATE THE   LOCATION, NATURE AND EXTENT OF THE WORK PROPOSED AND SHOW IN DETAIL   THAT IT WILL CONFORM TO THE PROVISIONS OF THIS CODE - FBC 107.2.1 -  A-PROVIDE STRUCTURAL AND ARCHITECTURAL PLANS FOR LANDINGS AND RAMPS SHOWING    ALL DETAILS FOR EDGE PROTECTION, HAND RAILS ETC..  B-PROVIDE ALL DETAILS OF BATHROOM CONVERSION TO INCLUDE MATERIALS, HEIGHTS    OF INSTALLATION ETC.. 2-THE CONSTRUCTION DOCUMENTS SHALL BE PREPARED BY A REGISTERED DESIGN   PROFESSIONAL  - FBC 107.1 FURTHER REVIEW PENDING RECEIPT OF REQUESTED DOCUMENTATION. IF YOU HAVE ANY QUESTIONS REGARDING THESE REVIEW COMMENTS, PLEASE CONTACT DON HATLEY BY E-MAIL AT A666@MIAMIDADE.GOV',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-06 16:42:27','2023-09-06 16:42:27',NULL,13),(880,840,8