costs. Once the contract is signed, can do a walkthrough.',6,NULL,'2024-03-26 15:30:39','2024-03-26 15:30:39',NULL,13),(1117,1078,1078,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello, I am looking to completely renovate an existing single story ranch style house located at 1919 West 3rd Street in Brooklyn. I would like to extend the front portion of the existing structure and add a second floor with attic space. The zoning is r4a and will remain a single family home. I am still in the infancy stage of shopping around. I will need an architectural survey, architect, and GC for the entire project.\n\nI want to confirm the sprinkler system is not required. I want to bump the current porch so the front is squared off. I also want to square off the back of the house. \nAdd second floor to match the first level and have attic space. \n\nSurvey us completed, need an architect and GC',2,NULL,'2024-03-26 20:32:23','2024-03-26 20:32:23',NULL,13),(1118,1079,1079,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'house in queens 1940s built. part of the property is on city land. stayed in the family from her mother, will be building within her property lines.\nhas the survey - will email \n\ntree was removed - part of the fence came down, ground is not leveled \nInstall a cement wall instead of the fence \nInstall driveway all the way, cemented \nBuild a room 18 by 22 - for physical therapy - either an extension of the house or a separate building with three walls and one glass wall facing the the yard, separate entrance',5,NULL,'2024-03-29 13:23:58','2024-03-29 13:23:58',NULL,13),(1119,1080,1080,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Basement full remodel \n\nthe floor needs to be leveled, has linoleum now in patches. Replace with the floor tile \nceiling and walls full drywall replacement, paint \n3 ceiling light fixtures replace with recessed lights \nthere is a temp wall, want to remove it\nInstall a pantry closet under the stairs (has a small closet currently, want to enlarge)\n\nbathroom \