nd bathroom - third floor \nreplace tub for tub, lower profile \nshower curtain\nreplace fixtures \nwall mounted toilet \nhas a skylight window, replace \nWall tile wet zone only \nhas a lot of pipes - questions about the layout \ndesign: not sure if she wants the same or different design, large format tiles. Possible for blue colors',3,NULL,'2024-04-15 14:30:13','2024-04-15 14:30:13',NULL,13),(1133,1094,1094,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Redo the basement to make it a standalone rental unit; convert the top three floors into a single family. Add a deck, and extend the kitchen out',NULL,NULL,'2024-04-16 16:07:29','2024-04-16 16:07:29',NULL,13),(1134,1095,1095,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'First time home buyer - looking to make an offer for the property\n(search criteria: 1 bed coop, UWS, UES, Midtown) \n\n1960s building, needs gut reno.  750 sq ft\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/525-east-86-street-new_york/1b\n\nEntire apartment: \nPaint all walls and ceilings, door trims, window trims and sills \nreplace the doors \nreplace closet organization \nreplace flooring with engineered wood, replace baseboards\nupgrade electrical, replace outlets where needed\n\nLiving room \ninstall recessed lights \n\nHallway\nRemove the wall between the dining room and hallway\nRearrange the closets in the hallway and bedroom, see proposed floor plan \n\n\nkitchen - full renovation \nremove the wall between the kitchen and living room, make open kitchen\ninstall the peninsula \nreplace all cabinets and appliances\nreplace floors with engineered wood \nInstall pendant lights over the island or possibly recessed lights \n\n\nbathroom - full remodel \nExpand the bathroom, see proposed floor plan \nreplace tub for a shower \nwall tile floor to ceiling \ninstall double vanity \nrelocate the toilet \nreplace all fixtures \ninstall recessed lights \nfloor mounted vanity and toilet \n\nhave a good sense for the design concept - will send references \n\n\nWalkthrough to be scheduled for May 1-3, they are on vacation prior to that',3,NULL,'2024-04-17 15:35:20','2024-04-17 15:35:20',NULL,13),(1135,1096,1096,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'We are looking to upgrade our electrical equipment, and Con Ed said that the wall with the meters, which happens to be creating a boiler room, needs to be moved back 3 feet. Because of this, we will also need a grill installed in the foundation for ventilation.\nSo demo of the wall, a new wall, up to plumbing code as far as fireproof, etc. \n\nI also have a foundation issue in the cellar door, do you work on that?',1,NULL,'2024-04-17 16:01:06','2024-04-17 16:01:06',NULL,13),(1136,1097,1097,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I am looking for a contractor to perform some work at a co-op in Queens Village. It includes a wall being removed in the dining room/kitchen area- kitchen renovation as well & washer dryer install where the wall used to be. Bathroom installed into closet space on the first floor. Closet removed in a room on the second floor. Attic access being relocated from one room to the next as well as the orientation of the opening being change. Bathroom renovation. As well as a few other items. An architect has already drawn, submitted, and had these plans approved. Let me know if this is something you\'d be interested working on at your earliest convenience. EPA lead-based certification is a must from the co-op',3,NULL,'2024-04-17 21:34:57','2024-04-17 21:34:57',NULL,13),(1137,1098,1098,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Two bathroom master bath and guest bath that need to be remodeled. The master bath the tub needs to be switched out for a standing shower, the tiles need to be replaced and a radiator needs to be moved as well. \n  The guest bathroom she needs tiles replaced and and sink and fixtures replaced',NULL,NULL,'2024-04-17 22:22:43','2024-04-17 22:22:43',NULL,13),(1138,1099,1099,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'We just purchased a 450 sqft condo that was partially renovated as part of the contract. The kitchen and floors are brand new and lovely. The main things that are left to renovated are: \n1. The walls - these are in poor shape and likely need to be sanded down before they can be re-painted. \n2. Removal of certain parts of walls - we have strange corners and juts that are anywhere from 3-6 inches in length and span from floor to ceiling. We would like to remove these to make the space feel bigger. This is the bulk of what we are looking to have done. \n3. Addition of walls to create a small home office - extending an existing closet by 2-3 feet will accomplish this. \n4. Addition of walls to create a bedroom - we are planning on installing an Ikea PAX closet system and want to understand how the walls need to be configured to best accommodate the length and width of the closet.',5,NULL,'2024-04-18 15:11:03','2024-04-18 15:11:03',NULL,13),(1139,1100,1100,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Houzz lead, Anna spoke on the phone: \n\nhttps://streeteasy.com/building/405-west-48-street-new_york/1fe\n\nKitchen - full remodel\nreplace the cabinets \nreplace the appliances (dw now, install a drawer style mw, replace the hood with a vent towards the window, replace with regular gas range) wolf and subzero panel ready appliances \n\nfloors are wood, continuous throughout the unit, no work\nreplace the light (it\'s above the cabinets), open to recessed lights \ninstall under cabinet lights \nreplace the backsplash with tile\nreplace countertop \ncover the window and put the cabinets \n\ndesign: more timeless and classic than modern, lighter colors, natural wood but to not look like wood, much lighter off white wood. Could be a shaker, unsure yet, panel ready appliances\n\nStart of the project after the summer \nDays off on  wednesday and thursday - contact then for a quicker response',3,NULL,'2024-04-19 19:40:59','2024-04-19 19:40:59',NULL,13),(1140,1101,1101,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Anna spoke via email, awaiting a call to discuss the scope \n\nSee attached drawings',3,NULL,'2024-04-19 21:12:31','2024-04-19 21:12:31',NULL,13),(1141,1102,1102,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2BD Coop apartment - Renovation thoughts/requests\nnotes here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rM3Afpn84rC-7XK-ls5qL4oCTYwtw8GIxtSFfp0Fb9w/edit?usp=sharing\n\nKitchen Needs\nTop Priority\nMore counter space! Currently I have 25-26” of work space, would like to have 40 minimum\nSpace for bulk items in glass jars\nCookbook space\nSlide out pantry\nReducing hard-to-reach dead space\nEfficient storage for pots/pans\nUtensil storage not right in front of work space\nImprove lighting\nCheck possibility of re-opening kitchen vent and how to filter/fan/kitchen exhaust\nExtend opening/window between kitchen and living room\n\nWould like to discuss, but not 100% necessary\nWould like to explore induction cooking to see if possible\nSmall built-in desk/work space?\nBetter storage for wine/sparkling water\n\nBathroom needs\nTop Priority\nReplace spa tub with regular tub/shower\nAdd electrical outlet\nTile that is easy to clean and doesn’t show brown minerals in water\nKeep linen/bath closet space - add organization?\nAdd shower surround (glass doors, but modern)\nTowel space for 4\n\nWould like but not 100% necessary\nLinen closet organization\nLevel bathroom floor - right now it is very uneven\nImprovements to ½ bath in main bedroom - current tile\nBedrooms\nTop Priority\nAdd closet to girls bedroom by taking space from larger bedroom\nAdd built-in clothing storage (hanging and shelves/drawers) to both bedrooms\nReplace lighting/fan in kids bedroom with LED energy efficient\n\nWould like but not 100% necessary\nAdd ceiling pendant to main bedroom and/or bedside lighting\n\n\nThroughout\nTop Priority\nClassic modern aesthetic - in keeping with age of building - not trendy or easily dated\nFix peeling ceilings\nRefinish floors and repair damage, if possible, rather than replacing\nBetter/energy efficient lighting (keeping integrated LED fixture above dining table)\n\nWould like, but not 100% necessary\nSkim coat and paint walls\nBetter closet organization\nMore bookshelf space in living room (built-in shelves on ½ wall facing kitchen?)',NULL,NULL,'2024-04-21 16:31:23','2024-04-21 16:31:23',NULL,13),(1142,1103,1103,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hi,\n\nWe are an Architectural / Estimation company. We provide these services to different General Contractors, Sub-Contractors, Home Builders and Specialty Contractors.\n\nPlease send over the project details if you are interested and mention the exact scope of work for the quote on our services charges. You will surely find our prices and work exceptionally outstanding.\n\nYou may ask for the samples of our previous work which we did recently. Thanks.',5,NULL,'2024-04-22 14:04:16','2024-04-22 14:04:16',NULL,13),(1143,1104,1104,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client needs Arch that separates the living room and the kitchen demolished needs that space painted as well as the ceilings in both rooms kitchen and living room',2,NULL,'2024-04-22 14:10:59','2024-04-22 14:10:59',NULL,13),(1144,1105,1105,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Looking to add add an addition to an existing 1 level family home, but also includes gutting , but also includes gutting the existing floor. Plans were submitted and approved by DOB about 9 years ago, looking to get an estimate and move forward with project',NULL,NULL,'2024-04-22 19:06:14','2024-04-22 19:06:14',NULL,13),(1145,1106,1106,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Client needs tub replaced or refinished, medicine cabinet and mirror need to be replaced, new tiles on wall the toilet does not have to be replaced as she recently got it installed the hallway needs to be repainted and the living room repainted and replastered',5,NULL,'2024-04-23 19:42:52','2024-04-23 19:42:52',NULL,13),(1146,1107,1107,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I have a 600 sf studio in the Parc Vendome at 56th and